1
00:00:42,677 --> 00:00:45,212
[SOMBER INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

2
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:21,181
<i>Hi. My name is Peter Parker.</i>

3
00:01:23,216 --> 00:01:24,217
<i>You don't remember me,</i>

4
00:01:24,251 --> 00:01:26,219
<i>but I have something</i>
<i>to tell you</i>

5
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:28,255
<i>that's gonna sound crazy.</i>

6
00:01:28,288 --> 00:01:30,858
[MACHINE WHIRRING]

7
00:01:30,892 --> 00:01:31,859
<i>But it's the truth.</i>

8
00:01:34,161 --> 00:01:35,830
<i>And I know</i>
<i>you're gonna believe me,</i>

9
00:01:35,863 --> 00:01:37,497
<i>because you're very good</i>
<i>at telling...</i>

10
00:01:37,532 --> 00:01:39,166
-[BEEPING]
<i>-...when I'm lying.</i>

11
00:01:40,802 --> 00:01:42,369
E.V.,
can you check the calibration

12
00:01:42,402 --> 00:01:43,437
of my targeting matrix?

13
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:45,205
That doesn't feel
zeroed in to me.

14
00:01:45,238 --> 00:01:47,240
E.V.:
<i>Checking target calibration.</i>

15
00:01:51,646 --> 00:01:54,381
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

16
00:01:55,883 --> 00:01:57,250
Hey, E.V., take five.

17
00:01:57,852 --> 00:01:58,886
E.V.: <i>Standing by.</i>

18
00:02:04,659 --> 00:02:06,193
PETER: <i>We used to</i>
<i>know each other.</i>

19
00:02:07,494 --> 00:02:09,329
<i>We were together.</i>

20
00:02:10,531 --> 00:02:12,232
<i>But something bad</i>
<i>was gonna happen,</i>

21
00:02:12,265 --> 00:02:13,901
<i>and the only way</i>
<i>to stop it</i>

22
00:02:13,935 --> 00:02:14,836
<i>was to make everyone</i>
<i>forget me.</i>

23
00:02:14,869 --> 00:02:15,737
[PHONE CHIMES]

24
00:02:20,642 --> 00:02:22,877
<i>First day at MIT, let's go!</i>

25
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:25,245
[LAUGHING] <i>Oh, my gosh!</i>
<i>We're here! We made it!</i>

26
00:02:25,278 --> 00:02:26,914
<i>Oh, MJ, come on.</i>

27
00:02:26,948 --> 00:02:28,348
PETER: <i>Including you.</i>

28
00:02:28,382 --> 00:02:29,017
NED: <i>Pretend like you're not</i>
<i>the happiest you've ever been</i>

29
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,119
<i>in your entire life right now.</i>

30
00:02:31,919 --> 00:02:32,987
<i>-I can't.</i>
-[NED EXCLAIMS]

31
00:02:33,021 --> 00:02:34,722
<i>-Let's just do this!</i>
<i>-Okay, okay, okay.</i>

32
00:02:34,756 --> 00:02:35,857
NED: <i>You're happy!</i>
MJ: <i>Okay.</i>

33
00:02:35,890 --> 00:02:38,158
PETER: <i>Because I'm not</i>
<i>just Peter Parker.</i>

34
00:02:39,761 --> 00:02:41,261
<i>I'm Spider-Man.</i>

35
00:02:41,294 --> 00:02:41,996
NED: [OVER PHONE]
<i>I'm really, really</i>

36
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:43,131
<i>understanding the culture</i>

37
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:44,532
<i>out here in Boston</i>
<i>is just so different.</i>

38
00:02:44,565 --> 00:02:45,566
PETER: <i>And sometimes,</i>

39
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,467
<i>Spider-Man has to do</i>
<i>the hard thing,</i>

40
00:02:47,502 --> 00:02:49,537
<i>even if it breaks</i>
<i>Peter Parker's heart.</i>

41
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:52,740
NED: <i>And everyone here is like,</i>
<i>"Pahk the cah by the hahba."</i>

42
00:02:54,008 --> 00:02:55,977
PETER: <i>And maybe</i>
<i>that's my responsibility.</i>

43
00:02:56,010 --> 00:02:56,978
[NED TALKING INDISTINCTLY]

44
00:02:57,011 --> 00:02:58,680
PETER: <i>To live alone</i>
<i>with the truth.</i>

45
00:03:00,014 --> 00:03:03,618
<i>But the truth is, MJ,</i>
<i>that I love you.</i>

46
00:03:05,252 --> 00:03:06,420
<i>And I hope that deep down,</i>

47
00:03:06,453 --> 00:03:07,387
<i>something inside of you</i>

48
00:03:07,421 --> 00:03:09,256
<i>remembers that</i>
<i>you love me, too.</i>

49
00:03:09,289 --> 00:03:10,457
[PHONE BEEPS]

50
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:13,293
E.V.: <i>Suspect is 5'8", 5'10",</i>
<i>medium build.</i>

51
00:03:13,326 --> 00:03:15,963
PETER: <i>But until then,</i>
<i>I'm just gonna be Spider-Man.</i>

52
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:20,400
[SIREN WAILING]

53
00:03:20,434 --> 00:03:21,936
[EXHILARATING MUSIC PLAYING]

54
00:03:21,969 --> 00:03:23,705
-SPIDER-MAN: Incoming!
-[THUG GROANS]

55
00:03:24,404 --> 00:03:26,440
[ALL GROANING]

56
00:03:26,473 --> 00:03:28,776
-Hey, get him!
-[THUG 2 GROANS]

57
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:30,310
SPIDER-MAN: Hey, hey, hey.
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

58
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:33,313
[THUG 3 SCREAMING]

59
00:03:36,851 --> 00:03:38,886
[SIREN WAILING]

60
00:03:41,055 --> 00:03:43,256
[CHUCKLING]

61
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:45,325
ANCHOR: [ON TV] <i>Members of</i>
<i>the Manfredi crime syndicate</i>

62
00:03:45,358 --> 00:03:47,895
<i>were apprehended</i>
<i>by Spider-Man yesterday.</i>

63
00:03:47,929 --> 00:03:49,997
[ROCK SONG PLAYING]

64
00:04:03,544 --> 00:04:04,545
[GROANS]

65
00:04:09,316 --> 00:04:12,419
-[ELEVATOR DINGS]
-Hey, we live on the same floor.

66
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:15,422
Oh. Cool.

67
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:18,826
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

68
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:21,328
PETER: Does anybody
ever come up here?

69
00:04:21,361 --> 00:04:23,798
LANDLORD: Not unless
they like asbestos.

70
00:04:23,831 --> 00:04:26,601
We've just been using it
for storage.

71
00:04:27,635 --> 00:04:30,505
[EXHALES] It's perfect.

72
00:04:30,538 --> 00:04:33,508
NED: [ON PHONE] <i>Hey, everyone,</i>
<i>sophomore-year Ned is back.</i>

73
00:04:33,541 --> 00:04:36,443
<i>Older, wiser, flyer.</i>

74
00:04:36,476 --> 00:04:39,080
-[EXCLAIMS] <i>Let's go!</i>
<i>-Whoa.</i>

75
00:04:39,113 --> 00:04:41,649
<i>-What is on your face?</i>
-NED: <i>How do you feel about it?</i>

76
00:04:41,682 --> 00:04:43,818
<i>I mean, you look</i>
<i>like an assistant coach.</i>

77
00:04:43,851 --> 00:04:44,786
<i>Huh.</i>

78
00:04:44,819 --> 00:04:46,988
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
-[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

79
00:04:48,523 --> 00:04:50,591
SPIDER-MAN: You sure
you wanna do this, Scorpion?

80
00:04:50,625 --> 00:04:51,793
Did you miss me, Spidey?

81
00:04:55,596 --> 00:04:56,831
[TOMBSTONE GRUNTS]

82
00:04:57,932 --> 00:04:59,066
If I drop you from here,

83
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,636
how long you think it will
take you to hit the ground?

84
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:03,436
SPIDER-MAN: Well, I don't know.

85
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:05,472
-You tell me.
-[TOMBSTONE YELPS]

86
00:05:05,506 --> 00:05:06,674
SPIDER-MAN: Let's end this
on a high note, huh?

87
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:09,677
[SCORPION GRUNTS]

88
00:05:09,710 --> 00:05:12,445
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
-[TOMBSTONE SCREAMING]

89
00:05:12,914 --> 00:05:14,015
Yo, Lonnie!

90
00:05:14,749 --> 00:05:15,883
Wha ha happened?

91
00:05:15,917 --> 00:05:17,952
SPIDER-MAN: DeWolff, all the
evidence you're gonna need

92
00:05:17,985 --> 00:05:19,587
is in the trunk of his car.

93
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:21,756
You tryin' to take my job,
Spider-Man?

94
00:05:21,789 --> 00:05:22,857
SPIDER-MAN: Hey, you guys
are the professionals,

95
00:05:22,890 --> 00:05:24,025
I'm just a volunteer.

96
00:05:26,093 --> 00:05:28,596
[ROCK SONG CONTINUES]

97
00:05:34,602 --> 00:05:36,637
ANCHOR: [ON TV]
<i>It's a new New York.</i>

98
00:05:36,671 --> 00:05:37,772
<i>Thanks to Spider-Man,</i>

99
00:05:37,805 --> 00:05:40,373
<i>crime rates have dropped</i>
<i>to a record low.</i>

100
00:05:40,407 --> 00:05:42,743
<i>Police and Damage Control</i>
<i>give much of the credit</i>

101
00:05:42,777 --> 00:05:43,678
<i>to the masked hero.</i>

102
00:05:43,711 --> 00:05:45,746
-PETER: Initiate HUD test.
-[PHONE BEEPING]

103
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:47,515
E.V.: <i>Armed robbery</i>
<i>at Civic Union Bank.</i>

104
00:05:47,548 --> 00:05:49,550
ANCHOR: <i>In the past six months,</i>
<i>he has taken down</i>

105
00:05:49,584 --> 00:05:52,587
<i>every major crime lord</i>
<i>across the five boroughs,</i>

106
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:55,990
<i>including the superpowered</i>
<i>ninja group The Hand.</i>

107
00:05:59,894 --> 00:06:01,629
<i>He is the pride</i>
<i>of New York City.</i>

108
00:06:01,662 --> 00:06:04,098
<i>The hero every</i>
<i>grown-up relies on</i>

109
00:06:04,131 --> 00:06:06,901
<i>and every kid wants to be.</i>

110
00:06:06,934 --> 00:06:09,469
NED: [ON PHONE]
<i>Final semester, MIT.</i>

111
00:06:09,503 --> 00:06:12,039
<i>Oh, my gosh,</i>
<i>we're graduating in a month.</i>

112
00:06:12,073 --> 00:06:15,475
<i>We've made so many memories.</i>
<i>Where do I begin?</i>

113
00:06:15,509 --> 00:06:16,911
<i>Night swimming</i>
<i>in the Charles River</i>

114
00:06:16,944 --> 00:06:18,679
<i>with Jim and Wiley.</i>

115
00:06:18,713 --> 00:06:21,582
<i>The infamous food fight</i>
<i>at the Banana Lounge.</i>

116
00:06:21,616 --> 00:06:25,887
<i>Pulling all-nighters in Stud 5</i>
<i>with MJ and Nate Dawg.</i>

117
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,888
<i>It feels like yesterday</i>

118
00:06:26,921 --> 00:06:28,756
<i>I was sitting</i>
<i>on a roof with MJ,</i>

119
00:06:28,789 --> 00:06:29,824
<i>dreaming about</i>
<i>coming here together,</i>

120
00:06:29,857 --> 00:06:32,093
<i>and I still can't believe</i>
<i>we did it.</i>

121
00:06:32,126 --> 00:06:34,929
<i>I'm so grateful for all</i>
<i>the friends that I've made.</i>

122
00:06:34,962 --> 00:06:37,464
<i>I couldn't imagine going</i>
<i>through this with anyone else.</i>

123
00:06:37,497 --> 00:06:39,533
<i>Ned, who do you think</i>
<i>is actually watching these?</i>

124
00:06:39,567 --> 00:06:40,668
[STUTTERING] <i>I don't know.</i>

125
00:06:40,701 --> 00:06:42,036
<i>-But maybe someone.</i>
<i>-</i> MJ: <i>Okay.</i>

126
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:43,537
<i>Okay, well, bye, someone.</i>

127
00:06:43,571 --> 00:06:44,437
NED: <i>What?</i>
MJ: <i>Bye. We're done.</i>

128
00:06:44,471 --> 00:06:45,640
NED: <i>No!</i>
MJ: <i>Yeah, we're done.</i>

129
00:07:03,724 --> 00:07:05,793
I mean, we're talking about
downtown Brooklyn

130
00:07:05,826 --> 00:07:06,928
in broad daylight.

131
00:07:06,961 --> 00:07:08,495
High-profile job like that,

132
00:07:08,529 --> 00:07:09,931
you know that Foswell
was involved.

133
00:07:09,964 --> 00:07:12,166
Yeah, I hear you,
but can you prove it?

134
00:07:12,199 --> 00:07:14,135
Yeah, I'm going through
his financial records

135
00:07:14,168 --> 00:07:15,468
and I'm following his crew
every night.

136
00:07:15,503 --> 00:07:18,806
DEWOLFF: [CHUCKLES] <i>Do you</i>
<i>do anything besides work?</i>

137
00:07:18,839 --> 00:07:20,508
You know the saying,
"You do something you love,

138
00:07:20,541 --> 00:07:21,776
"you don't work a day
in your life."

139
00:07:21,809 --> 00:07:23,177
[CHUCKLES, SPEAKING SPANISH]

140
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:24,245
[IN ENGLISH] Mom,
where's my calculator?

141
00:07:24,278 --> 00:07:25,246
[SOFTLY] I don't know.

142
00:07:25,279 --> 00:07:26,914
<i>Trust me, aight?</i>

143
00:07:26,948 --> 00:07:29,482
<i>Being married to the job</i>
<i>never ends well.</i>

144
00:07:29,517 --> 00:07:31,552
[CHUCKLES] Well, don't worry
about it. I'll be okay.

145
00:07:31,585 --> 00:07:34,088
Oh, yeah? You still getting
them headaches, though?

146
00:07:35,623 --> 00:07:37,992
Uh, yeah.
But, um... But I'll be fine.

147
00:07:38,025 --> 00:07:39,226
DEWOLFF: <i>Mmm,</i>
<i>I don't know, man.</i>

148
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:41,262
<i>I think your body's tryin'</i>
<i>to tell you somethin'.</i>

149
00:07:41,295 --> 00:07:42,830
Like you need to
get outta that suit

150
00:07:42,863 --> 00:07:43,731
every once in a while.

151
00:07:43,764 --> 00:07:45,866
Mom, do you know
where my calculator is?

152
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,234
I don't know, <i>Papi.</i>

153
00:07:47,268 --> 00:07:50,137
<i>What you need</i>
<i>is some real human connection.</i>

154
00:07:50,171 --> 00:07:51,906
Oh, what?
And we're not connecting?

155
00:07:51,939 --> 00:07:52,940
DEWOLFF: <i>Nah, dude.</i>

156
00:07:52,974 --> 00:07:54,241
<i>I don't know your name,</i>

157
00:07:54,275 --> 00:07:56,744
<i>your face,</i>
<i>or nothing about you.</i>

158
00:07:56,777 --> 00:07:57,912
I don't think
you've ever asked me

159
00:07:57,945 --> 00:07:59,113
a question about my life.

160
00:07:59,146 --> 00:08:00,214
PETER: <i>Sure, I have.</i>

161
00:08:00,247 --> 00:08:01,382
DEWOLFF: <i>Yeah,</i>
<i>what are my kids' names?</i>

162
00:08:01,415 --> 00:08:04,251
Uh, well, for starters,
your son's name's <i>Papi.</i>

163
00:08:04,285 --> 00:08:05,987
[LAUGHING]

164
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,121
Is it Spider-Man?

165
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:09,623
I can't tell you that,
sweetheart.

166
00:08:09,657 --> 00:08:11,025
That means it's Spider-Man.

167
00:08:11,058 --> 00:08:12,193
[SIGHS] Gosh.

168
00:08:12,893 --> 00:08:14,895
[ALARM BEEPING]

169
00:08:14,929 --> 00:08:16,731
DISPATCHER: <i>A hijacked tank</i>
<i>is heading southbound</i>

170
00:08:16,764 --> 00:08:17,898
<i>past 34th Street.</i>

171
00:08:17,932 --> 00:08:19,700
<i>All available units respond.</i>

172
00:08:19,734 --> 00:08:20,835
Hey, you getting this?

173
00:08:20,868 --> 00:08:22,703
More work. Lucky you.

174
00:08:22,737 --> 00:08:23,871
Okay, I'll see you out there.

175
00:08:23,904 --> 00:08:25,039
I'm so sorry, I gotta go.

176
00:08:25,072 --> 00:08:27,141
[SIREN WAILING]

177
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:29,210
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

178
00:08:33,948 --> 00:08:35,516
SPIDER-MAN: Whoo!

179
00:08:38,252 --> 00:08:39,253
[GROANS]

180
00:08:39,987 --> 00:08:41,889
[EXCLAIMING]

181
00:08:47,161 --> 00:08:48,929
[WIND WHISTLING]

182
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,935
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

183
00:09:00,608 --> 00:09:02,810
Awoo!

184
00:09:02,843 --> 00:09:05,012
[WEB WARBLING INTENSELY]

185
00:09:08,082 --> 00:09:10,117
[EXPLOSIONS]

186
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:14,021
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

187
00:09:15,289 --> 00:09:17,124
[SIREN WAILING]

188
00:09:24,765 --> 00:09:26,300
[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:09:27,902 --> 00:09:29,103
[SPIDER-MAN EXCLAIMS]

190
00:09:31,072 --> 00:09:32,073
SPIDER-MAN: Whoa!

191
00:09:35,743 --> 00:09:37,011
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

192
00:09:37,044 --> 00:09:38,179
[METAL CLANGS]

193
00:09:40,781 --> 00:09:42,283
[MUSIC PLAYING OVER STEREO]

194
00:09:42,316 --> 00:09:43,784
I got you, Spidey!

195
00:09:43,818 --> 00:09:45,086
SPIDER-MAN: No, no.
I don't need your...

196
00:09:45,119 --> 00:09:47,154
-[ENGINE ACCELERATING]
-SPIDER-MAN: Whoa.

197
00:09:48,756 --> 00:09:49,957
[CLINKS]

198
00:09:55,162 --> 00:09:56,797
[SCREECHING]

199
00:09:59,333 --> 00:10:00,367
SPIDER-MAN: Hey! Heads up!

200
00:10:02,236 --> 00:10:04,772
You okay, kid?
Yeah, you're okay.

201
00:10:04,805 --> 00:10:06,040
See ya later. [GRUNTS]

202
00:10:06,807 --> 00:10:08,642
[SIREN WAILING]

203
00:10:10,111 --> 00:10:11,712
You wouldn't know it
just by looking at it,

204
00:10:11,745 --> 00:10:13,013
but this very street

205
00:10:13,047 --> 00:10:15,783
was completely destroyed
in the Battle of New York.

206
00:10:15,816 --> 00:10:17,284
[PEOPLE GASPING]

207
00:10:17,318 --> 00:10:19,687
-[SPIDER-MAN SHOUTS]
-[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

208
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:20,821
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

209
00:10:23,023 --> 00:10:24,792
[STRAINING] Come on,
come on, come on.

210
00:10:26,327 --> 00:10:28,229
Come on.

211
00:10:29,296 --> 00:10:32,032
[SCREAMING, GROANING]

212
00:10:38,339 --> 00:10:39,406
[SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]

213
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,142
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

214
00:10:41,175 --> 00:10:43,677
Oh, God. [GRUNTS, GROANS]

215
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,781
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

216
00:10:50,951 --> 00:10:52,286
Come on.

217
00:10:52,319 --> 00:10:54,889
-Hey. [GROANS]
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

218
00:10:54,922 --> 00:10:56,924
The hell, Frank?
You just hit me with the van!

219
00:10:56,957 --> 00:10:58,225
Quit your whimpering.

220
00:10:58,259 --> 00:10:59,927
SPIDER-MAN: We're not
doing that again, Frank.

221
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,328
You're goddamn right we're not.

222
00:11:01,362 --> 00:11:03,731
This time you're gonna
get the hell outta my way.

223
00:11:03,764 --> 00:11:04,999
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, you mean
instead of saving your life?

224
00:11:05,032 --> 00:11:08,469
Eh, you gonna talk about that
Staten Island bullshit again?

225
00:11:08,503 --> 00:11:10,237
SPIDER-MAN: Ah, well,
you said it, not me.

226
00:11:10,271 --> 00:11:11,372
Jeez.

227
00:11:11,405 --> 00:11:11,972
SPIDER-MAN: Look, man,
you can't just shoot yourself

228
00:11:12,006 --> 00:11:13,340
out of every situation.

229
00:11:13,374 --> 00:11:14,909
Innocent people get hurt.

230
00:11:14,942 --> 00:11:17,178
Who do you think's downrange
of that tank, dumb-dumb?

231
00:11:17,878 --> 00:11:18,979
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

232
00:11:20,481 --> 00:11:22,082
[LAUGHS MOCKINGLY]

233
00:11:22,783 --> 00:11:23,784
Suit yourself.

234
00:11:24,952 --> 00:11:26,687
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

235
00:11:27,321 --> 00:11:28,222
Jackass.

236
00:11:28,255 --> 00:11:30,457
SPIDER-MAN: [EXHALES]
This freakin' guy.

237
00:11:34,428 --> 00:11:35,696
[EXCLAIMS]

238
00:11:36,463 --> 00:11:38,299
[BOTH GROANING]

239
00:11:38,332 --> 00:11:40,167
[GRUNTING]

240
00:11:41,468 --> 00:11:42,469
[CLANGS]

241
00:11:44,338 --> 00:11:46,508
-Motherf...
-[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

242
00:11:46,541 --> 00:11:47,975
SPIDER-MAN: Go home, Frank!

243
00:11:48,976 --> 00:11:49,877
[SPITS]

244
00:11:50,545 --> 00:11:51,412
[GRUNTS]

245
00:11:52,446 --> 00:11:54,081
I'm gonna kill this kid.

246
00:11:54,114 --> 00:11:56,116
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:11:57,484 --> 00:11:58,886
[CELL PHONE RINGING]

248
00:11:58,919 --> 00:11:59,753
SPIDER-MAN: DeWolff?

249
00:11:59,787 --> 00:12:01,188
Are you gonna stop that thing
or what?

250
00:12:01,222 --> 00:12:02,256
<i>It's heading straight for</i>

251
00:12:02,289 --> 00:12:03,958
<i>the Damage Control</i>
<i>Detention Center.</i>

252
00:12:03,991 --> 00:12:05,025
SPIDER-MAN: I'm trying.

253
00:12:05,059 --> 00:12:06,293
DEWOLFF: <i>Try harder.</i>

254
00:12:06,327 --> 00:12:07,394
<i>There's a lot of scary dudes</i>
<i>locked up in there.</i>

255
00:12:07,428 --> 00:12:09,496
SPIDER-MAN: Well, who do you
think put them in there?

256
00:12:09,531 --> 00:12:11,932
-[PRISON DOOR BEEPS]
-GUARD: Let's go, Scorpion.

257
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:13,867
Moving day.

258
00:12:13,901 --> 00:12:15,903
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

259
00:12:20,975 --> 00:12:22,476
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS, SHOUTS]

260
00:12:27,515 --> 00:12:28,949
[GRUNTS]

261
00:12:31,018 --> 00:12:32,853
[ALL CLAMORING]

262
00:12:37,358 --> 00:12:39,561
[ALL EXCLAIMING]

263
00:12:39,594 --> 00:12:41,195
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

264
00:12:41,228 --> 00:12:43,998
GUARD: Please! Evac now!

265
00:12:44,031 --> 00:12:45,232
SPIDER-MAN: All right,
everybody, clear out!

266
00:12:45,266 --> 00:12:46,867
This guy is armed
and dangerous.

267
00:12:49,370 --> 00:12:50,904
[STRAINING]

268
00:12:53,608 --> 00:12:54,975
[SPIDER-MAN EXHALES]

269
00:12:57,478 --> 00:13:01,148
Uh...
Get out of the vehicle, ma'am.

270
00:13:01,181 --> 00:13:03,050
I was thinking the same thing.

271
00:13:04,918 --> 00:13:06,020
[WHOOSHES]

272
00:13:08,956 --> 00:13:09,990
[SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]

273
00:13:10,024 --> 00:13:11,859
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

274
00:13:11,892 --> 00:13:13,260
Spider-Man?

275
00:13:14,596 --> 00:13:15,829
Where am I?

276
00:13:21,335 --> 00:13:22,903
[WHOOSHES]

277
00:13:22,936 --> 00:13:24,038
SPIDER-MAN: What the...

278
00:13:24,071 --> 00:13:26,440
[INDISTINCT CLAMOR]

279
00:13:26,473 --> 00:13:28,142
MAN: Move! Move! Move!
Move! Move!

280
00:13:28,175 --> 00:13:29,977
SPIDER-MAN: Keep her for
questioning. Clear the building.

281
00:13:33,113 --> 00:13:35,082
GUARD: Enjoy the ride,
Scorpion!

282
00:13:35,115 --> 00:13:37,818
You won't be seeing
much daylight in supermax.

283
00:13:38,653 --> 00:13:40,854
Scorpions are nocturnal,
buddy.

284
00:13:43,591 --> 00:13:45,292
GUARD 2: [OVER COMMS]
<i>The building is under attack.</i>

285
00:13:45,326 --> 00:13:47,094
<i>Get the prisoner</i>
<i>out of here now!</i>

286
00:13:47,895 --> 00:13:49,863
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

287
00:13:52,232 --> 00:13:53,267
-GUARD: Sir!
-[WHOOSHES]

288
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:55,069
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

289
00:13:56,303 --> 00:13:59,239
[WHOOSHING]

290
00:14:12,052 --> 00:14:13,521
GUARD: You gotta take off now!

291
00:14:13,555 --> 00:14:16,056
The building has been breached.
Go! Go!

292
00:14:16,090 --> 00:14:18,560
Hey, fire it up! Go! Go!

293
00:14:22,229 --> 00:14:23,864
[WHOOSHES]

294
00:14:27,101 --> 00:14:28,902
Change of plans!

295
00:14:28,936 --> 00:14:30,638
Take him to the helipad
at Bellevue.

296
00:14:31,438 --> 00:14:33,207
-What?
-That's an order

297
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,642
from Director Metzger. Go!

298
00:14:34,676 --> 00:14:35,943
Now!

299
00:14:35,976 --> 00:14:37,010
Copy that.

300
00:14:47,988 --> 00:14:49,557
SPIDER-MAN: Hey! What...

301
00:14:49,591 --> 00:14:52,126
-How did I get up here?
-SPIDER-MAN: Uh...

302
00:14:54,161 --> 00:14:55,329
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

303
00:14:55,362 --> 00:14:58,365
Spider-Man, save me,
would you?

304
00:14:59,199 --> 00:15:00,401
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

305
00:15:04,138 --> 00:15:05,139
Who are you?

306
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:07,941
You can see me.

307
00:15:07,975 --> 00:15:09,243
SPIDER-MAN:
Tell me who you are.

308
00:15:10,444 --> 00:15:12,045
-You first.
-[WHOOSHES]

309
00:15:13,013 --> 00:15:14,481
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

310
00:15:14,516 --> 00:15:16,651
MAY: Hey. Hey.

311
00:15:18,185 --> 00:15:20,688
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]
-[WHOOSHES]

312
00:15:22,557 --> 00:15:23,991
You pushed me out.

313
00:15:24,024 --> 00:15:25,693
-[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]
-GUARD: Interesting.

314
00:15:25,727 --> 00:15:27,361
SPIDER-MAN: What the hell
was that?

315
00:15:27,394 --> 00:15:29,496
Did you just try to jump
into my mind?

316
00:15:29,531 --> 00:15:33,367
You know, the whole time
you've been chasing me,

317
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:36,170
you forgot to ask yourself
a very important question.

318
00:15:36,203 --> 00:15:38,005
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

319
00:15:38,038 --> 00:15:39,273
What's in the tank?

320
00:15:41,241 --> 00:15:42,710
GUARD: Go! Move.

321
00:15:43,444 --> 00:15:45,179
[TIMER BEEPING]

322
00:15:52,352 --> 00:15:53,487
[WHOOSHES]

323
00:15:53,521 --> 00:15:55,189
[PANTING]

324
00:15:57,057 --> 00:15:58,058
Spider-Man?

325
00:15:59,226 --> 00:16:01,195
-What just happened?
-[SIREN WAILING]

326
00:16:01,228 --> 00:16:03,297
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

327
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:04,364
I don't know.

328
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:07,535
Hey, good job.

329
00:16:07,569 --> 00:16:08,670
FIREFIGHTER: Hey,
way to go, Spidey.

330
00:16:08,703 --> 00:16:10,505
SPIDER-MAN: You guys okay?
You good?

331
00:16:10,538 --> 00:16:12,507
I swear. All the things
they said I did,

332
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:13,307
I don't remember
doing any of them.

333
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:14,308
SPIDER-MAN: It's okay,
it's okay.

334
00:16:14,341 --> 00:16:15,643
Look, let these people
take good care of you.

335
00:16:15,677 --> 00:16:16,578
I would never hurt you.

336
00:16:16,611 --> 00:16:18,312
-SPIDER-MAN: Okay.
-I love you, Spider-Man.

337
00:16:18,345 --> 00:16:19,747
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.
All right, buddy. All right.

338
00:16:19,781 --> 00:16:22,082
-Hey, what do you got?
-Here, get this.

339
00:16:22,115 --> 00:16:23,685
Chopper took Scorpion
to Bellevue.

340
00:16:23,718 --> 00:16:26,220
Ten minutes later, a guard
walked him right out the door.

341
00:16:26,253 --> 00:16:27,488
SPIDER-MAN: What?
DEWOLFF: Mmm-hmm.

342
00:16:27,522 --> 00:16:28,623
SPIDER-MAN:
What about the tank?

343
00:16:28,656 --> 00:16:31,391
Stolen from the Damage Control
warehouse in Brooklyn.

344
00:16:31,425 --> 00:16:33,595
Driver was a janitor
who worked there.

345
00:16:33,628 --> 00:16:34,495
SPIDER-MAN: You got a motive?

346
00:16:34,529 --> 00:16:37,064
<i>Nada.</i> And no criminal record.

347
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:39,099
Scorpion must've
gotten to her somehow.

348
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:41,803
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah. Maybe.

349
00:16:41,836 --> 00:16:43,470
What do you mean, "maybe"?

350
00:16:43,505 --> 00:16:46,240
SPIDER-MAN: I mean, I...
I don't know.

351
00:16:46,273 --> 00:16:47,575
But I know someone that might.

352
00:16:47,609 --> 00:16:48,710
Where you going?

353
00:16:48,743 --> 00:16:50,512
SPIDER-MAN: You keep following
the leads on Scorpion.

354
00:16:50,545 --> 00:16:52,312
I'm gonna go talk to someone.

355
00:16:52,346 --> 00:16:53,247
[WHOOSHES]

356
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:56,149
[RUSSIAN POP SONG PLAYING]

357
00:17:03,858 --> 00:17:06,193
[SONG CONTINUES PLAYING
OVER SPEAKER]

358
00:17:07,729 --> 00:17:11,331
SPIDER-MAN: Hi, uh,
is this 3250 Brighton Beach?

359
00:17:12,332 --> 00:17:14,401
[SPEAKING RUSSIAN]

360
00:17:15,837 --> 00:17:17,672
SPIDER-MAN: [IN ENGLISH] Okay.

361
00:17:17,705 --> 00:17:19,541
I think I know
what that means.

362
00:17:24,612 --> 00:17:25,747
WOMAN: Take off your clothes.

363
00:17:27,682 --> 00:17:30,350
SPIDER-MAN: Uh, what?

364
00:17:30,384 --> 00:17:32,352
You don't wear clothes
in the <i>banya.</i>

365
00:17:33,487 --> 00:17:34,722
Ditch the leotard.

366
00:17:35,857 --> 00:17:38,191
SPIDER-MAN: This is not
a leotard.

367
00:17:38,225 --> 00:17:40,193
Your text said that
this was your office.

368
00:17:41,461 --> 00:17:43,665
This is my office.

369
00:17:43,698 --> 00:17:45,399
-Get in.
-[SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

370
00:17:45,432 --> 00:17:47,467
Uh, I'm fine, thanks.
I'll just...

371
00:17:47,502 --> 00:17:48,636
Wah-wah. [CHUCKLES]

372
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:50,203
My office, my rules.

373
00:17:50,237 --> 00:17:54,174
This way, you get to enjoy
a nice, relaxing soak,

374
00:17:54,207 --> 00:17:56,476
and I get to see that
you don't have any weapons,

375
00:17:56,511 --> 00:17:57,679
and we both win.

376
00:17:59,814 --> 00:18:00,815
SPIDER-MAN: Okay.

377
00:18:04,151 --> 00:18:05,218
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

378
00:18:06,921 --> 00:18:08,523
[YELENA LAUGHING]

379
00:18:10,257 --> 00:18:12,660
Really? What,
you never take that off?

380
00:18:12,694 --> 00:18:13,728
SPIDER-MAN: No, I...
You know, it defeats

381
00:18:13,761 --> 00:18:14,762
the whole anonymous thing.

382
00:18:14,796 --> 00:18:20,200
Even for your girlfriend
or boyfriend or whatever?

383
00:18:20,233 --> 00:18:22,537
There's a lot of conjecture
online.

384
00:18:22,570 --> 00:18:25,339
And super graphic artwork.
Have you seen?

385
00:18:25,372 --> 00:18:28,175
The one with you
and the ten Mysterios, it's...

386
00:18:28,208 --> 00:18:30,444
[STUTTERING] I've... I've...
I've seen it. I've...

387
00:18:30,477 --> 00:18:31,713
It's hard to unsee,
to be honest.

388
00:18:31,746 --> 00:18:34,749
But, look, I don't have anyone.
I just kinda keep to myself.

389
00:18:34,782 --> 00:18:36,416
All by yourself? All the time?

390
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:38,151
No wonder you're so sad.

391
00:18:38,185 --> 00:18:40,354
-[CHUCKLES] I'm not so sad.
-A little bit.

392
00:18:40,387 --> 00:18:42,389
Could we just talk about what I
came here to talk to you about,

393
00:18:42,422 --> 00:18:43,725
the attack on Damage Control?

394
00:18:43,758 --> 00:18:47,595
Yes.
So, that is more your area.

395
00:18:48,462 --> 00:18:51,431
Like, small potato stuff.

396
00:18:51,465 --> 00:18:57,538
Whereas the New Avengers are
focusing on big potato stuff.

397
00:18:58,573 --> 00:18:59,707
SPIDER-MAN: Right, okay.

398
00:18:59,741 --> 00:19:02,710
Well, there's more to it
than that, you know, the, uh...

399
00:19:02,744 --> 00:19:05,345
[WHISPERING] ...the driver
and the others who were helping,

400
00:19:05,379 --> 00:19:07,815
it was like someone
was talking to me through them.

401
00:19:07,849 --> 00:19:10,417
Like someone was looking at me
through their eyes.

402
00:19:10,450 --> 00:19:12,654
And you're wondering
if it's mind control?

403
00:19:12,687 --> 00:19:13,554
Exactly.

404
00:19:13,588 --> 00:19:15,389
Like how they used on me
in the Red Room?

405
00:19:15,422 --> 00:19:16,958
-Exactly.
-And the other widows?

406
00:19:16,991 --> 00:19:19,192
-Right.
-Right. No, I don't think so.

407
00:19:19,226 --> 00:19:23,798
I actually think it's probably
more like possession.

408
00:19:23,831 --> 00:19:26,233
-SPIDER-MAN: Possession?
-Hmm. Hmm.

409
00:19:26,266 --> 00:19:28,235
Like a ghost or a demon.

410
00:19:28,268 --> 00:19:29,871
-SPIDER-MAN: Oh, man.
-Or in Russia, we have leshy.

411
00:19:29,904 --> 00:19:33,608
Leshy rules the forest
and can possess...

412
00:19:35,977 --> 00:19:37,578
SPIDER-MAN: Sorry.

413
00:19:37,612 --> 00:19:39,747
Whatever it is,
they are looking for something.

414
00:19:39,781 --> 00:19:40,982
This is the fourth attack

415
00:19:41,015 --> 00:19:44,217
on the Damage Control facility
this month.

416
00:19:44,251 --> 00:19:45,753
And what do you think
they're looking for?

417
00:19:45,787 --> 00:19:46,988
YELENA: I don't know.

418
00:19:47,021 --> 00:19:48,656
But you know what?

419
00:19:48,690 --> 00:19:50,792
After the attack today,

420
00:19:50,825 --> 00:19:53,628
there was a cross-agency
cybersecurity alert

421
00:19:53,661 --> 00:19:55,328
that got triggered.

422
00:19:55,362 --> 00:19:56,531
Someone accessed

423
00:19:56,564 --> 00:19:58,700
the Damage Control
restricted servers

424
00:19:58,733 --> 00:20:02,302
using credentials from 30
employees from the way station.

425
00:20:02,335 --> 00:20:04,639
They all searched
for the same thing.

426
00:20:05,907 --> 00:20:06,974
V-Max.

427
00:20:07,008 --> 00:20:08,743
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:20:08,776 --> 00:20:10,210
SPIDER-MAN: V-Max.

429
00:20:11,344 --> 00:20:12,714
Well, what does that mean?

430
00:20:12,747 --> 00:20:15,583
I mean,
it could be alien tech,

431
00:20:15,616 --> 00:20:19,386
or secretive weapon programs,

432
00:20:19,419 --> 00:20:22,623
or launch codes or...

433
00:20:23,925 --> 00:20:26,027
I don't know,
this is for you to figure out.

434
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:27,895
This is small,
baby potato stuff...

435
00:20:27,929 --> 00:20:29,630
-SPIDER-MAN: Okay, okay.
-...not big potato brain stuff.

436
00:20:29,664 --> 00:20:30,998
SPIDER-MAN: You don't
have to shout about it. Jeez.

437
00:20:31,032 --> 00:20:33,000
Maybe I'll just go ask
Damage Control myself.

438
00:20:35,670 --> 00:20:38,573
You know, you're not
completely anonymous anymore.

439
00:20:38,606 --> 00:20:40,440
I've seen your belly button.

440
00:20:40,474 --> 00:20:43,745
SPIDER-MAN: [CHUCKLES] Okay.
YELENA: Bye.

441
00:21:07,034 --> 00:21:08,569
[DOOR SLAMS]

442
00:21:08,603 --> 00:21:09,670
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, God.

443
00:21:10,972 --> 00:21:12,673
Hi, I got an appointment
with, uh...

444
00:21:12,707 --> 00:21:13,975
Director Metzger. Yes.

445
00:21:14,008 --> 00:21:15,610
Please step through the scanner.

446
00:21:17,011 --> 00:21:18,513
[SCANNER POWERS ON]

447
00:21:18,546 --> 00:21:20,548
AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Enhanced human detected.</i>

448
00:21:21,115 --> 00:21:23,316
<i>Superior strength.</i>

449
00:21:23,350 --> 00:21:25,418
<i>Superior agility.</i>

450
00:21:25,452 --> 00:21:26,988
<i>Heightened senses.</i>

451
00:21:27,021 --> 00:21:29,456
<i>Exogenous DNA. Arachnid.</i>

452
00:21:30,858 --> 00:21:33,094
Please remove your face covering
for identity scan.

453
00:21:33,127 --> 00:21:34,529
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, no,
I can't do that.

454
00:21:34,562 --> 00:21:35,663
-That's not possible.
-Failure to remove

455
00:21:35,696 --> 00:21:38,633
your face covering will result
in defensive measures.

456
00:21:38,666 --> 00:21:40,568
SPIDER-MAN: Defensive measures?
What are you talk...

457
00:21:40,601 --> 00:21:41,602
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

458
00:21:41,636 --> 00:21:43,938
Guys, guys, guys!
I can't take my mask off. I'm...

459
00:21:43,971 --> 00:21:46,040
-METZGER: Spider-Man.
-[ALARM BLARING]

460
00:21:46,073 --> 00:21:48,543
-He's all right. At ease.
-[ALARM STOPS]

461
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:54,715
METZGER: My apologies.

462
00:21:54,749 --> 00:21:56,517
We are so glad you're here.

463
00:21:56,551 --> 00:21:59,086
Bill Metzger, Director of
Damage Control. How are you?

464
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:00,755
SPIDER-MAN: I'm good,
thank you.

465
00:22:00,788 --> 00:22:02,089
We had to beef up
security around here,

466
00:22:02,123 --> 00:22:03,323
but I hope
we didn't give you a fright.

467
00:22:03,356 --> 00:22:05,760
-SPIDER-MAN: No, not at all.
-All right, come on. This way.

468
00:22:05,793 --> 00:22:07,427
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

469
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:10,131
METZGER: This floor is mostly
research and administrative.

470
00:22:10,164 --> 00:22:12,099
Downstairs,
we have incident cleanup,

471
00:22:12,133 --> 00:22:13,801
laboratories, agent training.

472
00:22:13,835 --> 00:22:15,402
SPIDER-MAN: Oh.

473
00:22:15,435 --> 00:22:17,004
-Hey, what are they doing here?
-It's okay.

474
00:22:17,972 --> 00:22:20,041
The Hand works for us now.

475
00:22:20,074 --> 00:22:21,843
After you brought them in,
I realized that

476
00:22:21,876 --> 00:22:24,512
fundamentally, they're a group
of kids without a leader.

477
00:22:24,545 --> 00:22:26,514
All they needed
was a little direction.

478
00:22:26,547 --> 00:22:28,481
Then, suddenly, all the things
that made them dangerous

479
00:22:28,516 --> 00:22:30,818
turned them into an invaluable
part of our security team.

480
00:22:31,719 --> 00:22:33,821
[SPEAKING JAPANESE]

481
00:22:36,557 --> 00:22:38,125
[IN ENGLISH] You can look at
the many threats that face us

482
00:22:38,159 --> 00:22:39,359
and see only danger.

483
00:22:40,661 --> 00:22:42,029
Or you can see opportunity.

484
00:22:43,164 --> 00:22:44,699
SPIDER-MAN: Uh, okay.

485
00:22:46,834 --> 00:22:49,103
-[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]
-[SPIDER-MAN WHISTLES]

486
00:22:49,136 --> 00:22:51,172
Wow, look at that.

487
00:22:51,205 --> 00:22:54,041
In the hands of Shocker,
these are a nuisance.

488
00:22:54,075 --> 00:22:55,676
[CLANGS, ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

489
00:22:55,710 --> 00:22:57,511
But it doesn't mean we can't
learn from the technology,

490
00:22:57,545 --> 00:22:59,814
or respect the innovation.

491
00:22:59,847 --> 00:23:01,849
Our mission is to
redirect destructive energy

492
00:23:01,883 --> 00:23:03,885
into something useful.

493
00:23:03,918 --> 00:23:05,653
That's the true meaning
of Damage Control.

494
00:23:09,123 --> 00:23:10,925
[KNOCKING]

495
00:23:10,958 --> 00:23:12,126
SPIDER-MAN:
Be careful with that.

496
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:14,061
Right this way.

497
00:23:17,665 --> 00:23:18,933
SPIDER-MAN: I, uh...
I wanted to talk to you

498
00:23:18,966 --> 00:23:21,035
about the recent attacks
on the agency.

499
00:23:21,068 --> 00:23:22,970
There's been four, right?

500
00:23:23,004 --> 00:23:24,071
Please have a seat.

501
00:23:25,172 --> 00:23:27,074
You are right.

502
00:23:27,108 --> 00:23:30,111
It appears we're faced with
a threat we can't control.

503
00:23:30,144 --> 00:23:31,411
One we can't even see.

504
00:23:34,048 --> 00:23:35,415
But you can.

505
00:23:36,117 --> 00:23:37,818
I saw the security footage.

506
00:23:39,186 --> 00:23:42,489
I also read
Detective DeWolff's report.

507
00:23:42,523 --> 00:23:44,892
I believe you understand
exactly what we're up against.

508
00:23:44,926 --> 00:23:46,794
SPIDER-MAN: [SIGHS]
Someone or something

509
00:23:46,827 --> 00:23:48,763
that can
hop into people's minds.

510
00:23:49,797 --> 00:23:50,865
But not yours.

511
00:23:50,898 --> 00:23:53,634
SPIDER-MAN: No, I mean,
it tried, but it couldn't.

512
00:24:02,777 --> 00:24:04,211
I'm gonna be honest with you.

513
00:24:05,112 --> 00:24:06,547
We're on our heels right now.

514
00:24:07,682 --> 00:24:08,950
God forbid
if it were to get in here

515
00:24:08,983 --> 00:24:10,551
and find whatever it is
it's looking for,

516
00:24:10,584 --> 00:24:14,155
the consequences
could be unimaginable.

517
00:24:16,991 --> 00:24:18,826
SPIDER-MAN: Well, let me guess,
is whatever it's looking for

518
00:24:18,859 --> 00:24:19,961
in that giant vault?

519
00:24:22,930 --> 00:24:25,166
There are some things,
because of the nature of my job

520
00:24:25,199 --> 00:24:26,968
I cannot tell you.

521
00:24:27,001 --> 00:24:29,870
But I believe you are our
best defense against this.

522
00:24:29,904 --> 00:24:31,872
You're the only one
who can sense it.

523
00:24:31,906 --> 00:24:33,908
You're the only one
who's immune to it.

524
00:24:33,941 --> 00:24:35,643
I'm counting on you
to defeat it.

525
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:41,916
SPIDER-MAN: That's a pretty
good speech, Director.

526
00:24:41,949 --> 00:24:43,084
I'll do everything that I can,
I promise.

527
00:24:45,086 --> 00:24:47,555
Well, then consider yourself
a friend of Damage Control.

528
00:24:47,588 --> 00:24:48,589
SPIDER-MAN: Thank you.

529
00:24:49,557 --> 00:24:50,558
I'll be in touch.

530
00:24:51,826 --> 00:24:54,762
Oh. Uh, I wanted to ask, um...

531
00:24:54,795 --> 00:24:57,298
the phrase "V-Max" doesn't
mean anything to you, does it?

532
00:24:57,331 --> 00:24:58,833
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

533
00:24:58,866 --> 00:25:01,736
No. Where'd you hear that?

534
00:25:01,769 --> 00:25:04,672
Oh, it's just, you know,
nature of being a superhero,

535
00:25:04,705 --> 00:25:06,007
there are some things
I just can't tell ya.

536
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:07,208
[LAUGHING]

537
00:25:07,241 --> 00:25:08,676
SPIDER-MAN: Anyway,
I'll see you later.

538
00:25:09,710 --> 00:25:11,612
You guys are doing great.
Keep it up.

539
00:25:11,645 --> 00:25:13,748
<i>I don't think Metzger knows</i>
<i>any more than we do,</i>

540
00:25:13,781 --> 00:25:15,850
<i>but I told him</i>
<i>I'd do whatever I can to help.</i>

541
00:25:15,883 --> 00:25:18,219
You wanna help?
The best thing you could do

542
00:25:18,252 --> 00:25:20,588
<i>is find Scorpion.</i>
<i>He's our only lead.</i>

543
00:25:20,621 --> 00:25:22,289
Yeah, I know.
I have every camera in the city

544
00:25:22,323 --> 00:25:24,825
running a facial recognition
scan for him.

545
00:25:24,859 --> 00:25:26,794
That sounds super illegal,
Spider-Man.

546
00:25:26,827 --> 00:25:28,129
I'mma pretend
I didn't hear that.

547
00:25:28,162 --> 00:25:29,697
Yeah, probably for the best.
[CHUCKLES]

548
00:25:29,730 --> 00:25:31,132
But look, if he shows his face,
we'll know.

549
00:25:31,165 --> 00:25:32,767
MAN: Do you have
any mini-kegs?

550
00:25:33,601 --> 00:25:34,769
CASHIER: Down at the end.

551
00:25:34,802 --> 00:25:35,803
Thanks.

552
00:25:39,006 --> 00:25:40,107
I'll call you back.

553
00:25:42,276 --> 00:25:45,112
-Aha.
-[SLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

554
00:25:45,146 --> 00:25:46,147
Easy.

555
00:25:50,284 --> 00:25:53,854
Hey, uh, also,
you got any Sharkfire Energy?

556
00:25:53,888 --> 00:25:55,189
Yeah.

557
00:25:56,323 --> 00:25:57,425
Oh, no, no, no. [CHUCKLES]

558
00:25:57,458 --> 00:25:59,960
[STUTTERS] I don't want any.
That stuff will kill you.

559
00:25:59,994 --> 00:26:01,729
You know, all my friends were
drinking them during finals

560
00:26:01,762 --> 00:26:02,730
and now they're addicted.

561
00:26:02,763 --> 00:26:06,000
And so I'm gonna need you
to not sell me any.

562
00:26:06,033 --> 00:26:07,168
Memorize my face.

563
00:26:08,302 --> 00:26:11,939
Please do not sell this guy
any Sharkfire.

564
00:26:12,840 --> 00:26:13,974
Sure. Whatever.

565
00:26:14,942 --> 00:26:16,110
NED: Actually, I'll take one.

566
00:26:16,911 --> 00:26:18,079
Last one.

567
00:26:18,112 --> 00:26:19,647
[STUTTERING] Maybe two.

568
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:21,782
And then never sell me any.

569
00:26:23,250 --> 00:26:25,352
-[SOFTLY] Damn it.
-[CASH REGISTER BEEPING]

570
00:26:25,386 --> 00:26:26,555
[CASH REGISTER DINGS]

571
00:26:39,233 --> 00:26:41,268
[POP SONG PLAYING]

572
00:26:52,246 --> 00:26:53,114
[EXHALES]

573
00:26:58,419 --> 00:26:59,787
MAN 1: Yo, Ned!

574
00:26:59,820 --> 00:27:01,088
-Oh, what?
-MAN 2: Ned!

575
00:27:01,122 --> 00:27:02,857
-Give me that.
-Oh, my guy, appreciate you.

576
00:27:02,890 --> 00:27:04,358
-Let's go!
-Yeah, man.

577
00:27:04,391 --> 00:27:05,392
Let's go!

578
00:27:20,207 --> 00:27:22,743
[SONG CONTINUES
PLAYING OVER SPEAKER]

579
00:27:22,776 --> 00:27:24,778
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

580
00:27:32,486 --> 00:27:34,255
[WOMEN LAUGHING]

581
00:27:40,094 --> 00:27:42,863
You need a drink.
Take this, take this, take it.

582
00:27:42,897 --> 00:27:43,898
Thanks.

583
00:27:47,034 --> 00:27:48,469
WOMAN: Excuse me.

584
00:27:48,503 --> 00:27:50,371
[INDISTINCT CHATTER CONTINUES]

585
00:28:31,779 --> 00:28:32,446
Oh.

586
00:28:34,215 --> 00:28:35,482
Oh. Um...

587
00:28:35,517 --> 00:28:38,385
See you've stumbled across
my board. [CHUCKLES]

588
00:28:38,419 --> 00:28:40,454
I'm not one of those weirdos,
I swear.

589
00:28:40,487 --> 00:28:41,855
He actually saved me
and my friends' lives

590
00:28:41,889 --> 00:28:42,957
a few times in high school.

591
00:28:44,091 --> 00:28:45,960
-Oh, cool.
-NED: Yeah, yeah.

592
00:28:45,993 --> 00:28:48,495
And ever since, I've just been
trying to figure out who he is.

593
00:28:48,530 --> 00:28:51,031
[STUTTERS] Not to unmask him
to the world or anything,

594
00:28:51,065 --> 00:28:52,933
just to know, you know?

595
00:28:52,967 --> 00:28:55,202
And to, hopefully,
thank him face to face.

596
00:28:57,805 --> 00:29:01,308
I actually created this app
that monitors his sightings.

597
00:29:01,342 --> 00:29:03,010
Wait, you created
Spidey Tracker?

598
00:29:03,043 --> 00:29:04,912
You heard of it? Nice.
[CHUCKLES]

599
00:29:04,945 --> 00:29:05,980
[ <i>SPIDER-MAN</i> THEME
PLAYING ON DEVICE]

600
00:29:06,013 --> 00:29:07,281
APP VOICE: <i>Where is Spider-Man?</i>

601
00:29:07,314 --> 00:29:09,416
NED: Little chat room
right there. [CHUCKLES]

602
00:29:09,450 --> 00:29:12,086
Now, we know
he's definitely from Queens.

603
00:29:12,119 --> 00:29:13,854
Not the biggest revelation.

604
00:29:13,887 --> 00:29:16,423
But I have been able
to narrow it down

605
00:29:16,457 --> 00:29:18,392
to two prime suspects.

606
00:29:22,396 --> 00:29:25,866
Yeah, if you knew who they were,
it would really blow your mind.

607
00:29:25,899 --> 00:29:27,501
-I'm sure.
-[SIGHS]

608
00:29:27,535 --> 00:29:28,536
[CLICKS TONGUE] Ned,
by the way.

609
00:29:29,470 --> 00:29:30,672
Oh, I'm, um...

610
00:29:30,705 --> 00:29:33,207
[EXHALES] God, there's, like,
50 people in our apartment.

611
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:34,074
Statistically speaking,
that means

612
00:29:34,108 --> 00:29:36,410
at least two of them
are sociopaths,

613
00:29:36,443 --> 00:29:38,846
-which is kind of cool.
-[NED LAUGHS]

614
00:29:40,914 --> 00:29:41,915
Nice flowers.

615
00:29:43,083 --> 00:29:46,387
Oh, they're, uh,
a housewarming gift.

616
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:47,488
-MJ: Really?
-Yeah.

617
00:29:47,522 --> 00:29:49,089
Oh, okay. [CHUCKLES]

618
00:29:49,123 --> 00:29:50,357
Most people just brought
beer and chips.

619
00:29:50,391 --> 00:29:51,593
That's very nice.

620
00:29:51,626 --> 00:29:53,927
Uh, I'm MJ.

621
00:29:53,961 --> 00:29:57,298
I'm, uh... [CLEARS THROAT]
I'm, uh, Maynard.

622
00:29:58,232 --> 00:30:00,301
Uh, Maynard.

623
00:30:00,334 --> 00:30:02,870
Oh, you two
don't know each other?

624
00:30:02,903 --> 00:30:04,905
Uh, no, I'm a neighbor.

625
00:30:04,938 --> 00:30:06,006
Hmm, friendly neighbor.

626
00:30:06,608 --> 00:30:07,975
[COUGHING]

627
00:30:09,644 --> 00:30:11,312
[CHUCKLING] Sorry.

628
00:30:11,345 --> 00:30:13,480
So, how was the interview?

629
00:30:13,515 --> 00:30:15,215
I'm gonna go
put these in water.

630
00:30:15,249 --> 00:30:17,151
It was nice to meet you,
Maynard. Nerd.

631
00:30:17,184 --> 00:30:18,185
Maynard. Yeah.

632
00:30:18,919 --> 00:30:20,487
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

633
00:30:20,522 --> 00:30:23,390
Did you go?
Please tell me that you went.

634
00:30:23,424 --> 00:30:24,559
MJ: Yeah. No, I went.

635
00:30:24,592 --> 00:30:26,193
And?

636
00:30:26,226 --> 00:30:27,361
And I got the job.

637
00:30:27,394 --> 00:30:29,531
Oh, my God, MJ,
that's amazing.

638
00:30:29,564 --> 00:30:31,432
I turned it down.

639
00:30:31,465 --> 00:30:32,667
NED: What?

640
00:30:32,701 --> 00:30:35,135
MJ: Yeah. I don't wanna work
for some soulless corporation.

641
00:30:35,169 --> 00:30:39,006
NED: [SIGHS, STUTTERS]
They're not all soulless.

642
00:30:39,039 --> 00:30:40,974
Okay.
They're all mostly soulless.

643
00:30:41,008 --> 00:30:42,943
But don't you want, like,
health insurance?

644
00:30:42,976 --> 00:30:45,212
Yeah, of course I do.
But at what cost?

645
00:30:45,245 --> 00:30:46,947
Depends on your deductible.
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

646
00:30:48,015 --> 00:30:49,617
Oh, you mean,
like, your principles?

647
00:30:49,651 --> 00:30:50,951
-MJ: Yes.
-Sorry.

648
00:30:50,984 --> 00:30:52,286
I don't know.
I know it sounds cheesy,

649
00:30:52,319 --> 00:30:54,622
but something
is just telling me

650
00:30:54,656 --> 00:30:56,290
that I'm
supposed to be waiting

651
00:30:56,323 --> 00:30:58,258
for something great,
you know?

652
00:30:59,426 --> 00:31:01,195
NED: Okay. Well, um,

653
00:31:01,228 --> 00:31:04,031
to, uh,
waiting for something great.

654
00:31:04,064 --> 00:31:05,099
MJ: To waiting
for something great.

655
00:31:05,132 --> 00:31:06,166
[CLINKING]

656
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:08,035
BOYFRIEND: Well,
the wait is over.

657
00:31:08,068 --> 00:31:10,104
-Uh-oh. [LAUGHS]
-To your new home.

658
00:31:10,137 --> 00:31:11,438
Dude, this is top-shelf.

659
00:31:11,472 --> 00:31:12,540
BOYFRIEND: Just like you.

660
00:31:12,574 --> 00:31:15,976
-MJ: Aw!
-Aw! Dude. [GRUNTS]

661
00:31:16,009 --> 00:31:17,344
-I'm gonna hide this.
-[SNAPS FINGERS]

662
00:31:19,346 --> 00:31:20,881
I lifted this
off of him again.

663
00:31:22,584 --> 00:31:25,319
But what if Ned needs
the fire of a thousand sharks?

664
00:31:25,352 --> 00:31:28,590
-You mean heart palpitations?
-[LAUGHING]

665
00:31:28,623 --> 00:31:30,391
-You can't save everyone.
-I can try.

666
00:31:33,026 --> 00:31:34,027
BOYFRIEND: That's my girl.

667
00:31:37,297 --> 00:31:39,433
[POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING]

668
00:31:44,171 --> 00:31:45,939
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

669
00:31:50,545 --> 00:31:51,579
I'm sorry. I gotta...

670
00:31:56,684 --> 00:31:57,552
[GRUNTS]

671
00:31:59,353 --> 00:32:01,355
[POIGNANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

672
00:32:12,667 --> 00:32:16,270
When we get into MIT,
we should live together.

673
00:32:16,303 --> 00:32:18,506
PETER: <i>Yeah, for sure.</i>
MJ: <i>Yeah, I'd love that.</i>

674
00:32:18,540 --> 00:32:21,341
Be a fresh start.
And we'll all be together.

675
00:32:23,076 --> 00:32:24,411
Yeah, no, you're right.
Yeah. [CHUCKLES]

676
00:32:24,445 --> 00:32:25,547
Fresh start.

677
00:32:28,616 --> 00:32:30,718
PETER: <i>You're gonna</i>
<i>forget who I am.</i>

678
00:32:30,752 --> 00:32:32,620
MJ: <i>Forget who you are?</i>
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

679
00:32:32,654 --> 00:32:35,590
PETER: <i>It's okay.</i>
<i>I'm gonna come and find you,</i>

680
00:32:35,623 --> 00:32:36,990
<i>and I'll explain everything.</i>

681
00:32:38,225 --> 00:32:40,595
-I love...
-Just wait. [SNIFFLES]

682
00:32:40,628 --> 00:32:42,664
[VOICE SHAKING] Wait and tell me
when you see me again.

683
00:32:47,301 --> 00:32:51,338
My name is Peter Parker,
and I would like a coffee.

684
00:32:53,040 --> 00:32:55,175
Is there anything else?

685
00:32:57,211 --> 00:32:59,112
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

686
00:33:04,519 --> 00:33:05,520
No.

687
00:33:14,194 --> 00:33:15,697
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

688
00:33:19,333 --> 00:33:20,568
[RAIN PATTERING]

689
00:33:36,718 --> 00:33:38,252
[GRUNTING]

690
00:33:47,729 --> 00:33:49,363
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

691
00:34:05,613 --> 00:34:07,281
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

692
00:34:07,314 --> 00:34:08,382
MAY: <i>Hey.</i>

693
00:34:09,584 --> 00:34:10,585
Hey.

694
00:34:12,820 --> 00:34:14,856
You think
you don't have to listen to me

695
00:34:14,889 --> 00:34:16,558
now that you've got powers?

696
00:34:16,591 --> 00:34:18,593
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

697
00:34:21,461 --> 00:34:23,698
You know, this...

698
00:34:23,731 --> 00:34:26,601
this whole thing
can get really scary.

699
00:34:27,434 --> 00:34:28,435
You know that?

700
00:34:29,737 --> 00:34:31,405
Well, yeah,
it's already pretty scary.

701
00:34:33,641 --> 00:34:34,876
Yeah.

702
00:34:34,909 --> 00:34:38,245
And things can change, like...
[SNAPS FINGERS] ...very quickly,

703
00:34:38,278 --> 00:34:40,480
in ways that we can't
even imagine right now.

704
00:34:41,214 --> 00:34:42,482
Believe me, I know.

705
00:34:45,753 --> 00:34:47,220
I don't think you do know.

706
00:34:49,724 --> 00:34:50,692
What do you mean?

707
00:34:50,725 --> 00:34:53,561
-[GASPS, PANTS]
-[SIRENS WAILING DISTANTLY]

708
00:35:10,210 --> 00:35:12,212
[GRUNTS, BREATHES HEAVILY]

709
00:35:12,245 --> 00:35:13,548
[GROANING]

710
00:35:16,416 --> 00:35:18,151
Oh, God. Whoa!

711
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:21,288
[YELPING]

712
00:35:23,524 --> 00:35:25,325
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

713
00:35:25,359 --> 00:35:27,327
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

714
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:35,302
[EXCLAIMS, YELPS]

715
00:35:35,335 --> 00:35:36,203
[THUDS]

716
00:35:39,574 --> 00:35:40,875
[EXCLAIMING IN PAIN]

717
00:35:48,650 --> 00:35:49,751
[GROANS]

718
00:35:59,761 --> 00:36:00,762
[SOFTLY] What?

719
00:36:01,963 --> 00:36:03,497
[SIREN WAILS]

720
00:36:05,767 --> 00:36:07,267
[GRUNTING]

721
00:36:09,871 --> 00:36:11,238
[GROANS]

722
00:36:13,407 --> 00:36:14,408
[WINCES]

723
00:36:16,476 --> 00:36:18,713
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

724
00:36:18,746 --> 00:36:19,747
Oh, I, uh...

725
00:36:20,948 --> 00:36:22,249
I live here. I just, um...

726
00:36:24,652 --> 00:36:25,687
I'm gonna grab my stuff.

727
00:36:28,956 --> 00:36:30,223
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

728
00:36:44,471 --> 00:36:45,506
Is that my shirt?

729
00:36:46,473 --> 00:36:47,942
[CHUCKLES]

730
00:36:47,975 --> 00:36:48,976
No.

731
00:36:49,777 --> 00:36:50,978
-Oh, cute dog.
-[BARKS]

732
00:36:51,012 --> 00:36:52,212
Oh, sh...

733
00:36:52,947 --> 00:36:55,315
[MASHING BUTTON]

734
00:36:55,348 --> 00:36:56,884
-[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]
-[ELEVATOR DINGS]

735
00:36:57,652 --> 00:36:58,986
PETER: [SIGHS] Okay.

736
00:37:03,057 --> 00:37:04,625
[GRUNTS, PANTING]

737
00:37:04,659 --> 00:37:06,661
[MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

738
00:37:19,574 --> 00:37:22,877
E.V.: <i>Hi, Peter.</i>
<i>You have 107 new alerts.</i>

739
00:37:22,910 --> 00:37:24,545
<i>Please check backlog.</i>

740
00:37:25,613 --> 00:37:27,582
[MACHINE WHIRRING]

741
00:37:27,615 --> 00:37:28,683
[MACHINE STOPS]

742
00:37:30,985 --> 00:37:34,421
What is happening?

743
00:37:35,489 --> 00:37:36,958
E.V.: <i>The results</i>
<i>of your body scan</i>

744
00:37:36,991 --> 00:37:38,626
<i>show a surge in the hormones</i>

745
00:37:38,659 --> 00:37:40,995
<i>associated with</i>
<i>your arachnid DNA,</i>

746
00:37:41,028 --> 00:37:43,898
<i>resulting in the formation</i>
<i>of organic web spinnerets</i>

747
00:37:43,931 --> 00:37:46,934
<i>and dangerously heightened</i>
<i>sensory receptors.</i>

748
00:37:46,968 --> 00:37:47,869
[STUTTERS] Okay,

749
00:37:47,902 --> 00:37:49,070
-but I feel fine.
-[WEB SHOOTER CLICKING]

750
00:37:49,103 --> 00:37:51,706
E.V.: <i>Prolonged isolation</i>
<i>or emotional trauma</i>

751
00:37:51,739 --> 00:37:54,341
<i>could be contributing</i>
<i>to this sudden change.</i>

752
00:37:54,374 --> 00:37:56,911
<i>Have you experienced any</i>
<i>recent traumatic events?</i>

753
00:37:59,781 --> 00:38:01,448
<i>Peter?</i>

754
00:38:01,481 --> 00:38:02,950
SPIDER-MAN: I'm fine, E.V.

755
00:38:02,984 --> 00:38:04,519
E.V.: <i>You don't seem fine.</i>

756
00:38:04,552 --> 00:38:05,553
<i>I recommend you take</i>

757
00:38:05,586 --> 00:38:07,088
<i>-some time to rebalance.</i>
-[GADGET BEEPS]

758
00:38:07,121 --> 00:38:08,923
Well, that's not really
an option, is it?

759
00:38:12,026 --> 00:38:14,529
-[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]
-[CLATTERING]

760
00:38:15,395 --> 00:38:17,397
[SQUELCHING]

761
00:38:19,901 --> 00:38:20,935
[CLANKING]

762
00:38:20,968 --> 00:38:21,969
[OBJECTS SHATTER]

763
00:38:25,540 --> 00:38:27,875
E.V.: <i>Mechanical web shooters</i>
<i>and organic webs</i>

764
00:38:27,909 --> 00:38:30,044
<i>cannot be used simultaneously.</i>

765
00:38:31,646 --> 00:38:32,847
SPIDER-MAN: Come on, Peter.

766
00:38:34,081 --> 00:38:35,850
[CAR HORN HONKING]

767
00:38:35,883 --> 00:38:39,386
-[BREATHING DEEPLY]
-[TIME SLOWS DOWN]

768
00:38:39,419 --> 00:38:42,455
-[SLOWED WATER DRIPPING]
-[BREATHING HEAVILY]

769
00:38:46,093 --> 00:38:48,663
[REVERBERATES]

770
00:38:48,696 --> 00:38:50,731
[PRONOUNCED CRINKLING]

771
00:38:52,733 --> 00:38:55,368
E.V.: <i>Alert.</i>
<i>Senses are overloaded.</i>

772
00:38:55,402 --> 00:38:57,404
-[WINGS FLAPPING SHARPLY]
-[SIREN CHIRPS, WAILS SHARPLY]

773
00:38:57,437 --> 00:38:58,139
-[PANTING]
-E.V.: <i>Alert.</i>

774
00:38:58,172 --> 00:38:59,707
<i>Senses are overloaded.</i>

775
00:38:59,740 --> 00:39:01,976
[GARBLED, OVERLAPPING SOUNDS]

776
00:39:02,009 --> 00:39:05,012
E.V.: [ECHOING] <i>Alert. Alert.</i>
<i>Senses are overloaded. Alert.</i>

777
00:39:05,046 --> 00:39:07,782
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS, PANTS]
-[SOUNDS SUBSIDE]

778
00:39:08,783 --> 00:39:10,885
What the hell was that?

779
00:39:10,918 --> 00:39:12,086
E.V.: <i>Your heightened senses</i>

780
00:39:12,119 --> 00:39:14,822
<i>are taking in</i>
<i>too much information at once.</i>

781
00:39:14,856 --> 00:39:18,059
SPIDER-MAN: [BREATHING HEAVILY]
Okay. It's okay.

782
00:39:18,092 --> 00:39:18,993
It's okay.

783
00:39:19,026 --> 00:39:21,896
All right, organic webs.
Peter Two had 'em.

784
00:39:21,929 --> 00:39:23,764
He was cool. You're cool.

785
00:39:24,599 --> 00:39:27,535
[SQUELCHING]

786
00:39:27,568 --> 00:39:29,704
[GAGS, RETCHES]

787
00:39:29,737 --> 00:39:31,672
[COUGHS]

788
00:39:31,706 --> 00:39:34,008
Ugh! Oh, my God, that's hideous.

789
00:39:34,041 --> 00:39:35,910
[EXCLAIMS] Okay, here we go.

790
00:39:36,677 --> 00:39:38,079
[GRUNTS]

791
00:39:38,112 --> 00:39:40,915
Okay, that didn't work.
[GRUNTS, GROANS]

792
00:39:40,948 --> 00:39:43,084
Organic webs. Come on!
And web!

793
00:39:43,117 --> 00:39:44,986
[GROANING]

794
00:39:46,754 --> 00:39:47,755
No, no!

795
00:39:50,791 --> 00:39:52,660
Stop! [PANTING]

796
00:39:53,995 --> 00:39:56,864
-[SUIT BEEPING]
-What's going on, E.V.?

797
00:39:56,898 --> 00:39:59,567
E.V.: <i>Shots fired at</i>
<i>the Damage Control Data Center</i>

798
00:39:59,600 --> 00:40:00,568
<i>in Manhattan.</i>

799
00:40:00,601 --> 00:40:03,004
<i>Suspect facial match</i>
<i>with Scorpion.</i>

800
00:40:03,037 --> 00:40:04,505
SPIDER-MAN: Okay,
I'm on my way.

801
00:40:05,072 --> 00:40:07,074
Come on. Three, two...

802
00:40:07,108 --> 00:40:08,142
Web! [GRUNTS]

803
00:40:08,175 --> 00:40:11,612
[STRAINING, SCREAMING]

804
00:40:11,646 --> 00:40:14,582
-Web, stop! [GROANS]
-[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

805
00:40:14,615 --> 00:40:15,683
[SCREAMS]

806
00:40:15,716 --> 00:40:17,785
Web! Stop! Birds, birds, birds!

807
00:40:17,818 --> 00:40:19,654
[GROANING] Web! Stop.

808
00:40:19,687 --> 00:40:22,056
-[PIGEON COOS]
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

809
00:40:23,925 --> 00:40:25,159
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

810
00:40:25,993 --> 00:40:27,628
Web! Stop.

811
00:40:27,662 --> 00:40:29,496
Oh, God! [GROANS]

812
00:40:29,530 --> 00:40:32,133
-Web! Stop, stop, stop. [YELLS]
-[MUSIC ENDS]

813
00:40:32,166 --> 00:40:33,935
-[PEOPLE SCREAMING]
-[SIREN WAILING]

814
00:40:33,968 --> 00:40:35,970
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

815
00:40:37,638 --> 00:40:39,707
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

816
00:40:39,740 --> 00:40:41,208
[GUARD SCREAMS, GROANS]

817
00:40:42,543 --> 00:40:43,544
[GUNS FIRING]

818
00:40:45,780 --> 00:40:47,114
[BULLETS RICOCHETING]

819
00:40:48,883 --> 00:40:51,085
-[OFFICERS SCREAMING]
-[CAR ALARMS BLARING]

820
00:40:51,118 --> 00:40:52,787
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

821
00:40:55,256 --> 00:40:57,490
I don't know
what you're looking for.

822
00:40:57,525 --> 00:40:59,492
I'm looking for V-Max.

823
00:41:00,227 --> 00:41:01,929
[GUARD GASPING]

824
00:41:01,963 --> 00:41:04,131
I don't know anything.

825
00:41:04,165 --> 00:41:05,766
SCORPION: I'll see for myself.

826
00:41:06,634 --> 00:41:08,836
[SPIDER-MAN SCREAMING]

827
00:41:08,869 --> 00:41:10,938
-Oh, God, oh, God!
-[THUDDING]

828
00:41:10,972 --> 00:41:12,974
[SPIDER-MAN YELPING]

829
00:41:14,141 --> 00:41:15,643
-[GROANS]
-Hmm.

830
00:41:16,610 --> 00:41:18,546
-[GUARD YELPS]
-[BODY THUDS]

831
00:41:18,579 --> 00:41:19,647
SPIDER-MAN:
I'm sorry I'm late.

832
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:21,082
I've had a really crazy day.

833
00:41:22,717 --> 00:41:24,518
[GROANING]

834
00:41:29,557 --> 00:41:31,025
[BOTH GRUNTING]

835
00:41:39,767 --> 00:41:41,569
SPIDER-MAN: Scorpion, do we
really gotta keep doing this?

836
00:41:41,602 --> 00:41:43,070
My head is killing me.

837
00:41:44,105 --> 00:41:45,673
You think I'm Scorpion?

838
00:41:47,274 --> 00:41:48,275
-Web!
-[SQUIRTS]

839
00:41:50,277 --> 00:41:52,146
What's happening to you?

840
00:41:52,179 --> 00:41:53,614
[BOTH GRUNTING]

841
00:41:58,152 --> 00:41:59,687
Huh.

842
00:41:59,720 --> 00:42:01,689
You can't sense me anymore.

843
00:42:01,722 --> 00:42:03,024
[BOTH GRUNTING]

844
00:42:04,725 --> 00:42:05,559
SPIDER-MAN: You.

845
00:42:05,593 --> 00:42:07,661
What's going on with you,
Spider-Man?

846
00:42:07,695 --> 00:42:09,697
-[METAL CREAKING]
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

847
00:42:16,904 --> 00:42:19,607
E.V.: <i>Warning.</i>
<i>Arachnid hormones increasing.</i>

848
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:21,108
-[SUIT BEEPING]
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

849
00:42:21,142 --> 00:42:22,143
[DISTORTED WARBLE]

850
00:42:23,744 --> 00:42:25,746
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

851
00:42:27,882 --> 00:42:29,817
[SCORPION GROANING]

852
00:42:33,954 --> 00:42:35,156
[GROANS]

853
00:42:35,189 --> 00:42:36,223
SPIDER-MAN: Who are you?

854
00:42:37,191 --> 00:42:38,726
Do you know who you are?

855
00:42:38,759 --> 00:42:40,094
[SIREN WAILING]

856
00:42:42,630 --> 00:42:43,931
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

857
00:42:48,302 --> 00:42:50,971
[SIRENS APPROACHING]

858
00:42:51,005 --> 00:42:53,340
-[CRACKLING]
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

859
00:42:57,244 --> 00:42:58,813
[SCORPION GROANING]

860
00:43:02,850 --> 00:43:03,918
OFFICER 1: We need some help
over here.

861
00:43:03,951 --> 00:43:04,852
OFFICER 2: Get back!
Coming through.

862
00:43:04,885 --> 00:43:06,287
[BOTH GRUNT]

863
00:43:08,789 --> 00:43:10,091
-[EXHALES]
-[WHOOSHES]

864
00:43:10,958 --> 00:43:12,793
[GASPS, BREATHES DEEPLY]

865
00:43:13,861 --> 00:43:14,929
Spider-Man.

866
00:43:16,030 --> 00:43:17,631
[EXHALES]

867
00:43:17,665 --> 00:43:18,999
What the hell?

868
00:43:19,033 --> 00:43:20,634
DEWOLFF: Somebody get a medic.

869
00:43:20,668 --> 00:43:22,736
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

870
00:43:22,770 --> 00:43:24,805
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

871
00:43:24,839 --> 00:43:26,841
[CHATTER ECHOING]

872
00:43:37,418 --> 00:43:38,919
[SPIDER-MAN EXHALES]

873
00:43:40,921 --> 00:43:41,956
DeWolff, is she hurt?

874
00:43:43,090 --> 00:43:44,391
Is she okay?

875
00:43:44,425 --> 00:43:45,926
-Is she okay?
-DEWOLFF: No!

876
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:46,994
-SPIDER-MAN: Just let me go...
-Don't!

877
00:43:47,027 --> 00:43:47,928
What is going on with you?

878
00:43:47,962 --> 00:43:49,263
SPIDER-MAN: That wasn't
Scorpion, okay?

879
00:43:49,296 --> 00:43:50,431
[STUTTERING] I mean it was,

880
00:43:50,464 --> 00:43:53,200
but he was possessed by whatever
hijacked that tank, okay?

881
00:43:53,234 --> 00:43:55,369
-Look, please can I just...
-All right, listen. Slow down.

882
00:43:55,402 --> 00:43:57,938
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING IN PAIN]

883
00:43:57,972 --> 00:43:59,874
Listen, I don't know
what this is,

884
00:43:59,907 --> 00:44:02,243
but I need you
to pull it together.

885
00:44:02,276 --> 00:44:03,878
You almost killed a cop.

886
00:44:06,714 --> 00:44:08,182
This isn't you.

887
00:44:08,215 --> 00:44:09,884
SPIDER-MAN: I know. I'm sorry.

888
00:44:09,917 --> 00:44:13,354
If you act like this again,
I cannot protect you.

889
00:44:13,387 --> 00:44:16,223
Whatever this is,
you need to fix it.

890
00:44:16,257 --> 00:44:18,259
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

891
00:44:27,234 --> 00:44:28,235
[GRUNTS]

892
00:44:31,839 --> 00:44:32,873
[GROANS SOFTLY]

893
00:44:35,075 --> 00:44:37,378
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

894
00:44:37,411 --> 00:44:39,847
PROFESSOR: <i>Through lattice</i>
<i>chromodynamics,</i>

895
00:44:41,148 --> 00:44:44,952
we can arrange time and space
in a grid.

896
00:44:44,985 --> 00:44:47,721
Which allows us to simulate

897
00:44:47,755 --> 00:44:49,957
the quarks binding
into the protons.

898
00:44:50,991 --> 00:44:53,227
Cindy, is this
a question about protons

899
00:44:53,260 --> 00:44:55,362
-or more stuff about Avengers?
-[SCATTERED LAUGHTER]

900
00:44:55,396 --> 00:44:58,933
[CHUCKLES] Okay.
Guys, I love to tell stories,

901
00:44:58,966 --> 00:45:00,234
but you know I...
I gotta teach you

902
00:45:00,267 --> 00:45:02,002
some physics
at some point here.

903
00:45:02,036 --> 00:45:03,971
[STUDENTS BOOING, JEERING]

904
00:45:06,273 --> 00:45:08,510
All right. Let it rip, Cindy.

905
00:45:08,543 --> 00:45:11,912
If Thanos was so worried
about over-population,

906
00:45:11,946 --> 00:45:13,747
why didn't he
just use the magic glove

907
00:45:13,781 --> 00:45:14,949
to make more food?

908
00:45:15,816 --> 00:45:17,751
[STUDENTS MURMURING]

909
00:45:19,019 --> 00:45:21,121
Arthur, you wanna
answer that question?

910
00:45:21,989 --> 00:45:25,426
Hulk smash!

911
00:45:25,459 --> 00:45:27,294
[STUDENTS CHEERING]

912
00:45:28,996 --> 00:45:30,097
There you have it.

913
00:45:30,565 --> 00:45:31,799
[BANNER HUMMING]

914
00:45:31,832 --> 00:45:33,801
Uh, excuse me, Dr. Banner,
I, um...

915
00:45:34,468 --> 00:45:36,103
Uh...

916
00:45:36,136 --> 00:45:37,037
-You okay?
-Yeah,

917
00:45:37,071 --> 00:45:38,038
sorry, it's just a headache.

918
00:45:38,072 --> 00:45:39,073
Um, have you got a minute?

919
00:45:39,106 --> 00:45:41,543
I wanted to talk to you
about your inhibitor.

920
00:45:41,576 --> 00:45:45,547
Oh. Sure. Don't worry.
It's got fail-safes.

921
00:45:45,580 --> 00:45:46,681
I'm not gonna turn into

922
00:45:46,715 --> 00:45:50,351
the big green raging monster
machine in the cafeteria.

923
00:45:50,384 --> 00:45:53,020
But if you do see me
with this thing off, run.

924
00:45:53,053 --> 00:45:55,289
-[GROWLS]
-[BOTH LAUGHING]

925
00:45:56,423 --> 00:45:58,125
No, but you're
using target-specific

926
00:45:58,158 --> 00:45:59,860
short interfering RNA, right?

927
00:46:01,262 --> 00:46:02,229
It's like gene silencing,

928
00:46:02,263 --> 00:46:04,198
you're just incorporating
the gamma radiation?

929
00:46:06,900 --> 00:46:08,002
What'd you say your name was?

930
00:46:09,236 --> 00:46:12,406
Uh, Ned... Leeds.

931
00:46:12,439 --> 00:46:15,510
So you found a way to suppress
the expression of DNA

932
00:46:15,543 --> 00:46:17,411
even as
it's undergoing the mutation

933
00:46:17,444 --> 00:46:18,546
due to gamma radiation, right?

934
00:46:18,580 --> 00:46:21,982
-Yes.
-Okay, so my question is,

935
00:46:22,016 --> 00:46:25,152
would that same thing
be possible with DNA

936
00:46:25,185 --> 00:46:26,954
that's mutating
for another reason?

937
00:46:29,023 --> 00:46:29,890
What's the reason?

938
00:46:31,425 --> 00:46:34,028
[CHUCKLING] I don't know.
Uh... [SNIFFS]

939
00:46:34,061 --> 00:46:35,195
Let's say that the...

940
00:46:35,229 --> 00:46:38,065
the host genome is mixed with
some kind of foreign DNA.

941
00:46:38,098 --> 00:46:39,133
Theoretically.

942
00:46:40,067 --> 00:46:43,871
Theoretically?
Yes, that's possible. Yes.

943
00:46:43,904 --> 00:46:47,141
So, could you suppress only some
parts of that DNA expression?

944
00:46:47,174 --> 00:46:50,477
Like the bad aspects but just
keep all of the good stuff?

945
00:46:50,512 --> 00:46:52,446
You mean,
like, if I wanted to keep

946
00:46:52,479 --> 00:46:53,548
some parts of Hulk
but not others?

947
00:46:53,581 --> 00:46:55,249
Right.

948
00:46:55,282 --> 00:47:00,487
It would be enormously
dangerous and complex, but...

949
00:47:00,522 --> 00:47:04,358
if you were able to target
the correct mRNA strand...

950
00:47:05,259 --> 00:47:06,427
Possibly.

951
00:47:06,460 --> 00:47:08,996
Wait, so you could just turn
the mutating gene on and off

952
00:47:09,029 --> 00:47:11,465
as long as you do it
before the mRNA transcription?

953
00:47:12,166 --> 00:47:13,167
Maybe.

954
00:47:15,369 --> 00:47:18,272
I mean, if you apply the same
thinking, you could even...

955
00:47:18,305 --> 00:47:20,374
develop some kind of
automatic inhibitor

956
00:47:20,407 --> 00:47:24,411
that would just adjust
to any type of mutation.

957
00:47:24,445 --> 00:47:27,348
Well, now you're talking about
a universal inhibitor

958
00:47:27,381 --> 00:47:30,484
that would control anyone
who has any powers.

959
00:47:31,985 --> 00:47:33,153
It's a dangerous idea.

960
00:47:34,321 --> 00:47:36,323
Well, yeah.
But it's theoretical, right?

961
00:47:39,093 --> 00:47:40,494
You're not
one of my students, are ya?

962
00:47:43,097 --> 00:47:45,332
-No. I'm a grad student.
-Hmm.

963
00:47:45,366 --> 00:47:47,401
I've, uh... [CLEARS THROAT]

964
00:47:47,434 --> 00:47:48,369
I've taken enough of your time.

965
00:47:48,402 --> 00:47:51,138
I gotta get some books
back to the library.

966
00:47:51,171 --> 00:47:52,439
The library is that way.

967
00:47:54,441 --> 00:47:56,611
Right. Right. [CHUCKLES] Duh.

968
00:47:56,644 --> 00:47:58,112
How would you decide?

969
00:47:59,012 --> 00:48:01,048
What's that?

970
00:48:01,081 --> 00:48:03,685
Well, what parts of nature
are good or bad?

971
00:48:03,718 --> 00:48:05,687
What if you're trying
to control the expression

972
00:48:05,720 --> 00:48:07,921
of something that
needs to be expressed?

973
00:48:08,956 --> 00:48:10,924
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

974
00:48:13,561 --> 00:48:15,129
Good luck
with your studies, Ned.

975
00:48:17,131 --> 00:48:18,465
Thank you, Professor.

976
00:48:19,333 --> 00:48:20,267
NARRATOR: <i>Like reptiles...</i>

977
00:48:20,300 --> 00:48:23,036
-PETER: Oh, God.
<i>-...amphibians and arthropods,</i>

978
00:48:23,070 --> 00:48:24,271
<i>spiders shed skin</i>

979
00:48:24,304 --> 00:48:25,406
<i>at key points</i>

980
00:48:25,439 --> 00:48:26,039
<i>-in their life cycles.</i>
<i>-</i> [CRACKLING]

981
00:48:26,073 --> 00:48:27,241
<i>The process is known</i>

982
00:48:27,274 --> 00:48:28,409
<i>-as molting.</i>
<i>-</i> [COMPUTER TRILLS, BEEPS]

983
00:48:28,442 --> 00:48:31,211
E.V.: <i>Fourth inhibitor</i>
<i>prototype complete.</i>

984
00:48:31,245 --> 00:48:32,580
NARRATOR: <i>While molting</i>
<i>is a natural part</i>

985
00:48:32,614 --> 00:48:34,649
<i>-of a spider's life cycle...</i>
-PETER: Okay, come on. Come on.

986
00:48:34,682 --> 00:48:35,683
NARRATOR: <i>...it can</i>
<i>leave the spider</i>

987
00:48:35,717 --> 00:48:36,684
<i>vulnerable to threats.</i>

988
00:48:36,718 --> 00:48:39,219
Upload inhibitor
beta build seven.

989
00:48:39,253 --> 00:48:40,254
NARRATOR:
<i>...process is initiated by</i>

990
00:48:40,287 --> 00:48:41,054
<i>-hormonal changes...</i>
-E.V.: <i>Uploaded.</i>

991
00:48:41,088 --> 00:48:42,657
<i>Would you like to run a test?</i>

992
00:48:43,390 --> 00:48:44,458
Yeah, run it.

993
00:48:44,491 --> 00:48:45,693
NARRATOR: <i>...few hours</i>
<i>to several days.</i>

994
00:48:45,727 --> 00:48:50,197
<i>Spiders have three stages</i>
<i>in their life cycle.</i>

995
00:48:50,230 --> 00:48:53,434
<i>Each stage is characterized</i>
<i>by physical changes,</i>

996
00:48:53,467 --> 00:48:55,703
<i>with the largest changes</i>
<i>occurring during</i>

997
00:48:55,737 --> 00:48:58,640
<i>the beautiful transition</i>
<i>to adulthood.</i>

998
00:49:01,308 --> 00:49:03,177
<i>For those who make it through,</i>

999
00:49:03,210 --> 00:49:05,479
<i>molting amounts to</i>
<i>a kind of rebirth.</i>

1000
00:49:05,513 --> 00:49:07,047
Can you turn
that spider stuff off?

1001
00:49:07,080 --> 00:49:09,249
E.V.: <i>Turning off video.</i>

1002
00:49:09,283 --> 00:49:10,685
<i>-Inhibitor active.</i>
-Okay, here we go.

1003
00:49:10,718 --> 00:49:12,720
Come on. Come on. [SNIFFS]

1004
00:49:13,655 --> 00:49:15,255
Keep an eye on my vitals.

1005
00:49:16,423 --> 00:49:17,592
-[DEVICE BEEPS]
-[PETER GROANS]

1006
00:49:17,625 --> 00:49:19,259
E.V.: <i>Inhibitor engaged.</i>

1007
00:49:19,293 --> 00:49:21,295
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

1008
00:49:23,230 --> 00:49:26,701
<i>Suppressing arachnid hormones</i>
<i>to your baseline levels.</i>

1009
00:49:27,434 --> 00:49:28,736
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

1010
00:49:29,604 --> 00:49:30,605
Okay.

1011
00:49:33,440 --> 00:49:34,609
[GRUNTS]

1012
00:49:34,642 --> 00:49:36,276
All right, E.V.,
let's do this.

1013
00:49:36,310 --> 00:49:38,278
E.V.: <i>Initiating</i>
<i>field test one.</i>

1014
00:49:40,247 --> 00:49:41,583
SPIDER-MAN: That's working.
E.V.: <i>Alert.</i>

1015
00:49:41,616 --> 00:49:44,184
<i>-</i> [SUIT BEEPING RAPIDLY]
<i>-Inhibitor is overheating.</i>

1016
00:49:44,218 --> 00:49:45,385
<i>Functionality reducing.</i>

1017
00:49:45,419 --> 00:49:47,221
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah,
I'm sensing that.

1018
00:49:47,254 --> 00:49:48,523
E.V.: <i>Alert.</i>

1019
00:49:48,556 --> 00:49:49,657
<i>-Senses are overloaded.</i>
<i>-</i> [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1020
00:49:49,691 --> 00:49:50,792
E.V.: [ECHOING] <i>Alert.</i>
<i>Senses are overloaded.</i>

1021
00:49:50,825 --> 00:49:53,360
<i>-Senses are overloaded. Alert.</i>
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1022
00:49:53,393 --> 00:49:55,797
-[WEB CARTRIDGES CLINK, CLATTER]
-E.V.: <i>Web grenades activated.</i>

1023
00:49:55,830 --> 00:49:57,030
[BEEPING RAPIDLY]

1024
00:49:57,832 --> 00:49:59,534
-SPIDER-MAN: Oh, sh...
-[EXPLOSION]

1025
00:49:59,567 --> 00:50:01,669
-[PEOPLE GASPING]
-[CLATTERING]

1026
00:50:03,771 --> 00:50:06,608
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]
-[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

1027
00:50:11,411 --> 00:50:13,748
E.V.: <i>Inhibitor field test</i>
<i>one, failure.</i>

1028
00:50:13,781 --> 00:50:16,551
-[DEVICE POWERS OFF]
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1029
00:50:16,584 --> 00:50:20,153
Yo, Spider-Man, you okay?

1030
00:50:20,187 --> 00:50:22,657
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah. I'm just
trying out some new tech.

1031
00:50:22,690 --> 00:50:26,260
Oh, yeah. To get rid
of that monster inside you?

1032
00:50:26,293 --> 00:50:28,295
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

1033
00:50:31,164 --> 00:50:32,499
Still can't sense me, huh?

1034
00:50:34,234 --> 00:50:37,237
Guess your technology
isn't working.

1035
00:50:37,271 --> 00:50:39,541
You know, you're the only
person I've met that I can't...

1036
00:50:40,575 --> 00:50:42,577
hop into.

1037
00:50:42,610 --> 00:50:44,646
SPIDER-MAN: I'm sure that's
really frustrating for you.

1038
00:50:44,679 --> 00:50:46,246
Oh, I'll get in there one day.

1039
00:50:46,280 --> 00:50:47,447
SPIDER-MAN: What do you want?

1040
00:50:47,481 --> 00:50:49,249
Oh, boy.

1041
00:50:49,283 --> 00:50:52,587
I wanna know why
a half-human, half-spider

1042
00:50:52,620 --> 00:50:54,656
would decide to
work for an organization

1043
00:50:54,689 --> 00:50:58,358
whose sworn mission is to hunt
down anybody who's different.

1044
00:50:58,392 --> 00:51:00,695
SPIDER-MAN: [SCOFFS]
Damage Control isn't after you

1045
00:51:00,728 --> 00:51:02,530
because you're different.

1046
00:51:02,564 --> 00:51:04,498
They're hunting you down
because you're dangerous.

1047
00:51:04,532 --> 00:51:06,734
Now, what do you want?

1048
00:51:06,768 --> 00:51:09,436
Since you're
a very simple spider,

1049
00:51:09,469 --> 00:51:10,805
let me spell it out for you.

1050
00:51:11,906 --> 00:51:15,342
Damage Control
has something that I need.

1051
00:51:15,375 --> 00:51:16,678
SPIDER-MAN: Oh,
you mean V-Max?

1052
00:51:19,681 --> 00:51:21,381
I was planning to use Scorpion
to get it,

1053
00:51:21,415 --> 00:51:23,618
but you keep
getting in my way.

1054
00:51:23,651 --> 00:51:26,286
SPIDER-MAN: I will always
be in your way.

1055
00:51:26,320 --> 00:51:29,456
Oh, you sure about that,
Peter Parker?

1056
00:51:29,489 --> 00:51:31,491
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CRESCENDOES]

1057
00:51:33,928 --> 00:51:37,230
<i>You know, your apartment</i>
<i>is kinda like a parody</i>

1058
00:51:37,264 --> 00:51:40,835
of where you think a sad single
guy in his 20s might live.

1059
00:51:40,868 --> 00:51:45,640
Take-out containers,
free weights, protein powder.

1060
00:51:46,841 --> 00:51:49,209
[LAUGHING]

1061
00:51:50,511 --> 00:51:51,813
SPIDER-MAN: You're bluffing.

1062
00:51:51,846 --> 00:51:54,414
You know, you're not hard
to track down, Peter.

1063
00:51:54,448 --> 00:51:57,484
Well, at least
not for someone like me.

1064
00:51:58,720 --> 00:52:00,788
I did find
one interesting thing, though.

1065
00:52:02,189 --> 00:52:03,423
<i>In of all places...</i>

1066
00:52:05,593 --> 00:52:06,628
coffee cup.

1067
00:52:09,329 --> 00:52:10,898
SPIDER-MAN: E.V.,
display home work station.

1068
00:52:13,534 --> 00:52:14,702
MAN: You spent four years

1069
00:52:14,736 --> 00:52:17,872
erasing Peter Parker
from existence?

1070
00:52:17,905 --> 00:52:21,174
No wonder the spider's
trying to swallow up the man.

1071
00:52:21,208 --> 00:52:23,176
I wonder if MJ
would even recognize you.

1072
00:52:24,378 --> 00:52:26,514
-[GROANS]
-[WHOOSHES]

1073
00:52:26,547 --> 00:52:28,281
I think I might
go see how she's doing.

1074
00:52:28,315 --> 00:52:29,449
SPIDER-MAN: I'm not gonna
let that happen.

1075
00:52:29,483 --> 00:52:31,451
No, her roommate
was nice enough

1076
00:52:31,485 --> 00:52:33,621
-to post a new address online.
-[WHOOSHES]

1077
00:52:33,655 --> 00:52:36,758
How about this?
I'll race you there.

1078
00:52:36,791 --> 00:52:37,792
SPIDER-MAN: If you touch her...

1079
00:52:38,526 --> 00:52:40,227
Better start swinging.

1080
00:52:40,260 --> 00:52:41,596
I'm fast.

1081
00:52:41,629 --> 00:52:42,730
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

1082
00:52:42,764 --> 00:52:45,198
-[WHOOSHING]
-[PEOPLE GROANING]

1083
00:52:49,871 --> 00:52:51,539
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1084
00:52:51,572 --> 00:52:53,941
[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

1085
00:52:55,743 --> 00:52:58,278
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1086
00:53:02,282 --> 00:53:04,217
[YELLS, GRUNTS]

1087
00:53:04,852 --> 00:53:05,953
MAN: Hey.

1088
00:53:05,987 --> 00:53:08,255
It's a long way to MJ's.

1089
00:53:08,288 --> 00:53:10,692
-[WHOOSHES]
-You better pick up the pace.

1090
00:53:10,725 --> 00:53:13,326
-[WHOOSHING]
-[PEOPLE GROANING]

1091
00:53:17,598 --> 00:53:19,600
SPIDER-MAN: E.V.,
track physical anomalies.

1092
00:53:20,735 --> 00:53:22,302
E.V.: <i>Searching</i>
<i>for physical anomalies</i>

1093
00:53:22,335 --> 00:53:23,738
<i>-between subjects.</i>
-[COMPUTER BEEPING]

1094
00:53:23,771 --> 00:53:24,839
<i>Please stand by.</i>

1095
00:53:24,872 --> 00:53:27,575
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING, SCREAMING]

1096
00:53:28,408 --> 00:53:29,276
[SPIDER-MAN EXCLAIMS]

1097
00:53:29,309 --> 00:53:31,879
Thank you all so much
for coming today.

1098
00:53:31,913 --> 00:53:34,682
-[SHATTERING]
-[PEOPLE EXCLAIMING]

1099
00:53:34,716 --> 00:53:36,651
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1100
00:53:37,752 --> 00:53:40,320
Uh... I'm sorry about that.

1101
00:53:40,353 --> 00:53:42,355
Give it up for Spider-Man,

1102
00:53:42,389 --> 00:53:43,925
in a race
for the love of his life,

1103
00:53:43,958 --> 00:53:45,626
and it's not looking good.

1104
00:53:45,660 --> 00:53:47,762
-[WHOOSHES]
-[BRIDE GASPS]

1105
00:53:47,795 --> 00:53:49,997
Come on, Spidey. Keep up.

1106
00:53:51,065 --> 00:53:52,299
SPIDER-MAN: Excuse me. Sorry.

1107
00:53:52,332 --> 00:53:54,769
-[WHOOSHING]
-[PEOPLE GROANING]

1108
00:53:57,939 --> 00:53:59,941
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1109
00:54:00,975 --> 00:54:02,009
WOMAN: Spider-Man!

1110
00:54:02,043 --> 00:54:03,778
[TRACKER BEEPING]

1111
00:54:05,713 --> 00:54:07,582
SPIDER-MAN: E.V., run these
numbers with the others.

1112
00:54:08,950 --> 00:54:10,785
[GRUNTS]

1113
00:54:10,818 --> 00:54:13,320
E.V.: <i>Analyzing jump distances</i>
<i>for patterns.</i>

1114
00:54:13,353 --> 00:54:15,556
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1115
00:54:15,590 --> 00:54:17,357
Get me that jump data.

1116
00:54:17,390 --> 00:54:18,425
E.V.: <i>Calculating.</i>

1117
00:54:18,458 --> 00:54:19,727
[SPIDER-MAN SCREAMING]

1118
00:54:22,096 --> 00:54:23,831
Come on, I need an answer!

1119
00:54:23,865 --> 00:54:25,465
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

1120
00:54:25,499 --> 00:54:26,968
E.V.: <i>Calculations complete.</i>

1121
00:54:30,738 --> 00:54:32,907
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
-[MAN GRUNTS]

1122
00:54:42,650 --> 00:54:44,786
SPIDER-MAN: You have a limit
to your jump radius, don't ya?

1123
00:54:45,452 --> 00:54:47,487
Thirty-three feet.

1124
00:54:47,522 --> 00:54:49,724
I don't see anybody up here
for you to hop into.

1125
00:54:51,025 --> 00:54:52,660
Very clever.

1126
00:54:52,693 --> 00:54:55,830
Like I said,
you're not getting near her.

1127
00:54:56,697 --> 00:54:58,966
[HEROIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1128
00:55:06,406 --> 00:55:09,811
[UPBEAT SONG
PLAYING OVER HEADPHONES]

1129
00:55:09,844 --> 00:55:12,013
-[THUDS]
-MJ: [GASPS] Hey, hey, hey.

1130
00:55:12,046 --> 00:55:13,047
SPIDER-MAN: I'm sorry,
but you're in danger.

1131
00:55:13,080 --> 00:55:14,115
-Where's your roommate?
-What?

1132
00:55:14,148 --> 00:55:15,382
SPIDER-MAN: Where's Ned?

1133
00:55:15,415 --> 00:55:16,449
Uh, in Boston
with friends. Why?

1134
00:55:16,483 --> 00:55:17,552
SPIDER-MAN: Okay, good.
You gotta come with me.

1135
00:55:17,585 --> 00:55:19,720
What? I don't know if
you're the real Spider-Man.

1136
00:55:19,754 --> 00:55:21,388
-I'm not coming with you.
-We don't have time for this.

1137
00:55:21,421 --> 00:55:22,223
Please. Come on.

1138
00:55:22,256 --> 00:55:23,591
You need to get out
of my apartment.

1139
00:55:23,624 --> 00:55:24,959
Look, this is gonna
sound insane,

1140
00:55:24,992 --> 00:55:26,359
but there is someone
who is after you

1141
00:55:26,393 --> 00:55:27,628
who is really dangerous,
okay?

1142
00:55:27,662 --> 00:55:29,530
And I promised you
that I would keep you safe.

1143
00:55:29,564 --> 00:55:32,533
[PANTING] Please, you just
have to trust me. Come on.

1144
00:55:35,903 --> 00:55:37,004
Fine.

1145
00:55:37,038 --> 00:55:39,472
[SOMBER INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

1146
00:55:39,507 --> 00:55:42,076
-[CARS HONKING]
-[SIREN WAILING]

1147
00:55:43,711 --> 00:55:44,846
SPIDER-MAN: [SOFTLY]
Web. Stop.

1148
00:55:48,448 --> 00:55:49,449
Web. Stop.

1149
00:55:53,588 --> 00:55:54,655
Web. Stop.

1150
00:55:59,026 --> 00:56:01,662
-[GRUNTS] Are you okay?
-MJ: Yeah, yeah, I'm fine.

1151
00:56:01,696 --> 00:56:04,131
SPIDER-MAN: Okay.
Uh, we should be safe up here.

1152
00:56:04,165 --> 00:56:05,465
MJ: Okay, well, safe from what?

1153
00:56:05,498 --> 00:56:08,002
SPIDER-MAN: Uh,
I'm not entirely sure.

1154
00:56:08,035 --> 00:56:09,704
Okay, well,
what do they want with me?

1155
00:56:09,737 --> 00:56:10,972
SPIDER-MAN: [STUTTERS]
I don't know.

1156
00:56:11,005 --> 00:56:12,607
MJ: You don't know?

1157
00:56:12,640 --> 00:56:14,108
[STUTTERS]
It doesn't make any sense.

1158
00:56:14,141 --> 00:56:15,743
Why would they choose me?

1159
00:56:15,776 --> 00:56:17,945
SPIDER-MAN: Um, I wish
I could tell you. I just...

1160
00:56:17,979 --> 00:56:18,980
Uh...

1161
00:56:20,681 --> 00:56:22,116
We knew each other, didn't we?

1162
00:56:25,853 --> 00:56:26,854
SPIDER-MAN: What?

1163
00:56:27,855 --> 00:56:29,123
It's the only explanation.

1164
00:56:30,591 --> 00:56:31,726
It's been driving me crazy
for years,

1165
00:56:31,759 --> 00:56:34,996
all the times that Spider-Man
saved either me or Ned.

1166
00:56:35,029 --> 00:56:36,130
It was the Washington Monument,

1167
00:56:36,163 --> 00:56:37,698
and then it was London
and Prague

1168
00:56:37,732 --> 00:56:39,700
and the Night Monkey.

1169
00:56:39,734 --> 00:56:42,069
I mean, twice is a coincidence,
but over and over again...

1170
00:56:44,605 --> 00:56:46,173
We knew each other.
Tell me I'm wrong.

1171
00:56:48,209 --> 00:56:49,510
SPIDER-MAN: Well, you're wrong.

1172
00:56:49,543 --> 00:56:50,978
What were we?
Were we classmates

1173
00:56:51,012 --> 00:56:52,813
or friends or something?

1174
00:56:52,847 --> 00:56:53,881
SPIDER-MAN: [STUTTERS]
Look, I... I don't know

1175
00:56:53,915 --> 00:56:55,149
what you're talking about.

1176
00:56:55,182 --> 00:56:56,517
MJ: Were we something more?

1177
00:56:58,653 --> 00:57:00,988
I just, I can't...
I can't remember.

1178
00:57:01,022 --> 00:57:03,057
And I feel like
someone scrambled my brain.

1179
00:57:03,090 --> 00:57:05,660
And you're the only one
who would know why.

1180
00:57:05,693 --> 00:57:07,528
SPIDER-MAN: [EXHALES]
This is crazy. I can't...

1181
00:57:07,561 --> 00:57:09,496
MJ: I know that you can't
tell me the truth.

1182
00:57:12,266 --> 00:57:13,668
But I need to know.

1183
00:57:14,602 --> 00:57:16,671
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

1184
00:57:18,806 --> 00:57:20,808
Maybe there's a part of me
that still remembers.

1185
00:58:01,315 --> 00:58:02,516
Peter.

1186
00:58:04,552 --> 00:58:05,653
MJ.

1187
00:58:05,686 --> 00:58:06,754
MJ: Hey, Peter.

1188
00:58:09,290 --> 00:58:10,624
[PETER CRYING]

1189
00:58:12,960 --> 00:58:14,729
PETER: I've missed you
so much.

1190
00:58:19,700 --> 00:58:21,268
I can't believe
you figured it out.

1191
00:58:21,802 --> 00:58:22,837
MJ: I did.

1192
00:58:28,642 --> 00:58:31,012
Go ahead, Peter. Touch her.

1193
00:58:32,346 --> 00:58:33,781
Hold her.

1194
00:58:35,082 --> 00:58:36,684
You've been wanting to
for so long.

1195
00:58:36,717 --> 00:58:38,719
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

1196
00:58:45,359 --> 00:58:47,962
True love's kiss
breaks the spell

1197
00:58:47,995 --> 00:58:49,864
and reunites
the star-crossed lovers.

1198
00:58:52,066 --> 00:58:53,200
MJ would vomit.

1199
00:58:56,003 --> 00:58:57,705
You really are
a simple spider, aren't you?

1200
00:59:01,142 --> 00:59:02,143
I see why you like her.

1201
00:59:02,877 --> 00:59:03,911
She's, uh...

1202
00:59:05,046 --> 00:59:06,580
she's smart...

1203
00:59:07,014 --> 00:59:08,049
funny...

1204
00:59:08,949 --> 00:59:10,184
and a little dark and twisted.

1205
00:59:11,986 --> 00:59:12,987
[CHUCKLES]

1206
00:59:14,221 --> 00:59:16,357
I mean, it is sad.

1207
00:59:16,390 --> 00:59:19,693
There is, like,
no thoughts of you in here...

1208
00:59:20,995 --> 00:59:22,163
whatsoever.

1209
00:59:23,798 --> 00:59:25,066
But you knew that, didn't you?

1210
00:59:26,367 --> 00:59:28,736
You're a monster.

1211
00:59:28,769 --> 00:59:30,638
If you loved someone
the way that I love her,

1212
00:59:30,671 --> 00:59:32,173
then you'd know that
what you're doing right now

1213
00:59:32,206 --> 00:59:33,340
is unforgivable.

1214
00:59:33,374 --> 00:59:34,642
Oh, is that so?

1215
00:59:41,649 --> 00:59:42,850
You know, some people would kill

1216
00:59:42,883 --> 00:59:44,685
to hold the person they love
one last time.

1217
00:59:46,420 --> 00:59:47,922
Stop it now.

1218
00:59:50,658 --> 00:59:51,659
[GROANING]

1219
00:59:52,893 --> 00:59:54,228
[DISTORTED WARBLE]

1220
00:59:55,229 --> 00:59:56,230
Oof.

1221
00:59:57,765 --> 00:59:59,066
You're running out of time,
Peter.

1222
01:00:00,201 --> 01:00:02,203
Soon enough,
it won't just be your friends

1223
01:00:02,236 --> 01:00:03,804
who don't remember
Peter Parker.

1224
01:00:05,206 --> 01:00:06,974
Maybe you should write
a letter to yourself.

1225
01:00:07,408 --> 01:00:08,943
[GRUNTING]

1226
01:00:11,679 --> 01:00:12,713
Get out of her.

1227
01:00:14,148 --> 01:00:15,649
Who's the monster now, Peter?

1228
01:00:17,451 --> 01:00:20,321
-[PETER GRUNTS]
-[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

1229
01:00:22,857 --> 01:00:24,425
[WHOOSHES]

1230
01:00:24,458 --> 01:00:26,627
[GASPS, WHIMPERS]

1231
01:00:33,134 --> 01:00:34,768
[MJ SCREAMS]

1232
01:00:36,937 --> 01:00:38,906
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS, PANTS]

1233
01:00:38,939 --> 01:00:40,407
MJ.

1234
01:00:40,441 --> 01:00:42,943
MJ. No, no, no. Oh, God.

1235
01:00:42,977 --> 01:00:44,712
Oh, God, please, no, come on.

1236
01:00:44,745 --> 01:00:46,313
Come on, come on, come on.

1237
01:00:46,347 --> 01:00:49,016
Oh, thank God. Oh, thank God.

1238
01:00:49,049 --> 01:00:52,019
Oh, you're okay.
Oh, you're okay.

1239
01:00:52,052 --> 01:00:53,921
-Oh, I'm so sorry.
-[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

1240
01:00:55,823 --> 01:00:58,058
Stop. Wait, wait, stop, stop,
please, I'll quit.

1241
01:00:58,092 --> 01:01:00,194
You... You win, you win,
you win. Just don't hurt her.

1242
01:01:03,230 --> 01:01:04,798
You're a mess, Spider-Man.

1243
01:01:07,368 --> 01:01:09,036
Anytime I want...

1244
01:01:09,069 --> 01:01:10,337
I can be anyone I want.

1245
01:01:11,739 --> 01:01:13,340
So you can't protect MJ,

1246
01:01:14,842 --> 01:01:16,343
even from herself.

1247
01:01:16,377 --> 01:01:18,279
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

1248
01:01:23,484 --> 01:01:25,219
It really is a nice letter.

1249
01:01:26,187 --> 01:01:27,254
Little heavy-handed.

1250
01:01:27,288 --> 01:01:28,422
But not bad.

1251
01:01:33,260 --> 01:01:36,197
[CAR DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

1252
01:01:36,230 --> 01:01:38,365
[SCANNER BEEPING]

1253
01:01:42,236 --> 01:01:43,904
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1254
01:01:47,408 --> 01:01:50,077
You're okay. I'm gonna
take you someplace safe.

1255
01:01:50,110 --> 01:01:51,111
MJ: [WEAKLY] What?

1256
01:01:52,446 --> 01:01:53,847
Take me to 3165...

1257
01:01:53,881 --> 01:01:55,216
Lafayette Street.

1258
01:01:55,249 --> 01:01:57,418
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Navigating</i>
<i>to Empire State University.</i>

1259
01:02:02,456 --> 01:02:03,891
MJ: Wait, wait, wait! Okay.

1260
01:02:05,926 --> 01:02:06,661
SPIDER-MAN: I got you.
I got you.

1261
01:02:06,695 --> 01:02:07,728
MJ: Are you sure?
SPIDER-MAN: Yep.

1262
01:02:07,761 --> 01:02:09,430
Okay. 'Cause I feel like
I'm slipping a little bit.

1263
01:02:09,463 --> 01:02:10,464
-You're not slipping.
-MJ: Okay.

1264
01:02:11,432 --> 01:02:12,433
[MJ EXCLAIMS]

1265
01:02:12,466 --> 01:02:13,400
SPIDER-MAN: You're okay,
you're okay, you're okay.

1266
01:02:13,434 --> 01:02:15,369
MJ: Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I'm fine. I'm fine.

1267
01:02:18,239 --> 01:02:19,840
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
-MJ: Okay.

1268
01:02:19,873 --> 01:02:21,041
Can we just slow down

1269
01:02:21,075 --> 01:02:22,176
-for like two seconds, please?
-Well, we're almost there.

1270
01:02:22,209 --> 01:02:24,979
Yeah, yeah, but you just
told me I was mind controlled.

1271
01:02:25,012 --> 01:02:26,080
SPIDER-MAN: Well,
not technically.

1272
01:02:26,113 --> 01:02:27,181
I mean, you're lucky
I believe in that stuff, okay?

1273
01:02:27,214 --> 01:02:28,182
Because governments
have been doing it for years,

1274
01:02:28,215 --> 01:02:30,117
-especially the French.
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1275
01:02:30,150 --> 01:02:31,352
-Are you okay?
-SPIDER-MAN: Yeah...

1276
01:02:31,385 --> 01:02:32,820
Look. Sorry.
I'm just trying to take you

1277
01:02:32,853 --> 01:02:33,921
someplace safe, okay?

1278
01:02:33,954 --> 01:02:35,923
-[WEB CREAKS]
-[METAL GROANS]

1279
01:02:37,258 --> 01:02:38,359
[CLANKING]

1280
01:02:38,392 --> 01:02:39,827
I don't feel safe.

1281
01:02:39,860 --> 01:02:41,829
-[BOTH PANTING]
-[CREAKING]

1282
01:02:41,862 --> 01:02:42,863
MJ: Oh, shit.

1283
01:02:43,864 --> 01:02:44,999
[METAL GROANS]

1284
01:02:45,032 --> 01:02:46,433
[MJ SCREAMING]

1285
01:02:46,467 --> 01:02:47,434
[BOTH GRUNTING]

1286
01:02:47,468 --> 01:02:49,503
SPIDER-MAN: Sorry.
MJ: Oh, watch out! [YELPS]

1287
01:02:50,938 --> 01:02:52,873
[SPIDER-MAN STRAINING]

1288
01:02:58,513 --> 01:03:00,180
FRANK: You're losing it, kid.

1289
01:03:00,214 --> 01:03:02,883
Thought you'd be able to see
that coming a mile away.

1290
01:03:02,916 --> 01:03:03,817
SPIDER-MAN: What is wrong
with you?

1291
01:03:03,851 --> 01:03:05,520
-You could've killed us.
-FRANK: Excuse me.

1292
01:03:05,553 --> 01:03:07,154
You show up
to my house unannounced,

1293
01:03:07,187 --> 01:03:08,255
what do you think's
gonna happen?

1294
01:03:08,289 --> 01:03:09,256
MJ: Wait, this is your house?
SPIDER-MAN: No, no.

1295
01:03:09,290 --> 01:03:10,924
-Don't, don't, don't.
-Who the hell is that?

1296
01:03:10,958 --> 01:03:11,992
Who the hell are you?

1297
01:03:12,026 --> 01:03:13,528
SPIDER-MAN: [STUTTERS]
She's, um...

1298
01:03:13,561 --> 01:03:15,496
Uh, you know.

1299
01:03:15,530 --> 01:03:17,831
No, I don't know.
That's why I just asked you.

1300
01:03:17,865 --> 01:03:19,166
SPIDER-MAN:
She's in danger, Frank.

1301
01:03:19,199 --> 01:03:20,568
Look, I need your help, okay?

1302
01:03:20,602 --> 01:03:21,468
FRANK: Yeah, looks like it.

1303
01:03:21,502 --> 01:03:22,403
SPIDER-MAN: Well, come on.
You owe me.

1304
01:03:22,436 --> 01:03:24,572
Ah, for...
Aren't you sick of this story?

1305
01:03:24,606 --> 01:03:25,839
SPIDER-MAN: Staten Island!

1306
01:03:25,873 --> 01:03:27,274
Nah, Staten Island.

1307
01:03:27,308 --> 01:03:28,309
SPIDER-MAN: What more
do you want me to do?

1308
01:03:28,342 --> 01:03:29,910
I literally saved your life.

1309
01:03:29,943 --> 01:03:30,811
You're out of your mind, kid!

1310
01:03:30,844 --> 01:03:31,945
SPIDER-MAN: What,
I gotta save it twice

1311
01:03:31,979 --> 01:03:33,347
-to get a favor out of you?
-That guy couldn't hit me

1312
01:03:33,380 --> 01:03:34,448
-with a handful of rice.
-I mean,

1313
01:03:34,481 --> 01:03:35,482
what does that
sound like to you?

1314
01:03:35,517 --> 01:03:36,383
I had him exactly
where I want him.

1315
01:03:36,417 --> 01:03:37,619
A drug dealer was gonna
shoot a guy...

1316
01:03:37,652 --> 01:03:38,653
-I'm seein' him right there.
-...then I webbed the gun out of

1317
01:03:38,687 --> 01:03:39,654
-the drug dealer's hand...
-I know exactly what

1318
01:03:39,688 --> 01:03:41,989
-I'm completely up for.
-...and then kicked

1319
01:03:42,022 --> 01:03:43,057
-that drug dealer back into...
-Okay, fine, go ahead.

1320
01:03:43,090 --> 01:03:43,857
-...a storage container.
-What would you call that?

1321
01:03:43,891 --> 01:03:44,726
What does that
sound like to you?

1322
01:03:44,759 --> 01:03:46,628
I don't care.
I just wanna go home.

1323
01:03:46,661 --> 01:03:49,063
That's an excellent idea.
Kick rocks.

1324
01:03:49,096 --> 01:03:50,197
-Go home.
-SPIDER-MAN: No, no, wait, wait.

1325
01:03:50,230 --> 01:03:51,832
Frank, Frank, Frank, wait.
Please.

1326
01:03:52,966 --> 01:03:54,569
I have got to
keep her safe, okay?

1327
01:03:54,602 --> 01:03:56,470
And I don't have
anywhere else to go.

1328
01:04:00,441 --> 01:04:01,442
You like chili?

1329
01:04:02,644 --> 01:04:03,844
I made chili.

1330
01:04:05,479 --> 01:04:06,480
All right. Just...

1331
01:04:07,348 --> 01:04:08,516
watch out for the claymores.

1332
01:04:08,550 --> 01:04:11,218
Don't wanna pick up pieces
of you for the next two weeks.

1333
01:04:12,554 --> 01:04:14,622
SPIDER-MAN: Hey, I definitely
would not eat that chili.

1334
01:04:16,524 --> 01:04:18,392
FRANK: So,
you telling me that maniac

1335
01:04:18,425 --> 01:04:20,060
behind all that tank nonsense

1336
01:04:20,094 --> 01:04:21,929
is nothing but
a goddamn teenager?

1337
01:04:21,962 --> 01:04:23,063
SPIDER-MAN:
And it's not just the tank,

1338
01:04:23,097 --> 01:04:25,600
it's every attack on
Damage Control this past month.

1339
01:04:25,633 --> 01:04:27,602
And how does a kid learn
how to drive a tank?

1340
01:04:27,635 --> 01:04:28,703
SPIDER-MAN:
I don't know, Frank.

1341
01:04:28,737 --> 01:04:30,505
FRANK: Beat your ass
all over the street like that.

1342
01:04:30,538 --> 01:04:31,573
SPIDER-MAN: She did not
beat my ass.

1343
01:04:31,606 --> 01:04:32,973
-FRANK: Eh.
-[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1344
01:04:33,006 --> 01:04:34,074
This your family?

1345
01:04:37,077 --> 01:04:39,413
Would you get
the hell away from that?

1346
01:04:39,446 --> 01:04:41,649
Look, I got one rule
in this house.

1347
01:04:41,683 --> 01:04:44,519
You don't touch anything.
You don't move anything.

1348
01:04:44,552 --> 01:04:45,419
You sure as shit don't ask me

1349
01:04:45,452 --> 01:04:47,522
any goddamn questions
about anything.

1350
01:04:49,223 --> 01:04:51,158
-So, three rules?
-[FRANK GRUNTS]

1351
01:04:53,460 --> 01:04:54,962
I see why you like her.

1352
01:04:55,996 --> 01:04:57,264
I'll go put some pants on.

1353
01:04:58,700 --> 01:05:01,034
-Don't touch the chili.
-[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1354
01:05:02,102 --> 01:05:03,103
MJ: I like him.

1355
01:05:03,971 --> 01:05:05,005
SPIDER-MAN: Of course you do.

1356
01:05:06,473 --> 01:05:08,643
So I managed to pull
this image from my HUD

1357
01:05:08,676 --> 01:05:10,144
and run it through the system.

1358
01:05:10,177 --> 01:05:12,212
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

1359
01:05:13,247 --> 01:05:14,248
MJ: Who is she?

1360
01:05:14,281 --> 01:05:17,652
SPIDER-MAN: Until a couple
months ago, nobody.

1361
01:05:17,685 --> 01:05:20,354
She was in and out of
foster care, psych hospitals,

1362
01:05:20,387 --> 01:05:22,657
and then eventually she ran
away and dropped off the grid.

1363
01:05:22,690 --> 01:05:23,625
There's hardly
any information about her

1364
01:05:23,658 --> 01:05:24,958
that hasn't been scrubbed.

1365
01:05:24,992 --> 01:05:26,561
But she's classified
as a telepath.

1366
01:05:26,594 --> 01:05:28,996
And now we have a name.

1367
01:05:32,634 --> 01:05:33,635
"Jean Grey."

1368
01:05:35,603 --> 01:05:36,805
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.

1369
01:05:36,838 --> 01:05:39,406
These are the Damage Control
sites that she hasn't hit yet,

1370
01:05:39,440 --> 01:05:41,008
so if she surfaces,

1371
01:05:41,041 --> 01:05:42,943
then my facial tracking program
will pick her up.

1372
01:05:44,044 --> 01:05:45,145
Right.

1373
01:05:45,179 --> 01:05:46,480
FRANK: Oh, yeah? What then?

1374
01:05:49,016 --> 01:05:50,652
SPIDER-MAN: Well, don't worry
about "what then."

1375
01:05:50,685 --> 01:05:51,619
-Just look after her.
-[CHUCKLES]

1376
01:05:51,653 --> 01:05:53,320
Don't worry about it, huh?

1377
01:05:53,353 --> 01:05:55,322
I'm just supposed to sit here
and babysit your girlfriend?

1378
01:05:55,355 --> 01:05:56,356
I don't need to

1379
01:05:56,390 --> 01:05:57,458
-be babysat, so yeah.
-She's not my girlfriend.

1380
01:05:57,491 --> 01:05:58,660
All right, all right.
Look, what's the plan, huh?

1381
01:05:58,693 --> 01:06:03,130
Just gonna hope that your facial
tracking program works?

1382
01:06:03,163 --> 01:06:03,997
And you get yourself killed,

1383
01:06:04,031 --> 01:06:04,965
I gotta watch her
the rest of my life?

1384
01:06:04,998 --> 01:06:06,701
SPIDER-MAN: I'm not gonna
get killed, Frank.

1385
01:06:06,734 --> 01:06:07,635
I can catch her, okay?

1386
01:06:07,669 --> 01:06:08,903
I just...

1387
01:06:08,937 --> 01:06:11,773
I just have to fix my inhibitor
and then I'll be good to go.

1388
01:06:11,806 --> 01:06:13,340
Well, what do you need
to do that?

1389
01:06:13,373 --> 01:06:14,475
[SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

1390
01:06:14,509 --> 01:06:18,278
Frank. You do not have
what I need to do that, okay?

1391
01:06:19,714 --> 01:06:21,281
You know you've got
some mouth on you.

1392
01:06:21,315 --> 01:06:23,283
What do you think, you have
an anti-static mat,

1393
01:06:23,317 --> 01:06:24,985
a tonal probe,
and micro tools?

1394
01:06:25,553 --> 01:06:27,054
I got all that shit.

1395
01:06:27,522 --> 01:06:28,556
What for?

1396
01:06:28,590 --> 01:06:30,224
-Bombs.
-Bingo.

1397
01:06:31,526 --> 01:06:33,661
SPIDER-MAN: [SIGHS]
Unbelievable.

1398
01:06:34,361 --> 01:06:36,363
[SIZZLING]

1399
01:06:41,769 --> 01:06:43,638
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

1400
01:06:45,540 --> 01:06:47,742
Hey, do you think it's safe
to maybe call someone

1401
01:06:47,775 --> 01:06:49,476
and let them know I'm okay?

1402
01:06:52,079 --> 01:06:53,080
Uh...

1403
01:06:54,081 --> 01:06:55,082
Like your boyfriend?

1404
01:06:55,817 --> 01:06:58,485
Mmm, no. Like my roommate.

1405
01:06:59,152 --> 01:07:00,420
Oh, um...

1406
01:07:02,524 --> 01:07:03,825
I don't think
that's such a good idea,

1407
01:07:03,858 --> 01:07:05,058
you know, because...

1408
01:07:06,159 --> 01:07:07,595
she already knows who he is,

1409
01:07:07,629 --> 01:07:09,496
and she can inhabit anyone
she wants, so...

1410
01:07:09,531 --> 01:07:10,632
Right. Yeah.

1411
01:07:10,665 --> 01:07:12,132
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
You're right.

1412
01:07:12,165 --> 01:07:13,635
-Sorry.
-MJ: No, it's fine.

1413
01:07:13,668 --> 01:07:14,702
I totally get it.

1414
01:07:16,838 --> 01:07:19,172
If I called my boyfriend,

1415
01:07:19,206 --> 01:07:20,374
he'd just ask me
a bunch of questions

1416
01:07:20,407 --> 01:07:21,509
that I couldn't answer,

1417
01:07:21,543 --> 01:07:24,779
and then he'd tell me
I was being withholding again.

1418
01:07:24,812 --> 01:07:26,781
PETER: Withholding?
MJ: Yep.

1419
01:07:26,814 --> 01:07:28,716
Sounds like your boyfriend's
kind of a jerk.

1420
01:07:28,750 --> 01:07:30,284
[CHUCKLING]

1421
01:07:31,553 --> 01:07:32,687
But why'd he think
you're withholding?

1422
01:07:33,655 --> 01:07:35,289
I don't know. You tell me,

1423
01:07:35,322 --> 01:07:38,392
masked vigilante
behind the curtain.

1424
01:07:38,425 --> 01:07:39,727
-Um... [CHUCKLES]
-[MJ CHUCKLES]

1425
01:07:39,761 --> 01:07:41,495
Okay, I see your point.

1426
01:07:43,497 --> 01:07:45,232
So what about you?

1427
01:07:45,265 --> 01:07:47,200
PETER: What about me?

1428
01:07:47,234 --> 01:07:50,404
Well, do you have
a Mrs. Spider-Man?

1429
01:07:52,540 --> 01:07:55,075
Do I have a Mrs. Spider-Man?
Um...

1430
01:07:58,378 --> 01:07:59,847
No. No.

1431
01:08:01,148 --> 01:08:02,249
MJ: Why not?

1432
01:08:02,282 --> 01:08:03,818
Why not? Because I'm...

1433
01:08:05,620 --> 01:08:08,523
I'm too withholding, obviously.

1434
01:08:08,556 --> 01:08:10,858
-Welcome to the club.
-[PETER LAUGHS]

1435
01:08:16,631 --> 01:08:17,699
There was someone.

1436
01:08:19,166 --> 01:08:20,400
-MJ: Really?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1437
01:08:23,470 --> 01:08:24,539
What happened?

1438
01:08:25,339 --> 01:08:26,340
I, uh...

1439
01:08:27,875 --> 01:08:29,409
I had to let her go.

1440
01:08:30,678 --> 01:08:31,779
To keep her safe.

1441
01:08:31,813 --> 01:08:33,815
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

1442
01:08:36,216 --> 01:08:38,218
I'm sorry. That must have been
really hard for you.

1443
01:08:39,554 --> 01:08:41,488
Yeah, it was. Yeah. It is.

1444
01:08:42,624 --> 01:08:43,658
It is really hard.

1445
01:08:45,927 --> 01:08:47,929
-[CRACKLES]
-Oh. [BLOWS AIR]

1446
01:08:47,962 --> 01:08:49,296
Are you okay?

1447
01:08:49,329 --> 01:08:50,263
PETER: Yeah. Yeah, yeah,
I'm okay. I, uh...

1448
01:08:50,297 --> 01:08:51,431
MJ: You know what,
I'm just gonna come over.

1449
01:08:51,465 --> 01:08:53,768
PETER: Uh, hold on, hold on,
hold on, hold on, hold on.

1450
01:08:55,670 --> 01:08:56,704
-What's going on?
-SPIDER-MAN: Um...

1451
01:08:56,738 --> 01:08:59,439
It just keeps overheating on me.

1452
01:08:59,473 --> 01:09:01,809
It's been stumping me for days.

1453
01:09:01,843 --> 01:09:02,810
Before I switched to aerospace,

1454
01:09:02,844 --> 01:09:04,679
I was gonna major
in biochemical engineering,

1455
01:09:04,712 --> 01:09:07,180
so, do you mind if I...

1456
01:09:07,214 --> 01:09:08,448
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, yeah, for sure.

1457
01:09:08,482 --> 01:09:09,917
Here. There you go.

1458
01:09:11,886 --> 01:09:13,688
[SPIDER-MAN EXHALES]

1459
01:09:13,721 --> 01:09:14,722
Wow.

1460
01:09:17,759 --> 01:09:19,827
So, does the device itself...

1461
01:09:19,861 --> 01:09:21,963
I mean, does it generate
any kind of radiation

1462
01:09:21,996 --> 01:09:23,631
or a magnetic field?

1463
01:09:23,665 --> 01:09:25,298
'Cause that would
definitely interfere.

1464
01:09:25,332 --> 01:09:27,300
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, yeah,
it has a micro magnetic field,

1465
01:09:27,334 --> 01:09:29,336
but I accounted for that
in the design.

1466
01:09:29,369 --> 01:09:31,304
Okay, well,
what about your suit?

1467
01:09:31,338 --> 01:09:33,240
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, it actually
dissipates into the fabric,

1468
01:09:33,273 --> 01:09:34,609
which is pretty cool.

1469
01:09:35,576 --> 01:09:36,577
Okay.

1470
01:09:39,614 --> 01:09:40,715
What about those?

1471
01:09:41,816 --> 01:09:42,817
SPIDER-MAN: What about what?

1472
01:09:45,485 --> 01:09:47,955
Your goggles,
or whatever you call 'em.

1473
01:09:47,989 --> 01:09:49,991
SPIDER-MAN: Uh,
they would create a field.

1474
01:09:50,024 --> 01:09:51,793
It would be tiny, but...

1475
01:09:53,460 --> 01:09:54,294
But it's on your head,

1476
01:09:54,327 --> 01:09:55,429
which is very close
to the inhibitor.

1477
01:09:55,462 --> 01:09:58,231
SPIDER-MAN: Which is probably
why it's overheating.

1478
01:09:58,265 --> 01:09:59,967
Oh, MJ, that is genius.

1479
01:10:00,001 --> 01:10:01,736
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

1480
01:10:01,769 --> 01:10:03,004
Okay, this has to work.

1481
01:10:03,037 --> 01:10:05,873
[WISTFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

1482
01:10:05,907 --> 01:10:08,609
<i>-</i> [DEVICE BEEPS]
-E.V.: <i>Inhibitor engaged.</i>

1483
01:10:10,343 --> 01:10:13,881
<i>Suppressing selected</i>
<i>arachnid hormones.</i>

1484
01:10:13,915 --> 01:10:15,950
SPIDER-MAN: Okay.
That feels better.

1485
01:10:15,983 --> 01:10:17,852
That feels totally better.

1486
01:10:17,885 --> 01:10:20,688
Oh, my head feels so clear.
[SIGHS]

1487
01:10:20,722 --> 01:10:21,956
[SOFTLY] Web, web.

1488
01:10:21,989 --> 01:10:24,291
[NORMALLY] And I'm not
shooting organic webs.

1489
01:10:24,324 --> 01:10:27,528
Oh, my God, MJ,
that, like, totally worked.

1490
01:10:27,562 --> 01:10:28,896
You know, this is some
really intense stuff

1491
01:10:28,930 --> 01:10:29,997
you're working on here.

1492
01:10:30,031 --> 01:10:32,800
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

1493
01:10:32,834 --> 01:10:34,569
SPIDER-MAN: Well, yeah,
it's really important.

1494
01:10:36,938 --> 01:10:38,740
Yeah, but this is like,

1495
01:10:38,773 --> 01:10:41,843
I mean, this is like
altering your DNA.

1496
01:10:41,876 --> 01:10:43,644
I mean, this is the kind of
stuff you put on, like,

1497
01:10:43,678 --> 01:10:45,445
I don't know, like a monster.

1498
01:10:47,648 --> 01:10:49,416
SPIDER-MAN: Well, if you've seen
what's been happening to me

1499
01:10:49,449 --> 01:10:52,754
over the last couple days,
then you might understand.

1500
01:10:52,787 --> 01:10:54,354
Yeah, well, I've been with you
for the last few hours

1501
01:10:54,387 --> 01:10:56,323
and that's not what I've seen.

1502
01:10:56,356 --> 01:10:57,390
SPIDER-MAN:
And what have you seen?

1503
01:10:58,626 --> 01:10:59,594
From my side of the curtain?

1504
01:11:01,829 --> 01:11:05,365
A really good guy
who might just be changing.

1505
01:11:10,538 --> 01:11:11,639
Well, I don't mean to overstep.

1506
01:11:11,672 --> 01:11:14,307
I'll, uh,
let you get back to it.

1507
01:11:18,646 --> 01:11:21,314
-[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
-[SEAGULL SQUAWKS]

1508
01:11:29,624 --> 01:11:31,926
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

1509
01:11:35,563 --> 01:11:36,798
Can't sleep either, huh?

1510
01:11:37,632 --> 01:11:38,633
You want coffee?

1511
01:11:39,534 --> 01:11:40,568
SPIDER-MAN: Sure.

1512
01:11:41,736 --> 01:11:43,838
You get your shit fixed?

1513
01:11:43,871 --> 01:11:46,674
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah. I've been
wearing it all night.

1514
01:11:46,707 --> 01:11:47,775
So far, so good.

1515
01:11:48,709 --> 01:11:50,545
I made this other one universal.

1516
01:11:50,578 --> 01:11:52,513
So if I could get it on Jean,

1517
01:11:52,547 --> 01:11:54,982
it should completely
shut down her powers.

1518
01:11:55,016 --> 01:11:57,618
FRANK: Hmm.
You know what else would work?

1519
01:11:57,652 --> 01:11:58,953
You just shoot her.

1520
01:11:58,986 --> 01:12:00,087
SPIDER-MAN: Nice.

1521
01:12:00,855 --> 01:12:02,857
[CHUCKLES]

1522
01:12:02,890 --> 01:12:04,759
Jesus Christ.

1523
01:12:04,792 --> 01:12:06,794
[LAUGHS] That has gotta be
the goofiest shit

1524
01:12:06,828 --> 01:12:07,662
I ever seen in my life.

1525
01:12:07,695 --> 01:12:09,864
What, you can't even
take the mask off

1526
01:12:09,897 --> 01:12:10,932
to drink a cup of coffee?

1527
01:12:10,965 --> 01:12:12,133
[SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

1528
01:12:12,166 --> 01:12:15,102
Don't take it personally, Frank.
It stays on for everybody.

1529
01:12:16,137 --> 01:12:17,370
Even her?

1530
01:12:19,740 --> 01:12:20,875
Who is she, kid?

1531
01:12:20,908 --> 01:12:21,943
SPIDER-MAN: I don't know.

1532
01:12:21,976 --> 01:12:24,045
Eh! That's horseshit.
Who is she?

1533
01:12:24,078 --> 01:12:25,412
I'm telling you,
I don't know who she is.

1534
01:12:25,445 --> 01:12:26,581
What are you doin'?
You care about her.

1535
01:12:26,614 --> 01:12:27,515
-You're pretending not to. Why?
-I don't care about her.

1536
01:12:27,548 --> 01:12:29,784
Look, I don't know
who she is, Frank. Okay?

1537
01:12:29,817 --> 01:12:31,152
I don't have anybody.
I'm like you.

1538
01:12:31,185 --> 01:12:32,653
I just keep to myself.

1539
01:12:32,687 --> 01:12:33,721
You're like me?

1540
01:12:34,989 --> 01:12:36,456
What do you know
about me, kid?

1541
01:12:37,457 --> 01:12:38,693
You think this is a choice?

1542
01:12:38,726 --> 01:12:40,161
Living like this,
it's a lifestyle?

1543
01:12:40,194 --> 01:12:41,428
Is that what you think?

1544
01:12:41,963 --> 01:12:43,564
Kid, this is a sentence.

1545
01:12:44,699 --> 01:12:45,700
You know somethin'...

1546
01:12:46,534 --> 01:12:48,803
If I had one second,

1547
01:12:48,836 --> 01:12:50,137
people I love
were still breathing,

1548
01:12:50,171 --> 01:12:52,640
you think I'd be hiding
behind a mask?

1549
01:12:52,673 --> 01:12:54,842
You think I'd pretend
to be something that I'm not,

1550
01:12:54,876 --> 01:12:56,677
acting like a goddamn coward?

1551
01:12:57,812 --> 01:12:59,547
[ALERT CHIRPING ON COMPUTER]

1552
01:13:02,183 --> 01:13:03,150
SPIDER-MAN:
I got a facial match.

1553
01:13:03,184 --> 01:13:04,051
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

1554
01:13:07,788 --> 01:13:09,991
She's at the Damage Control HQ
in Manhattan.

1555
01:13:10,024 --> 01:13:11,391
I gotta go. Okay.

1556
01:13:15,796 --> 01:13:17,832
She's gonna be okay.

1557
01:13:17,865 --> 01:13:18,966
I'll see to it.

1558
01:13:22,003 --> 01:13:23,104
SPIDER-MAN: Thanks, Frank.

1559
01:13:25,640 --> 01:13:26,874
[FRANK SIGHS]

1560
01:13:27,775 --> 01:13:28,809
[DOOR CREAKS]

1561
01:13:29,911 --> 01:13:30,912
Hey.

1562
01:13:31,579 --> 01:13:32,380
FRANK: Hey.

1563
01:13:34,115 --> 01:13:35,783
You just gonna let him
go by himself?

1564
01:13:37,184 --> 01:13:38,686
You know,
I think he might need you.

1565
01:13:39,086 --> 01:13:40,521
Eh.

1566
01:13:41,622 --> 01:13:43,157
Kinda like you needed him
on Staten Island.

1567
01:13:47,128 --> 01:13:48,428
[SOFTLY] Yeah.

1568
01:13:49,664 --> 01:13:51,666
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1569
01:13:56,704 --> 01:13:58,438
[THUDDING]

1570
01:14:06,013 --> 01:14:07,949
-[SYSTEM TRILLING]
-[THUDDING CONTINUES]

1571
01:14:14,588 --> 01:14:16,724
-[THUDDING]
-[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

1572
01:14:18,192 --> 01:14:20,061
[THUDDING]

1573
01:14:21,796 --> 01:14:22,997
[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

1574
01:14:23,030 --> 01:14:24,231
[RADIO CHIRPS]

1575
01:14:24,265 --> 01:14:25,666
[THUDDING]

1576
01:14:25,700 --> 01:14:28,202
You can't hide from me
forever, Bill.

1577
01:14:28,235 --> 01:14:29,804
[OVER RADIO]
<i>You've got a strong door,</i>

1578
01:14:29,837 --> 01:14:31,639
<i>but it's the wall</i>
<i>you have to worry about.</i>

1579
01:14:32,640 --> 01:14:34,508
Who are you
and what do you want?

1580
01:14:34,542 --> 01:14:36,177
[THUDDING CONTINUES]

1581
01:14:39,246 --> 01:14:40,648
I'm Jean Grey...

1582
01:14:41,716 --> 01:14:43,184
and you know what I want.

1583
01:14:49,290 --> 01:14:50,992
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1584
01:14:51,025 --> 01:14:52,660
[DISTANT THUDDING]

1585
01:14:57,999 --> 01:15:00,034
[MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

1586
01:15:00,067 --> 01:15:02,670
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

1587
01:15:04,572 --> 01:15:06,140
[DISTANT THUDDING CONTINUES]

1588
01:15:18,285 --> 01:15:20,221
[THUDDING INTENSIFIES]

1589
01:15:23,124 --> 01:15:24,558
[THUDDING STOPS]

1590
01:15:29,663 --> 01:15:31,999
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

1591
01:15:43,944 --> 01:15:45,746
SPIDER-MAN: Jean?

1592
01:15:45,780 --> 01:15:49,683
You looked me up?
I'm blushing.

1593
01:15:49,717 --> 01:15:52,953
I told you what would happen to
your girl if you got in my way.

1594
01:15:52,987 --> 01:15:55,122
SPIDER-MAN: You're not getting
near her again.

1595
01:15:55,156 --> 01:15:57,224
And you're definitely
not getting inside that vault.

1596
01:15:57,858 --> 01:15:59,026
Hmm, maybe not.

1597
01:15:59,060 --> 01:16:00,628
[DEVICE CRACKLING]

1598
01:16:03,798 --> 01:16:05,032
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1599
01:16:06,233 --> 01:16:07,635
But this guy might.

1600
01:16:10,337 --> 01:16:13,107
SPIDER-MAN: Jean, you don't know
what you're dealing with.

1601
01:16:13,140 --> 01:16:15,976
You know, you and Banner
have a lot in common.

1602
01:16:16,010 --> 01:16:17,878
Both fighting a losing battle

1603
01:16:17,912 --> 01:16:20,648
against the monster
that lives inside you.

1604
01:16:20,681 --> 01:16:22,616
SPIDER-MAN: Jean, this is
the Hulk, you can't just...

1605
01:16:22,650 --> 01:16:24,752
-[HULK GRUNTING]
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1606
01:16:27,221 --> 01:16:29,356
-[HULK GRUNTS]
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1607
01:16:31,058 --> 01:16:33,360
-HULK: What the hell?
-[GRUNTS]

1608
01:16:33,394 --> 01:16:35,396
Oh, I see.

1609
01:16:35,429 --> 01:16:37,264
-[GRUNTS]
-[SPIDER-MAN GASPS]

1610
01:16:37,298 --> 01:16:40,835
Trying to muzzle me
like you muzzle yourself?

1611
01:16:40,868 --> 01:16:42,303
SPIDER-MAN:
I can't let you in there.

1612
01:16:42,336 --> 01:16:44,972
Whatever V-Max is,
you're not getting it.

1613
01:16:45,005 --> 01:16:46,407
Like hell I'm not.

1614
01:16:46,440 --> 01:16:47,942
-[ROARS]
-SPIDER-MAN: Oh, crap.

1615
01:16:47,975 --> 01:16:49,643
-[HULK GRUNTS]
-[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1616
01:16:52,179 --> 01:16:53,380
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
-[HULK GROANS]

1617
01:16:53,414 --> 01:16:55,683
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
-[WINCES]

1618
01:16:56,417 --> 01:16:57,785
[GROANS]

1619
01:16:59,053 --> 01:17:00,154
[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1620
01:17:00,187 --> 01:17:02,756
Jean, don't do this.

1621
01:17:02,790 --> 01:17:04,191
-Save your breath.
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1622
01:17:04,225 --> 01:17:05,392
[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1623
01:17:05,426 --> 01:17:07,695
-[HULK GRUNTING]
-[GROANING]

1624
01:17:07,728 --> 01:17:09,396
[CLANGING]

1625
01:17:09,430 --> 01:17:11,098
[SPIDER-MAN GASPS]

1626
01:17:11,132 --> 01:17:12,933
-[GUN FIRING]
-[GROANING]

1627
01:17:13,934 --> 01:17:16,003
[FRANK ROARING]

1628
01:17:24,111 --> 01:17:25,379
[GUN CLICKS]

1629
01:17:29,150 --> 01:17:31,051
SPIDER-MAN: Frank,
what are you doing here?

1630
01:17:31,085 --> 01:17:32,786
What you think I'm doing?
I'm saving your ass.

1631
01:17:32,820 --> 01:17:34,889
SPIDER-MAN: This is way above
your pay grade, dude.

1632
01:17:34,922 --> 01:17:36,223
-We're fighting the Hulk.
-Oh, shit!

1633
01:17:36,257 --> 01:17:37,124
[GRUNTS]

1634
01:17:37,858 --> 01:17:39,426
[FRANK GROANS]

1635
01:17:39,460 --> 01:17:41,428
[GRUNTS]

1636
01:17:41,462 --> 01:17:42,963
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1637
01:17:42,997 --> 01:17:44,031
[FRANK GRUNTS]

1638
01:17:45,199 --> 01:17:47,201
[HULK ROARING]

1639
01:17:55,075 --> 01:17:55,943
[BEEPS]

1640
01:17:57,411 --> 01:17:58,345
[GRUNTS]

1641
01:17:58,979 --> 01:17:59,980
Really?

1642
01:18:01,348 --> 01:18:02,383
[GROANS]

1643
01:18:02,416 --> 01:18:04,385
-[WHOOSHES]
-[GASPS, PANTS]

1644
01:18:05,486 --> 01:18:07,354
[GROANS]

1645
01:18:09,423 --> 01:18:10,824
[WHOOSHING]

1646
01:18:10,858 --> 01:18:13,260
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
-[GROANING] Get out!

1647
01:18:13,294 --> 01:18:15,896
-[WHOOSHES]
-[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1648
01:18:18,199 --> 01:18:19,466
[GUN FIRING]

1649
01:18:19,500 --> 01:18:20,868
SPIDER-MAN: Stop shooting him!

1650
01:18:20,901 --> 01:18:22,136
Are you out of your
goddamn mind?

1651
01:18:22,169 --> 01:18:23,470
SPIDER-MAN: He's...
Banner's not the problem!

1652
01:18:23,504 --> 01:18:24,371
She is.

1653
01:18:27,107 --> 01:18:29,043
[INAUDIBLE CONVERSATION]

1654
01:18:34,114 --> 01:18:35,716
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1655
01:18:36,383 --> 01:18:38,085
[BANNER GROANING]

1656
01:18:38,118 --> 01:18:39,920
SPIDER-MAN: I thought I told you
to stay home and watch MJ.

1657
01:18:39,954 --> 01:18:40,955
FRANK: Yeah, you did.

1658
01:18:40,988 --> 01:18:43,057
And then she tells me
I gotta come watch you.

1659
01:18:43,090 --> 01:18:44,225
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1660
01:18:44,258 --> 01:18:45,926
Wait, did she actually
say that to you?

1661
01:18:45,960 --> 01:18:48,095
-[OBJECTS CLATTERING]
-Are you blushing, daffodil?

1662
01:18:48,996 --> 01:18:50,130
SPIDER-MAN: I'm not blushing.

1663
01:18:50,164 --> 01:18:52,032
-[THUDDING]
-[SPIDER-MAN GASPS]

1664
01:18:52,066 --> 01:18:54,868
Goddamn it. I knew I should
have brought a bigger gun.

1665
01:18:54,902 --> 01:18:56,103
SPIDER-MAN: That's a good idea,
"Bring a bigger gun."

1666
01:18:56,136 --> 01:18:57,304
What are you gonna do,
tickle him to death?

1667
01:18:57,338 --> 01:18:58,472
No. Look, change of plan.

1668
01:18:58,506 --> 01:19:01,475
First, we get this on the Hulk,
then we go after Jean.

1669
01:19:01,509 --> 01:19:02,476
FRANK: I got one better.

1670
01:19:02,510 --> 01:19:04,845
That's the highest
casualty-producing threat.

1671
01:19:04,878 --> 01:19:06,514
You contain it.
I go find the source.

1672
01:19:06,548 --> 01:19:08,516
I take it down. You got it?

1673
01:19:08,550 --> 01:19:10,451
SPIDER-MAN: Are you just trying
to get out of fighting the Hulk?

1674
01:19:12,152 --> 01:19:13,187
-I guess so.
-SPIDER-MAN: Okay,

1675
01:19:13,220 --> 01:19:15,256
whatever, dude.
I got this.

1676
01:19:15,289 --> 01:19:17,091
-Wait, no, Frank, Frank, Frank.
-What?

1677
01:19:17,124 --> 01:19:18,359
SPIDER-MAN: Do not kill her!

1678
01:19:18,392 --> 01:19:20,562
Don't start with that
soft serve bullshit.

1679
01:19:20,595 --> 01:19:21,563
You know something?
I'm gonna do this,

1680
01:19:21,596 --> 01:19:22,496
I'm gonna do it my way.

1681
01:19:22,530 --> 01:19:25,065
Just... just go, just go.

1682
01:19:25,099 --> 01:19:26,367
SPIDER-MAN: And don't get
within 33 feet!

1683
01:19:26,400 --> 01:19:27,301
FRANK: Eh...

1684
01:19:27,334 --> 01:19:28,536
SPIDER-MAN: So frustrating.

1685
01:19:33,107 --> 01:19:35,109
[LIQUID BUBBLING]

1686
01:19:43,518 --> 01:19:44,552
JEAN: Hey.

1687
01:19:44,586 --> 01:19:46,186
-[WHOOSHES]
-[GRUNTS]

1688
01:19:46,220 --> 01:19:48,222
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

1689
01:19:49,123 --> 01:19:50,391
Whoa!

1690
01:19:50,424 --> 01:19:52,560
This guy's got issues.

1691
01:19:54,061 --> 01:19:57,031
BANNER: No. Oh, no.

1692
01:19:57,064 --> 01:20:00,434
No, not again. Oh, no.

1693
01:20:00,467 --> 01:20:03,137
SPIDER-MAN: Dr. Banner?
Is that you?

1694
01:20:03,170 --> 01:20:06,273
[BREATHING HEAVILY]
Spider-Man. What happened?

1695
01:20:06,307 --> 01:20:07,341
Where am I?

1696
01:20:07,374 --> 01:20:09,310
-SPIDER-MAN: Hey, hey, hey.
-Did I do all this?

1697
01:20:09,343 --> 01:20:10,911
-SPIDER-MAN: You...
-Did I hurt anyone?

1698
01:20:10,944 --> 01:20:12,446
SPIDER-MAN: It's not your fault.
She was in your mind.

1699
01:20:12,479 --> 01:20:13,581
You weren't in control.

1700
01:20:13,615 --> 01:20:15,416
-I lost my inhibitor.
-SPIDER-MAN: Look here, here.

1701
01:20:15,449 --> 01:20:17,885
BANNER: It's the only thing
keeping the monster inside.

1702
01:20:17,918 --> 01:20:18,687
SPIDER-MAN: It's okay.
I got another one here.

1703
01:20:18,720 --> 01:20:19,621
I just need you
to put this on.

1704
01:20:19,654 --> 01:20:21,455
-What is it?
-SPIDER-MAN: It's universal.

1705
01:20:21,488 --> 01:20:22,923
It should work on you.

1706
01:20:28,195 --> 01:20:29,229
FRANK: Hmm.

1707
01:20:32,232 --> 01:20:33,867
SPIDER-MAN: Please, sir,
there's people in the building.

1708
01:20:33,901 --> 01:20:34,569
Just put it on.

1709
01:20:37,371 --> 01:20:39,473
-[GROANS]
-SPIDER-MAN: You okay?

1710
01:20:39,507 --> 01:20:42,943
My head.
I think she broke something!

1711
01:20:42,976 --> 01:20:44,178
SPIDER-MAN:
Is she still in there?

1712
01:20:44,211 --> 01:20:45,446
BANNER: No.

1713
01:20:45,479 --> 01:20:46,648
It's the other guy.

1714
01:20:46,681 --> 01:20:48,415
SPIDER-MAN: Bruce?

1715
01:20:48,449 --> 01:20:49,983
Look, I can get you
out of here, okay?

1716
01:20:50,017 --> 01:20:51,418
I just need you to put
that inhibitor on.

1717
01:20:51,452 --> 01:20:52,587
-Get away from me!
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1718
01:20:54,455 --> 01:20:55,923
BANNER: He's coming.

1719
01:20:56,457 --> 01:20:58,459
I can't control.

1720
01:20:58,492 --> 01:21:00,394
SPIDER-MAN: Yes, you can,
Bruce! Yes, you can!

1721
01:21:00,427 --> 01:21:02,062
Get out of the building!

1722
01:21:02,096 --> 01:21:03,997
Get out of the building!

1723
01:21:04,031 --> 01:21:06,601
[VOICE GROWS DEEPER] Get
everyone out of the... [GROANS]

1724
01:21:06,634 --> 01:21:09,269
[ROARING]

1725
01:21:09,303 --> 01:21:11,205
No! No!

1726
01:21:11,238 --> 01:21:13,006
SPIDER-MAN: Banner, please.
Look at me.

1727
01:21:13,040 --> 01:21:15,476
[HULK ROARING]

1728
01:21:15,510 --> 01:21:18,379
[HOARSELY] No Banner.
No girl.

1729
01:21:19,647 --> 01:21:21,482
Only Hulk.

1730
01:21:21,516 --> 01:21:23,384
[HULK GROWLING]

1731
01:21:25,085 --> 01:21:26,487
[GROWLS]

1732
01:21:27,622 --> 01:21:29,089
[SNARLS]

1733
01:21:31,325 --> 01:21:33,127
SPIDER-MAN: I didn't know
you could get that big.

1734
01:21:33,160 --> 01:21:35,162
[GROWLING]

1735
01:21:37,231 --> 01:21:39,133
FRANK: Whoa!

1736
01:21:39,166 --> 01:21:40,401
Good luck with that, Peter.

1737
01:21:42,403 --> 01:21:44,905
-[HULK GRUNTING]
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1738
01:21:48,676 --> 01:21:50,512
-[HULK SNARLS]
-SPIDER-MAN: There you are.

1739
01:21:52,246 --> 01:21:53,113
Just hold still.
Just hold still...

1740
01:21:53,147 --> 01:21:55,349
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]
-[HULK ROARING]

1741
01:21:56,718 --> 01:21:57,918
SPIDER-MAN: Stay!

1742
01:22:03,490 --> 01:22:05,292
[ROARS]

1743
01:22:06,594 --> 01:22:08,128
SPIDER-MAN: [PANTS] Oh, God.

1744
01:22:09,396 --> 01:22:11,599
[SCREAMS, GROANS]

1745
01:22:12,332 --> 01:22:14,067
[GROANS, PANTS]

1746
01:22:14,101 --> 01:22:16,270
[FRANK WHISTLING]

1747
01:22:16,303 --> 01:22:17,572
[BOMB BEEPS, ARMS]

1748
01:22:19,440 --> 01:22:21,108
[BOMB BEEPS, ARMS]

1749
01:22:21,141 --> 01:22:22,710
[GUN COCKING]

1750
01:22:22,744 --> 01:22:23,977
No lethal rounds.

1751
01:22:24,011 --> 01:22:26,013
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1752
01:22:30,685 --> 01:22:32,554
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1753
01:22:36,758 --> 01:22:39,026
E.V.: <i>Tracking time</i>
<i>to detonation.</i>

1754
01:22:39,059 --> 01:22:40,227
[HULK ROARING]

1755
01:22:40,260 --> 01:22:41,563
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1756
01:22:42,530 --> 01:22:43,698
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1757
01:22:46,233 --> 01:22:48,969
[SPIDER-MAN SCREAMING]

1758
01:22:49,737 --> 01:22:52,372
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING, GROANING]

1759
01:22:58,613 --> 01:22:59,647
[GRUNTS]

1760
01:23:07,522 --> 01:23:09,423
E.V.: <i>Ninety seconds</i>
<i>to detonation.</i>

1761
01:23:09,456 --> 01:23:11,559
SPIDER-MAN: I know! I know!
[GRUNTING]

1762
01:23:11,593 --> 01:23:12,660
[SNARLING]

1763
01:23:14,094 --> 01:23:16,129
[BOTH GRUNTING]

1764
01:23:16,163 --> 01:23:17,498
SPIDER-MAN: Come on. Come on.

1765
01:23:17,532 --> 01:23:19,199
Why is your skin so thick?

1766
01:23:19,233 --> 01:23:20,400
E.V.: <i>Inhibitor cannot attach.</i>

1767
01:23:20,434 --> 01:23:22,069
-SPIDER-MAN: Oh, come on!
-[SNARLS]

1768
01:23:27,642 --> 01:23:28,643
[HULK ROARING]

1769
01:23:32,814 --> 01:23:34,081
[GRUNTS]

1770
01:23:37,652 --> 01:23:38,653
[GRUNTING]

1771
01:23:42,824 --> 01:23:44,491
[GAUNTLET POWERING UP]

1772
01:23:44,526 --> 01:23:47,094
-[MUSIC CRESCENDOES]
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1773
01:23:47,562 --> 01:23:49,162
[GRUNTS]

1774
01:23:54,636 --> 01:23:56,704
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1775
01:23:59,674 --> 01:24:01,441
SPIDER-MAN: [GROANING]
Dr. Banner...

1776
01:24:02,744 --> 01:24:04,077
please.

1777
01:24:04,111 --> 01:24:05,379
[GROANING]

1778
01:24:05,412 --> 01:24:06,446
Bruce.

1779
01:24:06,480 --> 01:24:07,649
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1780
01:24:07,682 --> 01:24:09,651
-SPIDER-MAN: It's Peter.
-[GROWLS]

1781
01:24:10,450 --> 01:24:12,185
I'm your friend.

1782
01:24:14,288 --> 01:24:15,422
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

1783
01:24:23,765 --> 01:24:25,432
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

1784
01:24:29,537 --> 01:24:30,672
[GROANING]

1785
01:24:35,409 --> 01:24:37,444
[SPIDER-MAN COUGHING]

1786
01:24:41,448 --> 01:24:42,449
Bruce.

1787
01:24:45,218 --> 01:24:47,421
-[PANTING]
-[CRASHING]

1788
01:24:47,454 --> 01:24:48,690
[TIMER BEEPING]

1789
01:24:50,223 --> 01:24:51,793
[DISTANT EXPLOSION]

1790
01:24:53,695 --> 01:24:54,729
[GUNSHOTS]

1791
01:24:54,762 --> 01:24:56,463
[GUARDS GROANING]

1792
01:25:01,536 --> 01:25:02,670
Throw down your guns,

1793
01:25:02,704 --> 01:25:04,371
or you'll get the next one
in the head.

1794
01:25:15,617 --> 01:25:17,184
Where is she?

1795
01:25:22,389 --> 01:25:23,524
[FRANK GRUNTS]

1796
01:25:26,259 --> 01:25:27,895
[INHIBITOR BEEPS, TRILLING]

1797
01:25:27,929 --> 01:25:29,831
-[WHOOSHES]
-[GROANS]

1798
01:25:30,531 --> 01:25:31,566
What did you...

1799
01:25:31,599 --> 01:25:32,767
SPIDER-MAN: It's over, Jean.

1800
01:25:33,568 --> 01:25:35,369
-[GUN FIRES]
-[GRUNTS]

1801
01:25:40,340 --> 01:25:42,376
[JEAN GRUNTING, GASPING]

1802
01:25:48,248 --> 01:25:49,249
Sara.

1803
01:26:00,494 --> 01:26:02,764
Is that my gun?

1804
01:26:02,797 --> 01:26:05,933
-[SIREN WAILING IN DISTANCE]
-[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

1805
01:26:10,605 --> 01:26:13,373
Is anyone hurt? It's just me?

1806
01:26:14,341 --> 01:26:15,510
Is anyone hurt?

1807
01:26:17,011 --> 01:26:18,211
METZGER: Spider-Man...

1808
01:26:20,815 --> 01:26:22,784
You saved my life.

1809
01:26:22,817 --> 01:26:24,519
And you saved
God knows how many lives

1810
01:26:24,552 --> 01:26:25,586
by making sure she didn't find

1811
01:26:25,620 --> 01:26:27,320
what she was looking for
in there.

1812
01:26:27,354 --> 01:26:28,623
EMT: Still inside.
We got her coming through.

1813
01:26:29,724 --> 01:26:30,625
SPIDER-MAN:
Before she passed out,

1814
01:26:30,658 --> 01:26:32,694
she tried to say something.

1815
01:26:32,727 --> 01:26:35,462
A name, Sara. Does that
mean something to you?

1816
01:26:36,731 --> 01:26:39,567
Before you got
the inhibitor on her,

1817
01:26:39,600 --> 01:26:41,602
she managed to get in my mind
for a moment.

1818
01:26:43,037 --> 01:26:44,539
Sara was the name of someone

1819
01:26:44,572 --> 01:26:47,274
I worked closely with
that recently passed.

1820
01:26:47,307 --> 01:26:48,375
SPIDER-MAN: I'm sorry
to hear that.

1821
01:26:49,777 --> 01:26:53,614
Somehow the memory of Sara
must have affected her.

1822
01:26:56,617 --> 01:26:58,452
SPIDER-MAN: Well, I'd love to
talk to her when she wakes up,

1823
01:26:58,485 --> 01:26:59,520
if that's all right.

1824
01:26:59,554 --> 01:27:01,288
Of course. She'll be transferred

1825
01:27:01,321 --> 01:27:03,558
to our facility
on Roosevelt Island.

1826
01:27:03,591 --> 01:27:05,893
Now, I'm just as eager
to get her talking as you are,

1827
01:27:05,927 --> 01:27:08,529
but let's not strain her
too much in one day.

1828
01:27:08,563 --> 01:27:10,397
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, of course.

1829
01:27:10,430 --> 01:27:11,733
METZGER: Thank you, Spider-Man.

1830
01:27:11,766 --> 01:27:12,767
SPIDER-MAN: My pleasure.

1831
01:27:13,868 --> 01:27:15,870
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

1832
01:27:24,712 --> 01:27:25,747
SPIDER-MAN: MJ!

1833
01:27:25,780 --> 01:27:28,049
It worked. She's in custody.

1834
01:27:28,082 --> 01:27:29,416
You're safe now.

1835
01:27:32,520 --> 01:27:33,521
You left this.

1836
01:27:41,763 --> 01:27:42,964
Did you want me to find it?

1837
01:27:45,066 --> 01:27:47,535
SPIDER-MAN: No. No. Um...

1838
01:27:48,335 --> 01:27:49,369
Look, I can explain, I...

1839
01:27:49,402 --> 01:27:50,738
Can you take that off, please?

1840
01:27:52,640 --> 01:27:53,641
SPIDER-MAN: What?

1841
01:27:54,675 --> 01:27:55,676
The mask.

1842
01:27:57,745 --> 01:27:59,547
I think I deserve to
have this conversation

1843
01:27:59,580 --> 01:28:02,415
with "Peter Parker."

1844
01:28:10,691 --> 01:28:11,692
[SIGHS]

1845
01:28:28,408 --> 01:28:30,310
You came to the party at our
apartment the other night.

1846
01:28:36,751 --> 01:28:38,786
And the donut shop. [SCOFFS]

1847
01:28:40,087 --> 01:28:41,556
The year I went off to school.

1848
01:28:44,457 --> 01:28:46,127
Why didn't you tell me then?

1849
01:28:46,160 --> 01:28:48,428
I was trying to protect you.

1850
01:28:48,461 --> 01:28:49,530
Yeah, well,
I've almost been killed,

1851
01:28:49,564 --> 01:28:51,364
like, five times
in the past 24 hours,

1852
01:28:51,398 --> 01:28:53,701
so it's not really
working that well.

1853
01:28:53,734 --> 01:28:55,002
PETER: I know.
I'm sorry. I...

1854
01:28:56,537 --> 01:28:57,772
Were you ever gonna tell me?

1855
01:29:04,712 --> 01:29:05,713
Right.

1856
01:29:07,114 --> 01:29:09,650
So you just were gonna
make that decision for me.

1857
01:29:10,450 --> 01:29:11,619
I know. I'm sorry.

1858
01:29:11,652 --> 01:29:13,554
I don't really need you to
keep saying that you're sorry.

1859
01:29:13,588 --> 01:29:14,655
I don't know
what you want me to tell you.

1860
01:29:14,689 --> 01:29:16,724
I want you to tell me
why you would do this to me.

1861
01:29:22,830 --> 01:29:24,031
I lost someone.

1862
01:29:28,002 --> 01:29:30,104
And they'd still be here
if it wasn't for me.

1863
01:29:34,942 --> 01:29:36,644
I didn't read you
that letter because...

1864
01:29:37,879 --> 01:29:40,181
I didn't want anything like that
to happen to you.

1865
01:29:40,214 --> 01:29:41,616
But that's not really
your decision to make.

1866
01:29:41,649 --> 01:29:42,884
PETER: I know it's not,
but...

1867
01:29:45,186 --> 01:29:46,654
You mean everything to me.

1868
01:29:49,857 --> 01:29:52,392
And I've been trying to live
my life without you, but I...

1869
01:29:54,095 --> 01:29:55,096
I can't.

1870
01:30:01,468 --> 01:30:02,469
I love you.

1871
01:30:09,610 --> 01:30:10,845
[MJ SIGHS]

1872
01:30:14,548 --> 01:30:17,618
This spell or whatever it is
that you did...

1873
01:30:21,155 --> 01:30:21,956
It worked.

1874
01:30:25,126 --> 01:30:26,794
All these memories
that you're saying

1875
01:30:26,827 --> 01:30:28,529
that we have together,
I don't...

1876
01:30:30,731 --> 01:30:31,832
I don't have them.

1877
01:30:35,670 --> 01:30:37,838
And I do see why, you know,
she would love you,

1878
01:30:37,872 --> 01:30:40,641
the girl you wrote
that letter to, but...

1879
01:30:45,246 --> 01:30:47,515
I understand...

1880
01:30:47,548 --> 01:30:50,483
that you did what
you had to do to protect her.

1881
01:30:52,720 --> 01:30:55,488
And for that I'm so grateful.

1882
01:30:58,893 --> 01:30:59,894
But I...

1883
01:31:03,931 --> 01:31:05,166
I don't love you.

1884
01:31:09,670 --> 01:31:11,138
Because I don't...

1885
01:31:11,172 --> 01:31:12,840
I don't even know you.

1886
01:31:21,615 --> 01:31:23,918
I should probably go now.

1887
01:31:30,257 --> 01:31:31,859
I really am sorry, Peter.

1888
01:31:50,144 --> 01:31:51,512
I don't have a phone.

1889
01:31:52,213 --> 01:31:53,214
Um...

1890
01:31:54,682 --> 01:31:55,950
Do you mind taking me home?

1891
01:31:58,819 --> 01:31:59,920
Yeah, of course.

1892
01:31:59,954 --> 01:32:00,955
Thank you.

1893
01:32:02,857 --> 01:32:04,859
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1894
01:32:40,761 --> 01:32:41,896
[MJ GRUNTS]

1895
01:32:43,064 --> 01:32:45,366
-[SIGHS] Thank you.
-SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, sure.

1896
01:32:45,399 --> 01:32:47,835
Um, I'm going to, uh...

1897
01:32:47,868 --> 01:32:49,270
Uh, yeah, yeah. Yeah, of course.

1898
01:32:52,273 --> 01:32:53,808
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1899
01:32:58,879 --> 01:32:59,947
Do you wanna come up?

1900
01:33:02,083 --> 01:33:04,285
Just to say hi to Ned. Maybe.

1901
01:33:07,822 --> 01:33:08,823
SPIDER-MAN: I would love that.

1902
01:33:09,790 --> 01:33:11,058
MJ: Okay.

1903
01:33:11,092 --> 01:33:13,160
FEMALE REPORTER: <i>The Hulk,</i>
<i>a.k.a. Dr. Bruce Banner,</i>

1904
01:33:13,194 --> 01:33:14,428
<i>is in custody,</i>

1905
01:33:14,462 --> 01:33:16,397
<i>currently being transferred</i>
<i>to a psychiatric ward.</i>

1906
01:33:16,430 --> 01:33:17,698
NED: Oh! So sad.

1907
01:33:17,731 --> 01:33:20,067
FEMALE REPORTER: <i>After years</i>
<i>as a peaceful academic,</i>

1908
01:33:20,101 --> 01:33:23,003
<i>the question</i>
<i>the world asked today is,</i>

1909
01:33:23,037 --> 01:33:24,638
<i>"What finally snapped?"</i>

1910
01:33:24,672 --> 01:33:26,273
-[PHONE VIBRATES]
-[ <i>SPIDER-MA</i> THEME PLAYS]

1911
01:33:26,307 --> 01:33:27,675
[GASPS]

1912
01:33:27,708 --> 01:33:28,976
[PHONE VIBRATING]

1913
01:33:29,777 --> 01:33:30,811
[DOOR OPENS]

1914
01:33:30,845 --> 01:33:32,746
APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1915
01:33:32,780 --> 01:33:34,348
<i>-Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
-MJ?

1916
01:33:34,381 --> 01:33:35,850
MJ: Yeah.
APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1917
01:33:35,883 --> 01:33:36,917
[DOOR CLOSES]

1918
01:33:36,951 --> 01:33:38,185
<i>-Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
-Uh...

1919
01:33:38,219 --> 01:33:39,521
You're not gonna
believe this...

1920
01:33:39,554 --> 01:33:40,921
-APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
-...but the Spidey Tracker app

1921
01:33:40,955 --> 01:33:42,256
-says that Spider-Man...
<i>-</i> APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1922
01:33:42,289 --> 01:33:44,758
-...is in the direct vicinity.
-APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1923
01:33:44,792 --> 01:33:46,026
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, yeah? No way.

1924
01:33:46,060 --> 01:33:46,794
-That's crazy.
<i>-</i> APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1925
01:33:46,827 --> 01:33:49,196
[DISTORTED] <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1926
01:33:49,230 --> 01:33:52,199
Uh, Ned, Spider-Man.
Spider-Man, Ned.

1927
01:33:52,233 --> 01:33:53,334
It's nice to meet you, Ned.

1928
01:33:53,367 --> 01:33:55,236
Hello. [CHUCKLES]

1929
01:33:55,269 --> 01:33:56,203
I'm not, like, a weirdo

1930
01:33:56,237 --> 01:33:57,972
-or anything, I'm...
-He's a little weird.

1931
01:33:58,005 --> 01:34:00,741
Why, uh...
Why are you here? [CHUCKLES]

1932
01:34:00,774 --> 01:34:02,376
-SPIDER-MAN: Oh, I...
-I was...

1933
01:34:02,409 --> 01:34:03,844
-I was on a subway platform.
-SPIDER-MAN: She was in the...

1934
01:34:03,878 --> 01:34:04,879
Platform. Right.

1935
01:34:04,912 --> 01:34:05,813
-And she was on her phone.
-Yeah, and... Yeah,

1936
01:34:05,846 --> 01:34:06,814
I got a little distracted.
And the train

1937
01:34:06,847 --> 01:34:07,616
-was coming and he...
-SPIDER-MAN: I mean...

1938
01:34:07,648 --> 01:34:09,450
And I just
swooped her right up.

1939
01:34:09,483 --> 01:34:10,951
-Yep. Saved me.
-SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.

1940
01:34:12,720 --> 01:34:14,188
Oh, my God.

1941
01:34:15,256 --> 01:34:16,857
Why has that
never happened to me?

1942
01:34:16,891 --> 01:34:19,260
-[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]
-So what if you're mid-swing

1943
01:34:19,293 --> 01:34:20,861
and you decide
you need to pee?

1944
01:34:20,895 --> 01:34:22,363
Do you just land
on top of a building?

1945
01:34:22,396 --> 01:34:23,731
SPIDER-MAN: What?

1946
01:34:23,764 --> 01:34:24,665
Do you drop down
to ground level

1947
01:34:24,698 --> 01:34:25,567
and run into a coffee shop
and you're like,

1948
01:34:25,600 --> 01:34:27,234
"Hey, it's Spider-Man.
I need to pee"?

1949
01:34:27,268 --> 01:34:29,103
Or do you find
a rooftop somewhere?

1950
01:34:29,136 --> 01:34:31,038
SPIDER-MAN: No, I don't find
a rooftop somewhere, Ned.

1951
01:34:31,071 --> 01:34:33,107
Is this really what you wanna
be asking him right now?

1952
01:34:33,140 --> 01:34:34,775
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, dude, come on,
you can ask me anything.

1953
01:34:34,808 --> 01:34:36,243
You wanna know
how my web shooters work?

1954
01:34:36,277 --> 01:34:37,945
I mean, I already know
how the web shooters work.

1955
01:34:37,978 --> 01:34:39,180
SPIDER-MAN: Is that right?

1956
01:34:39,213 --> 01:34:42,349
Well, there's obviously some
sort of a shear-thinning fluid

1957
01:34:42,383 --> 01:34:44,785
that is cycling
within a chamber, right?

1958
01:34:44,818 --> 01:34:46,020
So it can keep
its liquid form.

1959
01:34:46,053 --> 01:34:48,355
And then, when you activate it
by pressing on the triggers,

1960
01:34:48,389 --> 01:34:50,090
it runs through
a Teflon turbine,

1961
01:34:50,124 --> 01:34:53,961
and then it hardens when it
interacts with the air. Right?

1962
01:34:56,197 --> 01:34:59,066
SPIDER-MAN: Uh...
I mean, not exactly, but...

1963
01:34:59,099 --> 01:35:01,368
Okay, okay, well, then tell me
what's in the web fluid.

1964
01:35:01,402 --> 01:35:04,371
I would guess something
like a long chain polymer.

1965
01:35:04,405 --> 01:35:05,906
Uh, nylon?

1966
01:35:05,940 --> 01:35:06,907
SPIDER-MAN:
That's pretty close.

1967
01:35:06,941 --> 01:35:09,977
Okay, okay. What about
Nomex or, oh, Kevlar?

1968
01:35:12,446 --> 01:35:14,348
[IMITATES FRODO] "All right,
then. Keep your secrets."

1969
01:35:14,381 --> 01:35:15,482
SPIDER-MAN: [IMITATES GANDALF]
"If you're referring

1970
01:35:15,517 --> 01:35:16,518
"to the incident

1971
01:35:16,551 --> 01:35:17,519
-with the dragon..."
-[CHUCKLES]

1972
01:35:17,552 --> 01:35:18,986
"...I was barely involved."

1973
01:35:19,019 --> 01:35:20,788
[IMITATES GANDALF]
"All I did was simply

1974
01:35:20,821 --> 01:35:22,823
"give your uncle a little nudge
out the door."

1975
01:35:22,856 --> 01:35:25,192
[ALL LAUGH]

1976
01:35:25,226 --> 01:35:26,327
NED: Solid reference.

1977
01:35:26,360 --> 01:35:27,428
[WATCH CHIMES]

1978
01:35:27,461 --> 01:35:29,263
Ooh, banh mi time.

1979
01:35:29,296 --> 01:35:30,831
You ordered banh mis?

1980
01:35:30,864 --> 01:35:32,066
I ordered five banh mis.

1981
01:35:32,099 --> 01:35:33,133
We have Spider-Man
in the apartment.

1982
01:35:33,167 --> 01:35:33,867
He's gonna get fed.

1983
01:35:33,901 --> 01:35:35,903
-[CHUCKLES]
-[NED CHUCKLES]

1984
01:35:37,572 --> 01:35:39,073
Sorry about him.
He's just, like,

1985
01:35:39,106 --> 01:35:40,808
very excited that you're here.

1986
01:35:40,841 --> 01:35:41,543
SPIDER-MAN: You kidding?
This is, like,

1987
01:35:41,576 --> 01:35:43,143
the most fun I've had in years.

1988
01:35:43,177 --> 01:35:45,246
-[MJ CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
-I really missed you guys.

1989
01:35:47,181 --> 01:35:49,216
You guys really do
look like best friends.

1990
01:35:49,250 --> 01:35:50,251
SPIDER-MAN: What do you mean?

1991
01:35:59,893 --> 01:36:00,894
You should tell him.

1992
01:36:01,495 --> 01:36:02,496
He can handle it.

1993
01:36:04,398 --> 01:36:06,066
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, I know.
[SIGHS]

1994
01:36:08,168 --> 01:36:09,136
Um...

1995
01:36:12,507 --> 01:36:15,976
When she was inhabiting you
on the rooftop,

1996
01:36:17,311 --> 01:36:18,479
she kissed me...

1997
01:36:19,514 --> 01:36:21,248
and I kissed her back,

1998
01:36:21,282 --> 01:36:24,418
because I... I thought
it was you, but I didn't know.

1999
01:36:24,451 --> 01:36:26,287
And I'm... I'm really sorry.

2000
01:36:27,589 --> 01:36:29,023
I just thought you should know.

2001
01:36:31,358 --> 01:36:32,359
Thanks for telling me.

2002
01:36:36,063 --> 01:36:38,866
I mean, it's not like I
remember anything anyway, so...

2003
01:36:40,200 --> 01:36:41,302
SPIDER-MAN: Really?

2004
01:36:41,335 --> 01:36:42,870
Yeah. It was weird,
it was like,

2005
01:36:42,903 --> 01:36:44,238
one second
I was sitting at my desk,

2006
01:36:44,271 --> 01:36:46,974
and the next second
I was lying on the street.

2007
01:36:47,007 --> 01:36:48,475
I don't know,
like a light switch went off.

2008
01:36:48,510 --> 01:36:51,045
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

2009
01:36:51,078 --> 01:36:51,979
What?

2010
01:36:52,012 --> 01:36:53,515
SPIDER-MAN: So you don't
remember anything?

2011
01:36:55,550 --> 01:36:56,417
No. Why?

2012
01:36:56,450 --> 01:36:58,052
SPIDER-MAN:
Metzger said he remembered

2013
01:36:58,085 --> 01:36:59,621
thinking about
someone named Sara,

2014
01:36:59,654 --> 01:37:01,088
but what you're saying is that

2015
01:37:01,121 --> 01:37:03,057
you don't remember
anything at all?

2016
01:37:05,159 --> 01:37:07,494
I mean, yeah,
it was instantaneous.

2017
01:37:07,529 --> 01:37:08,862
That's what made it so scary.

2018
01:37:10,898 --> 01:37:12,099
SPIDER-MAN: He lied to me.

2019
01:37:13,535 --> 01:37:15,102
[LINE RINGING]

2020
01:37:15,135 --> 01:37:16,604
<i>I heard you caught leshy.</i>

2021
01:37:16,638 --> 01:37:17,772
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.
Her name's Jean Grey.

2022
01:37:17,806 --> 01:37:20,474
I need some help determining
the size of some potatoes.

2023
01:37:20,508 --> 01:37:21,308
Potatoes?

2024
01:37:21,342 --> 01:37:22,409
[SOFTLY]
I think that's Black Widow.

2025
01:37:22,443 --> 01:37:24,411
SPIDER-MAN: I think Metzger
lied to me about a name.

2026
01:37:24,445 --> 01:37:25,879
<i>Can you see</i>
<i>if there's a connection</i>

2027
01:37:25,913 --> 01:37:28,482
<i>between Jean</i>
<i>and someone named Sara?</i>

2028
01:37:28,516 --> 01:37:30,951
Hmm. These potatoes
sound meager.

2029
01:37:30,984 --> 01:37:32,419
-[KEYBOARD CLACKING]
-[LAPTOP TRILLING]

2030
01:37:32,453 --> 01:37:34,254
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, wow.
That really is your office.

2031
01:37:35,022 --> 01:37:36,123
Well, well, well.

2032
01:37:36,156 --> 01:37:38,492
Internet, government records,

2033
01:37:38,526 --> 01:37:40,628
and a lot of data
related to Jean Grey

2034
01:37:40,662 --> 01:37:43,330
has been scrubbed
by Damage Control.

2035
01:37:43,364 --> 01:37:44,365
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Data about what?</i>

2036
01:37:45,332 --> 01:37:47,067
Her sister.

2037
01:37:47,101 --> 01:37:48,435
SPIDER-MAN: Wait,
Jean has a sister?

2038
01:37:50,137 --> 01:37:52,139
Hmm. Sara Grey.

2039
01:37:52,172 --> 01:37:53,974
<i>Also a telepath.</i>

2040
01:37:54,007 --> 01:37:55,943
<i>Damage Control</i>
<i>took her into custody</i>

2041
01:37:55,976 --> 01:37:57,679
<i>for study and observation.</i>

2042
01:37:57,712 --> 01:37:59,213
<i>Wow. I mean,</i>
<i>you can probably guess</i>

2043
01:37:59,246 --> 01:38:00,247
<i>what they mean by that.</i>

2044
01:38:00,280 --> 01:38:02,449
Experimentation and other
human rights violations.

2045
01:38:02,483 --> 01:38:04,351
Hmm. Yes, exactly.
Wait, who are you?

2046
01:38:04,385 --> 01:38:06,220
<i>-Hi. Ned Leeds. Big fan.</i>
-MJ: <i>I'm...</i>

2047
01:38:06,253 --> 01:38:07,421
Hi.

2048
01:38:07,454 --> 01:38:09,156
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Uh, I'm sorry.</i>
<i>Uh...</i> [GRUNTS]

2049
01:38:09,189 --> 01:38:12,192
I'm just so happy
that the sad man has friends.

2050
01:38:13,060 --> 01:38:14,294
[SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

2051
01:38:14,328 --> 01:38:16,497
Thanks. I, uh...
I owe you one.

2052
01:38:17,599 --> 01:38:19,066
YELENA: <i>Good luck, Spider-Man.</i>

2053
01:38:19,099 --> 01:38:20,134
Bye.

2054
01:38:20,167 --> 01:38:21,603
SPIDER-MAN: She was
just looking for her sister

2055
01:38:21,636 --> 01:38:23,971
and I handed her
to the people that took her.

2056
01:38:24,004 --> 01:38:25,507
-I gotta go.
-MJ: Hey, Peter...

2057
01:38:25,540 --> 01:38:26,541
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah?

2058
01:38:27,575 --> 01:38:28,643
Just be careful, all right?

2059
01:38:30,545 --> 01:38:31,546
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, I will.

2060
01:38:35,015 --> 01:38:36,383
[WEB SHOOTER CLICKS]

2061
01:38:36,417 --> 01:38:38,152
Spider-Man's name is Peter?

2062
01:38:40,254 --> 01:38:42,289
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2063
01:38:51,699 --> 01:38:54,134
Jean, who do you want to be?

2064
01:38:56,571 --> 01:38:58,071
Her. Pink jacket.

2065
01:38:59,574 --> 01:39:00,575
She's too far.

2066
01:39:01,609 --> 01:39:02,644
You're gonna have to hop.

2067
01:39:02,677 --> 01:39:04,211
JEAN: Hop?

2068
01:39:04,244 --> 01:39:06,280
First, pick someone close.

2069
01:39:07,014 --> 01:39:08,015
And then...

2070
01:39:10,150 --> 01:39:12,219
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2071
01:39:13,454 --> 01:39:14,955
[WHOOSHING]

2072
01:39:20,728 --> 01:39:22,129
[JEAN LAUGHS]

2073
01:39:22,162 --> 01:39:23,665
Each hop has a limit.

2074
01:39:23,698 --> 01:39:25,600
But you can
string them together

2075
01:39:25,633 --> 01:39:27,569
and go as far as you want.

2076
01:39:27,602 --> 01:39:30,204
-And when you let go...
-[WHOOSHES]

2077
01:39:30,237 --> 01:39:32,607
You're right back
where you started.

2078
01:39:32,640 --> 01:39:35,042
Could you do that to everyone
in this park at once?

2079
01:39:35,810 --> 01:39:38,011
Well, yeah, maybe one day.

2080
01:39:38,045 --> 01:39:39,213
If you get really good.

2081
01:39:41,148 --> 01:39:42,449
[GIRL LAUGHING]

2082
01:39:44,652 --> 01:39:46,654
[BOTH LAUGHING]

2083
01:39:52,727 --> 01:39:53,728
How could she just...

2084
01:39:55,128 --> 01:39:56,163
send us away?

2085
01:39:57,665 --> 01:39:59,132
She wasn't really a mom.

2086
01:40:01,301 --> 01:40:02,402
Not like that, anyway.

2087
01:40:02,436 --> 01:40:04,471
She was, before we changed.

2088
01:40:04,505 --> 01:40:05,472
Yeah, well,
if that's all it takes

2089
01:40:05,507 --> 01:40:06,406
for you to stop being a mom,

2090
01:40:06,440 --> 01:40:08,342
then you're not a mom.

2091
01:40:08,375 --> 01:40:10,477
What would you do
if you had daughters like us?

2092
01:40:11,078 --> 01:40:12,145
I'd love them.

2093
01:40:15,617 --> 01:40:17,384
-Especially the redhead one.
-Shut up.

2094
01:40:20,220 --> 01:40:21,523
We have each other.

2095
01:40:22,690 --> 01:40:23,791
Mmm.

2096
01:40:25,359 --> 01:40:27,060
SARA: And we have ice cream.

2097
01:40:28,763 --> 01:40:30,264
-One mint chip, one chocolate?
-Yeah.

2098
01:40:34,268 --> 01:40:35,537
-[INDISTINCT CHATTER]
-[WOMAN GRUNTS]

2099
01:40:36,604 --> 01:40:37,605
WOMAN: Okay.

2100
01:40:39,239 --> 01:40:40,742
Now I know how you're playing.

2101
01:40:40,775 --> 01:40:42,476
-[GIRL LAUGHING]
-Oh.

2102
01:40:48,482 --> 01:40:49,617
[SARA WINCES]

2103
01:40:54,388 --> 01:40:55,590
[VEHICLE APPROACHING]

2104
01:40:58,258 --> 01:40:59,426
GUARD 1: Get down!
GUARD 2: Get down!

2105
01:40:59,459 --> 01:41:00,828
GUARD 3: Get down! Get down!
GUARD 1: Get down! Get down!

2106
01:41:00,862 --> 01:41:01,829
GUARD 2: Get down
on the ground now!

2107
01:41:01,863 --> 01:41:02,764
GUARD 3: Get down! Get down!

2108
01:41:02,797 --> 01:41:04,064
[GASPS]

2109
01:41:05,265 --> 01:41:06,266
Sara!

2110
01:41:08,570 --> 01:41:10,103
[PANTING]

2111
01:41:11,739 --> 01:41:13,273
SARA: <i>I'm sorry, Jean.</i>

2112
01:41:14,141 --> 01:41:15,543
<i>I have to keep you safe.</i>

2113
01:41:15,577 --> 01:41:18,145
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2114
01:41:18,178 --> 01:41:19,279
[WHOOSHES]

2115
01:41:19,313 --> 01:41:21,148
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

2116
01:41:25,853 --> 01:41:27,722
[MUSIC CRESCENDOES]

2117
01:41:28,656 --> 01:41:30,290
[GASPS, PANTS]

2118
01:41:33,427 --> 01:41:35,329
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2119
01:41:43,470 --> 01:41:45,472
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2120
01:41:46,908 --> 01:41:49,109
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2121
01:41:57,952 --> 01:42:01,254
METZGER: Subject is awake.
Heart rate is 94 bpm.

2122
01:42:01,723 --> 01:42:03,825
[FAINT TRILLING]

2123
01:42:03,858 --> 01:42:05,760
Jean, that's not
gonna work anymore,

2124
01:42:05,793 --> 01:42:07,528
thanks to Spider-Man.

2125
01:42:08,228 --> 01:42:10,464
[GRUNTS, PANTING]

2126
01:42:10,497 --> 01:42:11,899
-[JEAN GRUNTS SOFTLY]
-Jean?

2127
01:42:12,499 --> 01:42:13,901
[GRUNTING]

2128
01:42:13,935 --> 01:42:16,904
[JEAN GRUNTS, PANTS]

2129
01:42:21,542 --> 01:42:22,777
I need you to breathe.

2130
01:42:22,810 --> 01:42:24,579
I need you to look at me
and breathe.

2131
01:42:24,612 --> 01:42:26,380
-[BREATHES DEEPLY]
-METZGER: Okay?

2132
01:42:26,413 --> 01:42:27,815
You're safe. Breathe.

2133
01:42:30,484 --> 01:42:31,619
Where is she?

2134
01:42:32,954 --> 01:42:34,922
Like your sister, you've been
blessed with a power

2135
01:42:34,956 --> 01:42:37,792
that has the potential to do
tremendous good in the world,

2136
01:42:38,593 --> 01:42:40,795
or tremendous damage.

2137
01:42:40,828 --> 01:42:43,296
A power like yours
in the hands of a child

2138
01:42:43,330 --> 01:42:44,832
is an impossible burden.

2139
01:42:45,600 --> 01:42:47,735
But imagine...

2140
01:42:47,769 --> 01:42:50,337
if that power was placed
in the hands of people

2141
01:42:50,370 --> 01:42:51,673
who actually know
what to do with it.

2142
01:43:00,682 --> 01:43:02,482
Where is my sister?

2143
01:43:05,385 --> 01:43:07,387
METZGER: You're gonna change
the world, Jean.

2144
01:43:07,689 --> 01:43:08,690
Hey!

2145
01:43:09,489 --> 01:43:11,491
Hey! [GRUNTING]

2146
01:43:12,994 --> 01:43:15,195
-[MACHINERY WHIRRING]
-[GASPS]

2147
01:43:17,364 --> 01:43:19,366
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

2148
01:43:29,844 --> 01:43:31,679
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2149
01:43:31,713 --> 01:43:33,548
-[PHONE RINGING]
-SPIDER-MAN: Frank.

2150
01:43:33,581 --> 01:43:35,550
I know where you are,
what you're doing.

2151
01:43:35,583 --> 01:43:37,350
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Oh, yeah?</i>
<i>And how's that?</i>

2152
01:43:37,384 --> 01:43:38,720
I got eyes everywhere, kid.

2153
01:43:38,753 --> 01:43:40,253
[BEEPING]

2154
01:43:40,287 --> 01:43:41,122
SPIDER-MAN: Look, Frank.

2155
01:43:41,155 --> 01:43:42,824
Damage Control kidnapped
Jean's sister.

2156
01:43:42,857 --> 01:43:43,925
Jean was just
trying to find her.

2157
01:43:43,958 --> 01:43:45,459
We were wrong
about everything.

2158
01:43:45,492 --> 01:43:47,695
Sentimental horseshit.

2159
01:43:47,729 --> 01:43:49,831
You've seen what she can do
and what she's capable of.

2160
01:43:49,864 --> 01:43:51,398
What, you're gonna
let her loose?

2161
01:43:51,431 --> 01:43:52,499
Is that what you're gonna do?

2162
01:43:53,668 --> 01:43:55,937
I'll tell you right now,
you do that,

2163
01:43:55,970 --> 01:43:57,638
I handle it my way.

2164
01:43:57,672 --> 01:43:58,573
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Frank, please,</i>
<i>can you just...</i>

2165
01:43:58,606 --> 01:43:59,507
-Eh...
-[CALL ENDS]

2166
01:43:59,540 --> 01:44:00,742
SPIDER-MAN: Frank!

2167
01:44:00,775 --> 01:44:02,777
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

2168
01:44:13,087 --> 01:44:14,021
Distance check?

2169
01:44:14,055 --> 01:44:15,656
-[KEYBOARD CLACKING]
-Forty-foot clearance.

2170
01:44:15,690 --> 01:44:17,058
METZGER:
Locking down the room.

2171
01:44:17,091 --> 01:44:17,992
GUARD: Locking down.

2172
01:44:18,025 --> 01:44:19,660
[DOOR BUZZES]

2173
01:44:23,497 --> 01:44:24,498
METZGER: <i>Disengage inhibitor.</i>

2174
01:44:27,400 --> 01:44:28,703
[GROANS SOFTLY]

2175
01:44:28,736 --> 01:44:31,304
METZGER: <i>Jean, your powers</i>
<i>are now fully operational.</i>

2176
01:44:31,338 --> 01:44:33,541
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
-[WARBLING]

2177
01:44:34,909 --> 01:44:36,010
[JEAN STRAINING]

2178
01:44:38,079 --> 01:44:39,914
[GRUNTS, GROANS]

2179
01:44:40,715 --> 01:44:41,682
METZGER: <i>As you can tell,</i>

2180
01:44:41,716 --> 01:44:44,051
<i>we are beyond</i>
<i>your jump radius.</i>

2181
01:44:44,085 --> 01:44:47,454
[BREATHING HEAVILY]
Tell me what V-Max is.

2182
01:44:47,487 --> 01:44:50,057
You're the second person
to ask me about that. I...

2183
01:44:50,091 --> 01:44:51,759
I have no idea what that means.

2184
01:44:51,793 --> 01:44:53,928
JEAN: <i>She sent me a message.</i>

2185
01:44:53,961 --> 01:44:56,764
She was trying to help me
find her.

2186
01:44:56,798 --> 01:44:58,733
She communicated
with you telepathically

2187
01:44:58,766 --> 01:45:00,668
across all that distance?

2188
01:45:00,701 --> 01:45:03,738
We did register a huge spike
in that session.

2189
01:45:05,606 --> 01:45:06,707
Fascinating.

2190
01:45:06,741 --> 01:45:08,910
What does it mean, asshole?

2191
01:45:10,678 --> 01:45:11,712
I don't know.

2192
01:45:12,680 --> 01:45:13,981
Let's begin.

2193
01:45:14,015 --> 01:45:15,650
[DEVICE BUZZES]

2194
01:45:17,450 --> 01:45:19,921
[DEVICE POWERING UP]

2195
01:45:22,089 --> 01:45:24,559
METZGER: <i>Our work with Sara</i>
<i>centered on two areas,</i>

2196
01:45:24,592 --> 01:45:26,861
identifying the source
of her power

2197
01:45:26,894 --> 01:45:29,530
and identifying a path
towards copying it.

2198
01:45:29,564 --> 01:45:31,398
-[SYSTEM TRILLING]
-If we could find a way

2199
01:45:31,431 --> 01:45:33,868
to record a telepathic brain
during a jump,

2200
01:45:33,901 --> 01:45:36,971
then perhaps we could
replicate those pathways

2201
01:45:37,004 --> 01:45:38,806
in a mind of our choosing.

2202
01:45:40,141 --> 01:45:44,512
<i>This instrument</i>
<i>is your sister's legacy.</i>

2203
01:45:44,545 --> 01:45:47,447
<i>We built this together over</i>
<i>many months of trial and error.</i>

2204
01:45:48,649 --> 01:45:50,751
I hope you and I
can honor her sacrifice.

2205
01:45:53,888 --> 01:45:55,355
What are you talking about?

2206
01:45:56,757 --> 01:45:58,025
Trigger the first jump.

2207
01:45:59,594 --> 01:46:01,428
[DEVICE TRILLING]

2208
01:46:02,797 --> 01:46:05,432
Tell me what V-Max is.

2209
01:46:05,465 --> 01:46:06,968
I know that's where
you're hiding her.

2210
01:46:07,001 --> 01:46:08,803
-[WHOOSHES]
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2211
01:46:08,836 --> 01:46:09,904
[DEVICE TRILLING]

2212
01:46:11,438 --> 01:46:12,773
[GASPS, PANTS]

2213
01:46:16,077 --> 01:46:17,979
-[DEVICE TRILLING]
-[WHOOSHES]

2214
01:46:18,012 --> 01:46:19,780
[SYSTEM CRACKLING]

2215
01:46:22,149 --> 01:46:23,184
She's jumping.

2216
01:46:23,217 --> 01:46:25,553
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CRESCENDOES,
ENDS]

2217
01:46:25,586 --> 01:46:26,988
Copy.

2218
01:46:27,021 --> 01:46:30,057
We're in full lockdown.
Process has commenced.

2219
01:46:30,091 --> 01:46:31,092
SPIDER-MAN: What process?

2220
01:46:32,660 --> 01:46:35,796
Hey, whoa, that's a pretty
serious look there, dude.

2221
01:46:35,830 --> 01:46:37,497
Hey, hey, whoa!
What the hell, man?

2222
01:46:37,531 --> 01:46:38,699
Come on. I'm a friend
of Damage Control.

2223
01:46:38,733 --> 01:46:39,600
What are you doin'?

2224
01:46:42,970 --> 01:46:43,804
Huh.

2225
01:46:43,838 --> 01:46:45,740
It's gonna be like that.
You wanna go.

2226
01:46:45,773 --> 01:46:47,141
All right.

2227
01:46:47,174 --> 01:46:48,776
All right, well,
just give me a sec.

2228
01:46:49,210 --> 01:46:51,078
Give me a sec.

2229
01:46:51,112 --> 01:46:52,780
I'm not in high school anymore.

2230
01:46:52,813 --> 01:46:54,849
[GRUNTING]

2231
01:46:54,882 --> 01:46:56,517
Do you stretch?
You a big stretcher?

2232
01:46:56,550 --> 01:46:58,552
I mean, you should do
in your line of work.

2233
01:46:58,586 --> 01:47:00,187
What about you?
You guys stretch?

2234
01:47:00,221 --> 01:47:01,722
It's so good for you.

2235
01:47:01,756 --> 01:47:03,157
[GROANING]

2236
01:47:03,190 --> 01:47:04,225
You ready?

2237
01:47:04,258 --> 01:47:06,560
-[GUNSHOTS]
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2238
01:47:13,901 --> 01:47:14,902
Watch your head!

2239
01:47:19,807 --> 01:47:21,008
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2240
01:47:23,010 --> 01:47:24,145
[GROANING]

2241
01:47:25,913 --> 01:47:27,148
-[GUARD GRUNTING]
-[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2242
01:47:34,822 --> 01:47:36,624
Where is Jean Grey?

2243
01:47:36,657 --> 01:47:37,658
[WHOOSHES]

2244
01:47:37,692 --> 01:47:39,492
-[DEVICE TRILLING]
-TECHNICIAN: That's jump 26.

2245
01:47:39,527 --> 01:47:40,761
-Recordings look good.
-[WHOOSHING CONTINUES]

2246
01:47:40,795 --> 01:47:41,929
GUARD: Excuse me, sir.

2247
01:47:42,830 --> 01:47:43,898
We have an intruder.

2248
01:47:44,732 --> 01:47:45,833
[WHOOSHING]

2249
01:47:47,101 --> 01:47:48,936
[DOOR BEEPS, CLICKS]

2250
01:47:48,970 --> 01:47:50,171
-TECHNICIAN: You were right.
-[WHOOSHING]

2251
01:47:50,204 --> 01:47:52,239
She's much stronger
than her sister.

2252
01:47:53,240 --> 01:47:54,675
Increase the frequency.

2253
01:47:54,709 --> 01:47:56,010
[DEVICE AMPLIFIES, WARBLES]

2254
01:47:56,043 --> 01:47:57,545
You're doing very well, Jean.

2255
01:47:57,578 --> 01:47:58,913
-[DEVICE TRILLING]
-[WHOOSHING RAPIDLY]

2256
01:47:58,946 --> 01:48:02,616
-[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]
-[SYSTEM CRACKLING RAPIDLY]

2257
01:48:02,650 --> 01:48:05,485
-[DEVICE TRILLING]
-[WHOOSHING RAPIDLY]

2258
01:48:06,654 --> 01:48:08,022
[SILENCE]

2259
01:48:09,256 --> 01:48:11,926
[PANTING STEADILY]

2260
01:48:13,661 --> 01:48:15,563
[RATTLING OVERHEAD]

2261
01:48:19,967 --> 01:48:21,836
[VENT RATTLING FAINTLY]

2262
01:48:29,677 --> 01:48:31,212
[VENT RATTLING]

2263
01:48:31,245 --> 01:48:32,847
[LABEL RUSTLING]

2264
01:48:34,081 --> 01:48:35,216
[SCOFFS WEAKLY]

2265
01:48:36,717 --> 01:48:38,052
[LABEL RUSTLING]

2266
01:48:45,292 --> 01:48:46,761
METZGER: <i>Jean?</i>

2267
01:48:48,963 --> 01:48:51,065
-[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
-[SYSTEM CRACKLING]

2268
01:48:51,098 --> 01:48:52,266
METZGER: Jean,
can you hear me?

2269
01:48:52,299 --> 01:48:54,735
[SYSTEM CHIMING,
CRACKLING RAPIDLY]

2270
01:48:56,303 --> 01:48:58,773
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2271
01:48:58,806 --> 01:48:59,840
Jean?

2272
01:48:59,874 --> 01:49:01,609
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2273
01:49:04,278 --> 01:49:05,679
You're a murderer.

2274
01:49:05,713 --> 01:49:07,882
[SYSTEM BEEPING RAPIDLY]

2275
01:49:07,915 --> 01:49:11,018
-Her frequencies are evolving.
-[SYSTEM CRACKLING]

2276
01:49:11,052 --> 01:49:13,187
This doesn't make sense.

2277
01:49:13,220 --> 01:49:17,591
The last thing
my sister saw was this room.

2278
01:49:17,625 --> 01:49:18,859
TECHNICIAN:
Her brainwaves are somehow

2279
01:49:18,893 --> 01:49:20,161
affecting the objects
around her.

2280
01:49:20,194 --> 01:49:21,228
Shut it down.

2281
01:49:21,262 --> 01:49:22,663
I'm trying, sir.

2282
01:49:22,696 --> 01:49:24,065
What do you mean
you're trying?

2283
01:49:24,098 --> 01:49:29,203
The last thing my sister saw
was this goddamn room!

2284
01:49:29,236 --> 01:49:31,138
-Shut it down!
-I can't, sir.

2285
01:49:32,206 --> 01:49:33,207
Move.

2286
01:49:33,908 --> 01:49:35,743
[ALARM BLARING]

2287
01:49:35,776 --> 01:49:37,745
I can't let you
do that, Bill.

2288
01:49:37,778 --> 01:49:39,780
[OMINOUS MUSICAL STING]

2289
01:49:41,282 --> 01:49:43,284
-[FIELD WARBLING]
-The only hands

2290
01:49:43,317 --> 01:49:45,352
that will wield this power...

2291
01:49:45,386 --> 01:49:48,756
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING STOPS]
-...are mine.

2292
01:49:48,789 --> 01:49:50,825
-[WHOOSHES]
-[ALL GRUNTING]

2293
01:49:52,359 --> 01:49:54,361
[FIELD WARBLING]

2294
01:49:55,329 --> 01:49:57,598
[ALL SCREAMING, GRUNTING]

2295
01:49:58,799 --> 01:50:01,001
-[HORN HONKING]
-[PEOPLE GRUNTING]

2296
01:50:01,035 --> 01:50:02,069
[ALL GRUNTING]

2297
01:50:02,103 --> 01:50:03,771
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

2298
01:50:03,804 --> 01:50:06,140
-[TIRES SCREECH]
-[CAR ALARM BLARING]

2299
01:50:07,675 --> 01:50:09,043
[BRAKES SQUEAL]

2300
01:50:10,144 --> 01:50:12,713
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

2301
01:50:12,746 --> 01:50:14,348
-[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]
-WOMAN: What is happening?

2302
01:50:15,850 --> 01:50:17,184
MAN 1: Get inside.

2303
01:50:19,854 --> 01:50:20,888
[DOG BARKING]

2304
01:50:24,125 --> 01:50:25,159
MAN 2: Wait for me!

2305
01:50:25,192 --> 01:50:26,861
[BARKING]

2306
01:50:27,962 --> 01:50:29,697
[FIELD WARBLING]

2307
01:50:35,870 --> 01:50:37,638
-[WHOOSHES]
-[PEOPLE SCREAM]

2308
01:50:43,010 --> 01:50:45,012
[FIELD WARBLING]

2309
01:50:47,381 --> 01:50:49,383
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

2310
01:50:57,158 --> 01:50:59,994
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
-[WHOOSHES]

2311
01:51:06,233 --> 01:51:08,068
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2312
01:51:09,870 --> 01:51:11,872
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

2313
01:51:53,113 --> 01:51:55,249
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

2314
01:52:00,522 --> 01:52:02,189
-What...
-ALL: What do you want?

2315
01:52:05,960 --> 01:52:08,929
SPIDER-MAN: Jean,
I'm here to help you.

2316
01:52:10,197 --> 01:52:12,199
You put me here.

2317
01:52:12,233 --> 01:52:14,134
SPIDER-MAN: I know,
and I'm sorry about Sara,

2318
01:52:14,168 --> 01:52:16,237
and I'm sorry
that I got it so wrong.

2319
01:52:17,004 --> 01:52:18,405
[DOOR SLAMS]

2320
01:52:18,439 --> 01:52:19,406
JEAN: If you came here

2321
01:52:19,440 --> 01:52:21,875
to save a helpless girl
from Damage Control,

2322
01:52:21,909 --> 01:52:22,910
you're too late.

2323
01:52:23,978 --> 01:52:25,846
They're the ones
who need saving.

2324
01:52:25,879 --> 01:52:27,181
And now...

2325
01:52:27,848 --> 01:52:28,849
so do you.

2326
01:52:30,050 --> 01:52:31,185
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

2327
01:52:31,218 --> 01:52:32,253
Here we go.

2328
01:52:32,286 --> 01:52:33,754
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2329
01:52:41,462 --> 01:52:43,097
-[MALE NINJA GRUNTS]
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

2330
01:52:46,834 --> 01:52:48,202
SPIDER-MAN: God, that's cool.

2331
01:52:49,537 --> 01:52:50,971
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2332
01:52:54,074 --> 01:52:55,776
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

2333
01:53:03,551 --> 01:53:05,052
SPIDER-MAN: Ow! Ow!

2334
01:53:09,256 --> 01:53:11,292
Jean! Jean, please!

2335
01:53:11,325 --> 01:53:13,127
[THUDDING]

2336
01:53:24,104 --> 01:53:25,506
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2337
01:53:25,540 --> 01:53:27,308
Come on! Come on! Come on!

2338
01:53:30,545 --> 01:53:32,212
-[FEMALE NINJA GRUNTS]
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

2339
01:53:32,246 --> 01:53:33,314
[GROANS]

2340
01:53:33,347 --> 01:53:35,583
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

2341
01:53:37,619 --> 01:53:39,386
[FIELD WARBLING]

2342
01:53:42,056 --> 01:53:43,257
[WEAPONS ENERGIZING]

2343
01:53:48,062 --> 01:53:49,163
SPIDER-MAN: What the...

2344
01:53:49,196 --> 01:53:50,297
[NINJAS GRUNTING]

2345
01:53:51,031 --> 01:53:52,066
JEAN: Isn't it funny

2346
01:53:52,099 --> 01:53:54,201
how your friends
from Damage Control

2347
01:53:54,234 --> 01:53:55,502
developed a special weapon

2348
01:53:55,537 --> 01:53:56,970
just for you?

2349
01:53:57,004 --> 01:53:58,138
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

2350
01:53:58,172 --> 01:54:00,941
They've got
a whole task force ready.

2351
01:54:00,974 --> 01:54:02,876
Just in case
you ever get out of line.

2352
01:54:02,910 --> 01:54:05,045
-[FIELD WARBLING]
-[METZGER GRUNTS]

2353
01:54:07,314 --> 01:54:08,616
People are monsters.

2354
01:54:12,419 --> 01:54:13,521
[BOTH GRUNTING]

2355
01:54:13,555 --> 01:54:16,924
You shouldn't trust them
any more than they trust you.

2356
01:54:16,957 --> 01:54:18,125
[NINJA GRUNTING]

2357
01:54:19,493 --> 01:54:20,494
[GROANS]

2358
01:54:23,097 --> 01:54:25,099
-[HORN BLARES]
-[PEOPLE SCREAM]

2359
01:54:27,401 --> 01:54:29,169
-[PHONE RINGING]
-[NINJAS GRUNTING]

2360
01:54:30,437 --> 01:54:31,606
SPIDER-MAN:
I'm a little busy, Frank.

2361
01:54:31,639 --> 01:54:33,073
We got a problem, kid.

2362
01:54:33,107 --> 01:54:34,308
<i>She got ahold of everyone</i>

2363
01:54:34,341 --> 01:54:35,976
<i>within a kilometer</i>
<i>of the island.</i>

2364
01:54:36,009 --> 01:54:37,411
SPIDER-MAN: [SIGHS]
Wait, what?

2365
01:54:37,444 --> 01:54:39,246
[FIELD WARBLING]

2366
01:54:39,279 --> 01:54:40,548
[GROANS SOFTLY]

2367
01:54:42,316 --> 01:54:43,450
[WHIMPERING SOFTLY]

2368
01:54:43,484 --> 01:54:44,952
Hey, look,
if you're gonna do something,

2369
01:54:44,985 --> 01:54:45,687
you better do it now.

2370
01:54:45,720 --> 01:54:46,987
SPIDER-MAN: I'm trying!

2371
01:54:52,393 --> 01:54:53,595
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2372
01:54:57,398 --> 01:54:58,499
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

2373
01:55:02,269 --> 01:55:04,606
-[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]
-[NINJAS GRUNTING]

2374
01:55:06,440 --> 01:55:08,475
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2375
01:55:12,479 --> 01:55:14,047
-[LINE DISCONNECTS]
-Kid?

2376
01:55:14,081 --> 01:55:15,949
Shit! Goddamn it.

2377
01:55:15,983 --> 01:55:17,985
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2378
01:55:18,018 --> 01:55:19,420
[TIRES SCREECHING]

2379
01:55:19,453 --> 01:55:21,021
[HORN HONKING]

2380
01:55:21,054 --> 01:55:22,524
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

2381
01:55:23,691 --> 01:55:25,292
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2382
01:55:26,260 --> 01:55:27,928
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2383
01:55:35,102 --> 01:55:36,437
[COUGHING]

2384
01:55:38,472 --> 01:55:39,973
[GASPS]

2385
01:55:40,007 --> 01:55:41,975
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2386
01:55:49,584 --> 01:55:50,984
JEAN: My sister died

2387
01:55:51,018 --> 01:55:52,219
in this room,

2388
01:55:53,521 --> 01:55:55,222
surrounded by these men.

2389
01:55:56,490 --> 01:55:57,659
And her only crime

2390
01:55:57,692 --> 01:55:59,359
was that she was special.

2391
01:56:00,427 --> 01:56:02,362
-[PANTING]
-JEAN: Just like you.

2392
01:56:03,731 --> 01:56:05,098
Just like me.

2393
01:56:07,635 --> 01:56:10,638
People like us don't get to
live a normal life.

2394
01:56:13,641 --> 01:56:16,977
We don't get to have friends
or a family.

2395
01:56:18,780 --> 01:56:20,280
Those people are gone.

2396
01:56:23,150 --> 01:56:24,719
That life is over.

2397
01:56:24,752 --> 01:56:27,087
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2398
01:56:38,566 --> 01:56:41,034
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

2399
01:56:50,845 --> 01:56:53,380
So why don't you just
be honest with yourself?

2400
01:56:56,350 --> 01:56:57,619
Are you Peter Parker?

2401
01:56:59,754 --> 01:57:01,255
Or are you Spider-Man?

2402
01:57:13,535 --> 01:57:15,502
[INHIBITOR BEEPS, POWERS DOWN]

2403
01:57:18,238 --> 01:57:20,173
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

2404
01:57:21,709 --> 01:57:23,377
[DISTORTED WARBLE]

2405
01:57:26,313 --> 01:57:28,315
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

2406
01:57:34,254 --> 01:57:35,289
I'm both.

2407
01:57:35,322 --> 01:57:37,559
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2408
01:57:42,730 --> 01:57:44,464
[NINJA GASPS]

2409
01:57:44,498 --> 01:57:46,500
[HEROIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2410
01:57:49,804 --> 01:57:50,805
[WHOOSHES]

2411
01:58:08,590 --> 01:58:09,824
[NINJA GRUNTS]

2412
01:58:12,292 --> 01:58:13,761
-[WEAPONS ENERGIZING]
-[GRUNTS]

2413
01:58:18,365 --> 01:58:19,366
[GUARD GRUNTS]

2414
01:58:25,940 --> 01:58:27,508
[NINJAS GRUNTING]

2415
01:58:55,837 --> 01:58:57,739
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

2416
01:59:07,548 --> 01:59:09,416
[FIELD WARBLING]

2417
01:59:17,659 --> 01:59:19,894
[PETER BREATHING HEAVILY]

2418
01:59:19,927 --> 01:59:22,162
Jean, please.

2419
01:59:23,397 --> 01:59:24,732
This won't make it right.

2420
01:59:26,868 --> 01:59:28,803
Oh, come on.
You're not a killer, Jean.

2421
01:59:28,836 --> 01:59:30,270
You have no idea what I am.

2422
01:59:31,873 --> 01:59:33,574
I know that
you loved your sister.

2423
01:59:36,844 --> 01:59:39,847
And I know that losing her
felt like you'd lost everything.

2424
01:59:39,881 --> 01:59:42,884
If you come any closer,
he dies! They all do!

2425
01:59:42,917 --> 01:59:44,519
[FIELD WARBLING]

2426
01:59:45,920 --> 01:59:47,922
[SIRENS WAILING]

2427
01:59:58,866 --> 02:00:01,268
[PETER PANTING]

2428
02:00:01,301 --> 02:00:02,737
You know this won't
bring her back, right, Jean?

2429
02:00:02,770 --> 02:00:04,572
-You... [GRUNTING]
-[FIELD WARBLING]

2430
02:00:04,605 --> 02:00:06,373
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

2431
02:00:11,012 --> 02:00:12,780
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2432
02:00:20,487 --> 02:00:22,990
Don't be so sure
I can't get into your mind.

2433
02:00:23,024 --> 02:00:24,692
[PETER GRUNTING SOFTLY]

2434
02:00:24,726 --> 02:00:26,928
I'm a lot more powerful
since I last tried.

2435
02:00:28,796 --> 02:00:30,464
[FIELD WARBLING]

2436
02:00:37,038 --> 02:00:38,438
[STRAINING] Go ahead.

2437
02:00:40,074 --> 02:00:41,308
[EXHALES]

2438
02:00:45,613 --> 02:00:46,714
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

2439
02:00:47,481 --> 02:00:48,482
MAY: Hey.

2440
02:00:49,784 --> 02:00:50,785
Hey.

2441
02:00:53,054 --> 02:00:55,022
You think
you don't have to listen to me

2442
02:00:55,056 --> 02:00:56,791
now that you've got powers?

2443
02:00:56,824 --> 02:00:58,492
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

2444
02:01:01,529 --> 02:01:07,001
You know, this... this whole
thing can get really scary.

2445
02:01:07,034 --> 02:01:08,035
You know that?

2446
02:01:10,671 --> 02:01:12,807
[FIELD WARBLING]

2447
02:01:14,709 --> 02:01:17,277
[SERENE MUSIC PLAYING]

2448
02:01:26,754 --> 02:01:28,421
It's already pretty scary.

2449
02:01:29,757 --> 02:01:31,324
MAY: Yeah.

2450
02:01:31,358 --> 02:01:32,693
And things can change,

2451
02:01:32,727 --> 02:01:34,361
like, very quickly...
[SNAPS FINGERS]

2452
02:01:34,394 --> 02:01:37,430
...in ways that we can't
even imagine right now.

2453
02:01:37,464 --> 02:01:38,566
I know.

2454
02:01:38,599 --> 02:01:39,867
MAY: No. [CHUCKLES]

2455
02:01:42,402 --> 02:01:43,971
I don't think you do know.

2456
02:01:45,840 --> 02:01:47,508
What do you mean?

2457
02:01:50,611 --> 02:01:52,379
You're a really special person.

2458
02:01:53,881 --> 02:01:55,382
And I would hope
that that will always

2459
02:01:55,415 --> 02:01:56,784
make you feel
really great about yourself,

2460
02:01:57,885 --> 02:02:00,788
but I know
sometimes it doesn't.

2461
02:02:00,822 --> 02:02:03,356
Sometimes,
you'll be really lonely.

2462
02:02:06,861 --> 02:02:08,029
And sometimes,

2463
02:02:09,496 --> 02:02:10,898
because you're special,

2464
02:02:13,433 --> 02:02:16,971
people can do dark,
monstrous things to you.

2465
02:02:19,173 --> 02:02:20,440
But...

2466
02:02:21,876 --> 02:02:23,410
this is what
I want you to know.

2467
02:02:25,412 --> 02:02:27,114
You're beautiful,

2468
02:02:27,148 --> 02:02:28,749
and the people who love you,

2469
02:02:28,783 --> 02:02:30,785
we love you
not because you're special,

2470
02:02:30,818 --> 02:02:32,653
we love you
because you're you.

2471
02:02:34,755 --> 02:02:36,123
I want you to remember that.

2472
02:02:38,526 --> 02:02:40,528
Even when it feels like
you're totally alone.

2473
02:02:43,531 --> 02:02:45,465
That's your
deepest responsibility.

2474
02:02:48,703 --> 02:02:49,770
Never forget that,

2475
02:02:49,804 --> 02:02:51,906
no matter how powerful
you become.

2476
02:02:52,940 --> 02:02:55,109
[SOMBER PIANO INSTRUMENTAL
PLAYS]

2477
02:03:08,089 --> 02:03:09,156
PETER: Hey.

2478
02:03:18,733 --> 02:03:20,601
-[JEAN EXHALES SHAKILY]
-[SIGHS]

2479
02:03:24,939 --> 02:03:26,574
I'm sorry about your sister.

2480
02:03:31,812 --> 02:03:33,648
I'm sorry about your aunt.

2481
02:03:37,018 --> 02:03:38,219
Yeah, you would've loved her.

2482
02:03:42,089 --> 02:03:44,025
Just because
we've lost someone...

2483
02:03:47,161 --> 02:03:49,163
It doesn't mean
we have to do this alone.

2484
02:03:51,198 --> 02:03:54,168
I mean, we can't.

2485
02:03:54,201 --> 02:03:55,903
Trust me, I've been trying.

2486
02:03:59,106 --> 02:04:00,473
It doesn't work.

2487
02:04:05,146 --> 02:04:06,514
Even if that's true...

2488
02:04:10,818 --> 02:04:11,953
I have no one.

2489
02:04:16,724 --> 02:04:17,792
You have me.

2490
02:04:25,866 --> 02:04:29,070
-[MUSIC FADES]
-[SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]

2491
02:04:33,774 --> 02:04:37,044
-[SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]
-[GUN COCK ECHOING]

2492
02:04:37,078 --> 02:04:37,979
[GUN FIRES]

2493
02:04:42,850 --> 02:04:44,819
[PETER GRUNTS]

2494
02:04:44,852 --> 02:04:46,287
-[FIELD WARBLES, DISSIPATES]
-[METZGER GRUNTS]

2495
02:04:46,320 --> 02:04:47,888
[ALL GRUNTING]

2496
02:04:47,922 --> 02:04:49,256
[ALL GRUNTING]

2497
02:04:50,224 --> 02:04:52,226
[FIELD WARBLES, DISSIPATES]

2498
02:04:54,895 --> 02:04:57,064
[GASPS, PANTS]

2499
02:04:57,098 --> 02:04:58,599
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2500
02:05:02,303 --> 02:05:03,838
Are you hurt?

2501
02:05:03,871 --> 02:05:05,873
No, I'm fine.
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2502
02:05:06,741 --> 02:05:08,142
[GASPS]

2503
02:05:10,878 --> 02:05:12,780
I'm okay.

2504
02:05:12,813 --> 02:05:14,215
-JEAN: Peter.
-I'm okay, I'm okay, I'm okay.

2505
02:05:14,248 --> 02:05:15,516
JEAN: Peter. No.

2506
02:05:19,620 --> 02:05:21,589
-Peter, Peter. No, no.
-[PETER GROANING]

2507
02:05:21,622 --> 02:05:22,857
-[COUGHS]
-JEAN: No, no, no, Peter.

2508
02:05:22,890 --> 02:05:24,658
-Peter.
-[GASPS]

2509
02:05:24,692 --> 02:05:27,061
Jean, you gotta get outta here.
They'll be looking for you.

2510
02:05:27,094 --> 02:05:28,896
No, no, no, no, no.
Please, just stay with me.

2511
02:05:28,929 --> 02:05:30,164
Come on, hold on.
Come on, please!

2512
02:05:30,197 --> 02:05:31,532
Jean, you're...

2513
02:05:32,233 --> 02:05:33,834
You're gonna be okay.

2514
02:05:35,069 --> 02:05:36,103
Just go.

2515
02:05:36,137 --> 02:05:37,705
-[SNIFFLES]
-[GROANS]

2516
02:05:38,239 --> 02:05:39,840
Look at me.

2517
02:05:39,874 --> 02:05:41,976
[GROANS, BREATHES RAGGEDLY]

2518
02:05:42,009 --> 02:05:44,145
-[INHALES]
-[PETER MUTTERING]

2519
02:05:45,880 --> 02:05:47,181
[EXHALES]

2520
02:05:49,383 --> 02:05:51,585
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

2521
02:05:52,787 --> 02:05:54,655
[INAUDIBLE]

2522
02:05:57,058 --> 02:05:58,626
MALE REPORTER: <i>Shock today,</i>

2523
02:05:58,659 --> 02:06:00,728
<i>as Spider-Man arrived</i>
<i>at Bellevue Hospital</i>

2524
02:06:00,761 --> 02:06:02,329
<i>with a bullet wound,</i>

2525
02:06:02,363 --> 02:06:04,098
<i>seemingly at death's door.</i>

2526
02:06:06,267 --> 02:06:09,003
<i>The reclusive crime fighter</i>
<i>is in critical condition,</i>

2527
02:06:09,036 --> 02:06:11,939
<i>as the city's top medical</i>
<i>experts work to save him.</i>

2528
02:06:15,409 --> 02:06:18,212
<i>Tonight, all eyes</i>
<i>are on Spider-Man.</i>

2529
02:06:20,247 --> 02:06:23,084
<i>The hero who saved</i>
<i>New York so many times...</i>

2530
02:06:23,117 --> 02:06:25,686
<i>is now in the hands</i>
<i>of its best and brightest.</i>

2531
02:06:28,089 --> 02:06:31,058
<i>And the people of New York</i>
<i>hold their breath.</i>

2532
02:06:42,136 --> 02:06:44,138
[EKG MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]

2533
02:06:49,043 --> 02:06:51,178
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

2534
02:06:56,016 --> 02:06:58,719
[FIELD WARBLING FAINTLY]

2535
02:07:06,961 --> 02:07:09,430
[INHALES, EXHALES]

2536
02:07:09,463 --> 02:07:11,765
-[WARBLING STOPS]
-[BIRD CHIRPING]

2537
02:07:16,203 --> 02:07:18,205
[EKG MACHINE BEEPING FAINTLY]

2538
02:07:34,221 --> 02:07:35,656
[SNORING]

2539
02:07:37,958 --> 02:07:38,959
PETER: Frank?

2540
02:07:42,329 --> 02:07:43,664
Where am I?

2541
02:07:45,432 --> 02:07:46,734
FRANK: No, no, no, no, no.

2542
02:07:46,767 --> 02:07:47,935
-Hey.
-Where's my mask?

2543
02:07:47,968 --> 02:07:49,236
Don't worry about that.
I got you covered.

2544
02:07:49,270 --> 02:07:50,871
Hey, you're good.

2545
02:07:50,905 --> 02:07:52,239
PETER: Where's Jean?
Is she okay?

2546
02:07:52,273 --> 02:07:54,241
Yeah, she's okay. [CHUCKLES]
She's okay.

2547
02:07:54,275 --> 02:07:55,442
PETER: Where is she?

2548
02:07:56,877 --> 02:07:58,312
I think maybe she just left.

2549
02:07:59,747 --> 02:08:03,050
She was, uh,
using her magic voodoo shit

2550
02:08:03,083 --> 02:08:05,019
to keep you alive.

2551
02:08:05,052 --> 02:08:08,055
[CHUCKLES] Yeah...
she's all right.

2552
02:08:14,795 --> 02:08:15,796
I'm sorry.

2553
02:08:20,501 --> 02:08:22,036
-Frank.
-Just... Just... I'm...

2554
02:08:22,069 --> 02:08:22,970
-Frank, it's okay.
-I'm really sorry

2555
02:08:23,003 --> 02:08:23,938
for what I did.

2556
02:08:23,971 --> 02:08:24,972
-No, Frank, it's okay.
-FRANK: And it's...

2557
02:08:25,005 --> 02:08:25,940
No, it's a lot of things,

2558
02:08:25,973 --> 02:08:27,708
but it sure as shit
ain't okay, all right?

2559
02:08:31,245 --> 02:08:32,246
I've seen...

2560
02:08:34,114 --> 02:08:37,785
I've seen real bravery, kid,
in my day.

2561
02:08:39,386 --> 02:08:40,387
But that...

2562
02:08:41,956 --> 02:08:43,290
that was something else.

2563
02:08:46,827 --> 02:08:48,128
-You crying, Frank?
-[LAUGHS]

2564
02:08:48,162 --> 02:08:49,797
No. I ain't...

2565
02:08:49,830 --> 02:08:51,432
[LAUGHING]

2566
02:08:52,066 --> 02:08:53,968
[LAUGHING]

2567
02:08:56,370 --> 02:08:58,305
You know, you look the exact
way I thought you would.

2568
02:08:59,406 --> 02:09:00,941
You know.

2569
02:09:00,975 --> 02:09:02,109
A nice kid.

2570
02:09:04,512 --> 02:09:05,980
Never had a friend like that.

2571
02:09:07,848 --> 02:09:09,283
Are we friends now?

2572
02:09:16,257 --> 02:09:17,958
I can't believe
I just saw you cry.

2573
02:09:17,992 --> 02:09:19,059
-[PETER LAUGHS]
-[LAUGHS] I didn't cry.

2574
02:09:19,093 --> 02:09:19,994
What are you talking about?

2575
02:09:20,027 --> 02:09:21,428
Bullshit.

2576
02:09:21,462 --> 02:09:23,364
[DISTANT SHOUTING]

2577
02:09:23,397 --> 02:09:25,099
Oh, yeah, this.

2578
02:09:25,132 --> 02:09:26,867
They've been doing it
all night.

2579
02:09:26,900 --> 02:09:28,435
They've been here since
you walked in.

2580
02:09:28,469 --> 02:09:29,336
Just take a look.

2581
02:09:37,077 --> 02:09:38,245
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

2582
02:09:40,147 --> 02:09:41,982
Yo, kid, when you came in,

2583
02:09:42,016 --> 02:09:43,150
they had to
cut through the suit,

2584
02:09:43,183 --> 02:09:46,086
but when you're ready
to split...

2585
02:09:46,120 --> 02:09:47,522
[SMACKS LIPS] ...I got a plan.

2586
02:10:09,476 --> 02:10:12,379
-MAN: Hey, it's Spider-Man!
-[ALL CHEERING]

2587
02:10:14,081 --> 02:10:15,449
MAN 2: Spider-Man!

2588
02:10:15,482 --> 02:10:17,552
[ALL CHEERING]

2589
02:10:19,253 --> 02:10:20,321
MAN 3: Hey!

2590
02:10:21,922 --> 02:10:22,990
[CHUCKLES]

2591
02:10:23,023 --> 02:10:24,358
MAN 3: Yeah, Spider-Man!

2592
02:10:25,893 --> 02:10:27,494
MAN 4: You're the best,
Spider-Man!

2593
02:10:28,563 --> 02:10:29,997
MAN 5: Spider-Man!

2594
02:10:31,566 --> 02:10:32,900
MAN 2: Over here!

2595
02:10:33,901 --> 02:10:35,102
WOMAN: Thank you!

2596
02:10:35,135 --> 02:10:36,370
MAN 6: Spider-Man!

2597
02:10:49,216 --> 02:10:51,218
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

2598
02:11:01,696 --> 02:11:03,197
[FRANK GRUNTING]

2599
02:11:03,230 --> 02:11:05,299
[ALL CHEERING]

2600
02:11:06,934 --> 02:11:09,169
CROWD: [CHANTING]
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2601
02:11:09,203 --> 02:11:13,307
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!
Spider-Man!

2602
02:11:13,340 --> 02:11:18,412
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2603
02:11:20,447 --> 02:11:21,882
[BLOWS AIR SHARPLY]

2604
02:11:28,523 --> 02:11:32,560
BOY: [CHANTING] Spider-Man!
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2605
02:11:32,594 --> 02:11:36,531
CROWD: [CHANTING] Spider-Man!
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2606
02:11:36,564 --> 02:11:39,099
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2607
02:11:39,133 --> 02:11:41,201
[SERENE MUSIC PLAYING]

2608
02:12:14,536 --> 02:12:16,538
[SERENE MUSIC CONTINUES]

2609
02:12:42,564 --> 02:12:43,565
I've, uh...

2610
02:12:46,568 --> 02:12:48,536
Been thinking a lot
about what you said.

2611
02:12:51,171 --> 02:12:53,741
And you'd be happy to know
that I've decided I'm not...

2612
02:12:55,476 --> 02:12:57,478
I'm not gonna do this
alone anymore.

2613
02:13:03,383 --> 02:13:04,519
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

2614
02:13:07,087 --> 02:13:08,288
I miss you, May.

2615
02:13:16,631 --> 02:13:18,666
PETER: I mean, I've still got
a little pain in my back,

2616
02:13:18,700 --> 02:13:20,602
but I could probably
get back out there

2617
02:13:20,635 --> 02:13:21,736
if you need me for anything.

2618
02:13:21,769 --> 02:13:24,338
DEWOLFF: <i>No. What I need you</i>
<i>to do is rest.</i>

2619
02:13:24,371 --> 02:13:26,440
I know, I know, but come on,
you gotta give me something.

2620
02:13:26,473 --> 02:13:28,442
I mean,
how's the investigation going?

2621
02:13:28,475 --> 02:13:31,445
DEWOLFF: <i>Well,</i>
<i>Metzger's still missing,</i>

2622
02:13:31,478 --> 02:13:34,081
but your friend, Black Widow,

2623
02:13:34,114 --> 02:13:36,651
she's been helping us
dig through all the records

2624
02:13:36,684 --> 02:13:39,353
Damage Control tried to
have scrubbed.

2625
02:13:39,386 --> 02:13:41,756
<i>Had me drop by her office</i>
<i>the other day.</i>

2626
02:13:41,789 --> 02:13:43,357
And how was that?

2627
02:13:43,390 --> 02:13:45,827
Well, uh,
my skin feels amazing.

2628
02:13:45,860 --> 02:13:47,461
[ALARM BEEPS]

2629
02:13:47,494 --> 02:13:48,696
DISPATCHER: [ON PHONE]
<i>Attention, all units.</i>

2630
02:13:48,730 --> 02:13:50,698
<i>We have a confirmed</i>
<i>bank robbery in progress.</i>

2631
02:13:50,732 --> 02:13:51,733
Hey, are you getting this?

2632
02:13:53,467 --> 02:13:54,569
Yeah, I'm on it.

2633
02:13:54,602 --> 02:13:55,670
Hey, it's not that far
from me.

2634
02:13:55,703 --> 02:13:57,104
I could probably
meet you down there.

2635
02:13:57,137 --> 02:14:00,407
No. We can handle a robbery.

2636
02:14:00,440 --> 02:14:03,243
Just try to
take care of yourself.

2637
02:14:04,812 --> 02:14:05,813
Okay.

2638
02:14:07,281 --> 02:14:08,282
You too.

2639
02:14:09,316 --> 02:14:11,385
Say hello
to EJ and Marley for me.

2640
02:14:11,418 --> 02:14:13,387
[CHUCKLES] Okay.

2641
02:14:15,422 --> 02:14:16,758
Spider-Man says hello.

2642
02:14:18,358 --> 02:14:19,527
[DOOR BELL CHIMES]

2643
02:14:27,802 --> 02:14:29,236
[DEVICE CHIMES]

2644
02:14:30,270 --> 02:14:31,706
[CRUNCHING]

2645
02:14:39,814 --> 02:14:42,215
[SERENE MUSIC PLAYING]

2646
02:14:53,160 --> 02:14:54,194
Hi.

2647
02:14:54,227 --> 02:14:55,630
NED: Uh, hey.

2648
02:14:57,599 --> 02:15:00,802
Oh, oh. Uh, flower guy, right,
from... from the party?

2649
02:15:00,835 --> 02:15:01,836
Yeah.

2650
02:15:02,604 --> 02:15:03,705
I'm Peter.

2651
02:15:04,772 --> 02:15:06,273
Okay. Hello.

2652
02:15:09,711 --> 02:15:11,779
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

2653
02:15:24,726 --> 02:15:25,793
Peter.

2654
02:15:31,198 --> 02:15:33,668
[MELLOW,
MID-TEMPO SONG PLAYING]

2655
02:15:49,717 --> 02:15:51,552
[INAUDIBLE CONVERSATION]

2656
02:16:16,476 --> 02:16:18,245
[INAUDIBLE CONVERSATION]

2657
